it toepas."}],"highlights_en":["Practical wisdom for daily choices","Fear of the Lord as foundation","One principle to practice today"],"highlights_af":["Praktiese wysheid vir daaglikse keuses","Vrees vir die Here as fondament","Een beginsel om vandag te oefen"]}],"commentary_en":"Today you read one chapter of Proverbs. Study each section below, then look for one practical principle to live out.\n\nProverbs 11\nHonest scales; pride before destruction; gossip like choice food. Read Proverbs 11 yourself and verify each statement against the verses in your Bible version.\n\nPractical wisdom for daily choices\nThe text of Proverbs 11 records or illustrates: Practical wisdom for daily choices. Re-read those verses and note exactly what Scripture states.\n\nFear of the Lord as foundation\nThe text of Proverbs 11 records or illustrates: Fear of the Lord as foundation. Re-read those verses and note exactly what Scripture states.\n\nOne principle to practice today\nThe text of Proverbs 11 records or illustrates: One principle to practice today. Re-read those verses and note exactly what Scripture states.\n\nWhat God wants us to know:\nGod wants us to know that true wisdom begins with reverence for him and shapes daily choices, speech, and worship.\n\nWhy:\nWisdom passages tie understanding to the fear of the Lord and practical living. Notice commands, prayers, or counsel in this chapter and what attitude toward God they assume.\n\nSimilar elsewhere:\nBook 20 10: Compare with Book 20 10, which immediately precedes this chapter in the same book — notice what events or themes continue or change.\nProverbs 1:7: Wisdom books often repeat the theme that the fear of the Lord is the beginning of wisdom (Proverbs 1:7). Compare how each psalm or proverb applies that foundation differently.","commentary_af":"Vandag lees jy een hoofstuk van Spreuke. Bestudeer elke afdeling hieronder, soek dan een praktiese beginsel om uit te leef.\n\nSpreuke 11\nEerlike weegskaal; hoogmoed voor vernietiging; klets soos lekker kos. Lees Spreuke 11 self en kontroleer elke stelling teen die verse in jou Bybelweergawe.\n\nPraktiese wysheid vir daaglikse keuses\nDie teks van Spreuke 11 noem of illustreer: Praktiese wysheid vir daaglikse keuses. Lees daardie verse weer en skryf presies op wat die Bybel sê — nie wat jy dink nie.\n\nVrees vir die Here as fondament\nDie teks van Spreuke 11 noem of illustreer: Vrees vir die Here as fondament. Lees daardie verse weer en skryf presies op wat die Bybel sê — nie wat jy dink nie.\n\nEen beginsel om vandag te oefen\nDie teks van Spreuke 11 noem of illustreer: Een beginsel om vandag te oefen. Lees daardie verse weer en skryf presies op wat die Bybel sê — nie wat jy dink nie.\n\nWhat God wants us to know:\nGod wil hê ons moet weet dat ware wysheid begin met eerbied vir Hom en daaglikse keuses, spraak en aanbidding vorm.\n\nWhy:\nWysheid verbind insig met die vrees vir die Here. Let op gebooie, gebede of raad in hierdie hoofstuk en watter houding teenoor God dit veronderstel.\n\nSimilar elsewhere:\nBook 20 10: Compare with Book 20 10, wat direct voor hierdie hoofstuk kom — let op wat voortgaan of verander.\nSpreuke 1:7: Wysheidsboeke herhaal dat die vrees vir die Here die begin van wysheid is (Spr 1:7). Vergelyk hoe elke psalm of spreuk dit toepas.","questions_en":["What does this passage reveal about God?","What promise, command, or truth stands out to you?","How can you apply this to your life today?"],"questions_af":["Wat openbaar hierdie gedeelte oor God?","Watter belofte, gebod of waarheid val vir jou op?","Hoe kan jy dit vandag in jou lewe toepas?"]},{"day":12,"title_en":"Proverbs 12","title_af":"Spreuke 12","passages":[{"book_id":20,"chapter":12}],"commentary_intro_en":"Today you read one chapter of Proverbs. Study each section below, then look for one practical principle to live out.","commentary_intro_af":"Vandag lees jy een hoofstuk van Spreuke. Bestudeer elke afdeling hieronder, soek dan een praktiese beginsel om uit te l