 begin van wysheid is (Spr 1:7). Vergelyk hoe elke psalm of spreuk dit toepas.","questions_en":["What does this passage reveal about God?","What promise, command, or truth stands out to you?","How can you apply this to your life today?"],"questions_af":["Wat openbaar hierdie gedeelte oor God?","Watter belofte, gebod of waarheid val vir jou op?","Hoe kan jy dit vandag in jou lewe toepas?"]},{"day":14,"title_en":"Psalms 66–70","title_af":"Psalms 66–70","passages":[{"book_id":19,"chapter":66},{"book_id":19,"chapter":67},{"book_id":19,"chapter":68},{"book_id":19,"chapter":69},{"book_id":19,"chapter":70}],"commentary_intro_en":"These psalms cover a range of human experience before God. Use the chapter summaries as a guide for prayer and reflection.","commentary_intro_af":"Hierdie psalms dek ''n reeks menslike ervaring voor God. Gebruik die hoofstuk-opsommings as gids vir gebed en refleksie.","commentary_sections":[{"book_id":19,"chapter":66,"heading_en":"Psalms 66","heading_af":"Psalms 66","summary_en":"Psalm 66 expresses worship, lament, or wisdom before God. Read it as prayer — many psalms foreshadow Christ and speak to every season of the soul. Read Psalms 66 yourself and verify each statement against the verses in your Bible version.","summary_af":"Psalm 66 druk aanbidding, klagte of wysheid voor God uit. Lees dit as gebed — baie psalms wys na Christus en spreek tot elke seisoen van die siel. Lees Psalms 66 self en kontroleer elke stelling teen die verse in jou Bybelweergawe.","study_points_en":[{"title":"Pray the psalm back to God","verses":"","detail":"The text of Psalms 66 records or illustrates: Pray the psalm back to God. Re-read those verses and note exactly what Scripture states."},{"title":"Notice metaphors for God","verses":"","detail":"The text of Psalms 66 records or illustrates: Notice metaphors for God. Re-read those verses and note exactly what Scripture states."},{"title":"Apply its emotion honestly","verses":"","detail":"The text of Psalms 66 records 