 and John appear in more than one Gospel with matching or overlapping details. Compare the same episode across Gospels to see what each writer records."}],"cross_references_af":[{"ref":"Book 40 8","comparison":"Compare with Book 40 8, wat direct voor hierdie hoofstuk kom — let op wat voortgaan of verander."},{"ref":"Parallelle Evangelies","comparison":"Baie gebeure in Matteus, Markus, Lukas en Johannes verskyn in meer as een Evangelie. Vergelyk dieselfde episode oor Evangelies heen."}],"highlights_en":["Jesus'' identity and authority","Kingdom teaching","Calls to follow"],"highlights_af":["Jesus se identiteit en gesag","Koninkryk-lering","Oproepe om te volg"]}],"commentary_en":"New Testament reading for today. Each section summarizes a chapter so you can follow the flow of the text.\n\nMatthew 7\nMatthew 7. The Gospels reveal Jesus — His teaching, authority, compassion, and mission. Ask: Who is Jesus here, and what is He calling me to believe and do? Read Matthew 7 yourself and verify each statement against the verses in your Bible version.\n\nJesus'' identity and authority\nThe text of Matthew 7 records or illustrates: Jesus'' identity and authority. Re-read those verses and note exactly what Scripture states.\n\nKingdom teaching\nThe text of Matthew 7 records or illustrates: Kingdom teaching. Re-read those verses and note exactly what Scripture states.\n\nCalls to follow\nThe text of Matthew 7 records or illustrates: Calls to follow. Re-read those verses and note exactly what Scripture states.\n\nWhat God wants us to know:\nGod wants us to know who Jesus is and what he calls people to believe and do through his words, actions, and authority.\n\nWhy:\nGospel chapters record what Jesus taught, healed, commanded, or revealed about the kingdom. Focus on what the chapter says Jesus did and said—not later tradition.\n\nSimilar elsewhere:\nBook 40 6: Compare with Book 40 6, which immediately precedes this chapter in the same book — notice what events or themes continue or change.\nParallel Gospels: Many events in Matthew, Mark, Luke, and John appear in more than one Gospel with matching or overlapping details. Compare the same episode across Gospels to see what each writer records.\n\nMatthew 8\nMatthew 8. The Gospels reveal Jesus — His teaching, authority, compassion, and mission. Ask: Who is Jesus here, and what is He calling me to believe and do? Read Matthew 8 yourself and verify each statement against the verses in your Bible version.\n\nJesus'' identity and authority\nThe text of Matthew 8 records or illustrates: Jesus'' identity and authority. Re-read those verses and note exactly what Scripture states.\n\nKingdom teaching\nThe text of Matthew 8 records or illustrates: Kingdom teaching. Re-read those verses and note exactly what Scripture states.\n\nCalls to follow\nThe text of Matthew 8 records or illustrates: Calls to follow. Re-read those verses and note exactly what Scripture states.\n\nWhat God wants us to know:\nGod wants us to know who Jesus is and what he calls people to believe and do through his words, actions, and authority.\n\nWhy:\nGospel chapters record what Jesus taught, healed, commanded, or revealed about the kingdom. Focus on what the chapter says Jesus did and said—not later tradition.\n\nSimilar elsewhere:\nBook 40 7: Compare with Book 40 7, which immediately precedes this chapter in the same book — notice what events or themes continue or change.\nParallel Gospels: Many events in Matthew, Mark, Luke, and John appear in more than one Gospel with matching or overlapping details. Compare the same episode across Gospels to see what each writer records.\n\nMatthew 9\nMatthew 9. The Gospels reveal Jesus — His teaching, authority, compassion, and mission. Ask: Who is Jesus here, and what is He calling me to believe and do? Read Matthew 9 yourself and verify each statement against the verses in your Bible version.\n\nJesus'' identity and authority\nThe text of Matthew 9 records or illustrates: Jesus'' identity and authority. Re-read those verses and note exactly what Scripture states.\n\nKingdom teaching\nThe text of Matthew 9 records or illustrates: Kingdom teaching. Re-read those verses and note exactly what Scripture states.\n\nCalls to follow\nThe text of Matthew 9 records or illustrates: Calls to follow. Re-read those verses and note exactly what Scripture states.\n\nWhat God wants us to know:\nGod wants us to know who Jesus is and what he calls people to believe and do through his words, actions, and authority.\n\nWhy:\nGospel chapters record what Jesus taught, healed, commanded, or revealed about the kingdom. Focus on what the chapter says Jesus did and said—not later tradition.\n\nSimilar elsewhere:\nBook 40 8: Compare with Book 40 8, which immediately precedes this chapter in the same book — notice what events or themes continue or change.\nParallel Gospels: Many events in Matthew, Mark, Luke, and John appear in more than one Gospel with matching or overlapping details. Compare the same episode across Gospels to see what each writer records.","commentary_af":"Nuwe Testament leeswerk vir vandag. Elke afdeling som ''n hoofstuk op sodat jy die vloei van die teks kan volg.\n\nMatteus 7\nMatteus 7. Die Evangelies openbaar Jesus — Sy lering, gesag, barmhartigheid en sending. Vra: Wie is Jesus hier, en wat roep Hy my om te glo en te doen? Lees Matteus 7 self en kontroleer elke stelling teen die verse in jou Bybelweergawe.\n\nJesus se identiteit en gesag\nDie teks van Matteus 7 noem of illustreer: Jesus se identiteit en gesag. Lees daardie verse weer en skryf presies op wat die Bybel sê — nie wat jy dink nie.\n\nKoninkryk-lering\nDie teks van Matteus 7 noem of illustreer: Koninkryk-lering. Lees daardie verse weer en skryf presies op wat die Bybel sê — nie wat jy dink nie.\n\nOproepe om te volg\nDie teks van Matteus 7 noem of illustreer: Oproepe om te volg. Lees daardie verse weer en skryf presies op wat die Bybel sê — nie wat jy dink nie.\n\nWhat God wants us to know:\nGod wil hê ons moet weet wie Jesus is en wat Hy mense roep om te glo en te doen deur sy woorde, dade en gesag.\n\nWhy:\nEvangelie-hoofstukke beskryf wat Jesus geleer, genees, beveel of openbaar het. Fokus op wat die hoofstuk sê Jesus gedoen en gesê het.\n\nSimilar elsewhere:\nBook 40 6: Compare with Book 40 6, wat direct voor hierdie hoofstuk kom — let op wat voortgaan of verander.\nParallelle Evangelies: Baie gebeure in Matteus, Markus, Lukas en Johannes verskyn in meer as een Evangelie. Vergelyk dieselfde episode oor Evangelies heen.\n\nMatteus 8\nMatteus 8. Die Evangelies openbaar Jesus — Sy lering, gesag, barmhartigheid en sending. Vra: Wie is Jesus hier, en wat roep Hy my om te glo en te doen? Lees Matteus 8 self en kontroleer elke stelling teen die verse in jou Bybelweergawe.\n\nJesus se identiteit en gesag\nDie teks van Matteus 8 noem of illustreer: Jesus se identiteit en gesag. Lees daardie verse weer en skryf presies op wat die Bybel sê — nie wat jy dink nie.\n\nKoninkryk-lering\nDie teks van Matteus 8 noem of illustreer: Koninkryk-lering. Lees daardie verse weer en skryf presies op wat die Bybel sê — nie wat jy dink nie.\n\nOproepe om te volg\nDie teks van Matteus 8 noem of illustreer: Oproepe om te volg. Lees daardie verse weer en skryf presies op wat die Bybel sê — nie wat jy dink nie.\n\nWhat God wants us to know:\nGod wil hê ons moet weet wie Jesus is en wat Hy mense roep om te glo en te doen deur sy woorde, dade en gesag.\n\nWhy:\nEvangelie-hoofstukke beskryf wat Jesus geleer, genees, beveel of openbaar het. Fokus op wat die hoofstuk sê Jesus gedoen en gesê het.\n\nSimilar elsewhere:\nBook 40 7: Compare with Book 40 7, wat direct voor hierdie hoofstuk kom — let op wat voortgaan of verander.\nParallelle Evangelies: Baie gebeure in Matteus, Markus, Lukas en Johannes verskyn in meer as een Evangelie. Vergelyk dieselfde episode oor Evangelies heen.\n\nMatteus 9\nMatteus 9. Die Evangelies openbaar Jesus — Sy lering, gesag, barmhartigheid en sending. Vra: Wie is Jesus hier, en wat roep Hy my om te glo en te doen? Lees Matteus 9 self en kontroleer elke stelling teen die verse in jou Bybelweergawe.\n\nJesus se identiteit en gesag\nDie teks van Matteus 9 noem of illustreer: Jesus se identiteit en gesag. Lees daardie verse weer en skryf presies op wat die Bybel sê — nie wat jy dink nie.\n\nKoninkryk-lering\nDie teks van Matteus 9 noem of illustreer: Koninkryk-lering. Lees daardie verse weer en skryf presies op wat die Bybel sê — nie wat jy dink nie.\n\nOproepe om te volg\nDie teks van Matteus 9 noem of illustreer: Oproepe om te volg. Lees daardie verse weer en skryf presies op wat die Bybel sê — nie wat jy dink nie.\n\nWhat God wants us to know:\nGod wil hê ons moet weet wie Jesus is en wat Hy mense roep om te glo en te doen deur sy woorde, dade en gesag.\n\nWhy:\nEvangelie-hoofstukke beskryf wat Jesus geleer, genees, beveel of openbaar het. Fokus op wat die hoofstuk sê Jesus gedoen en gesê het.\n\nSimilar elsewhere:\nBook 40 8: Compare with Book 40 8, wat direct voor hierdie hoofstuk kom — let op wat voortgaan of verander.\nParallelle Evangelies: Baie gebeure in Matteus, Markus, Lukas en Johannes verskyn in meer as een Evangelie. Vergelyk dieselfde episode oor Evangelies heen.","questions_en":["What does this passage reveal about God?","What promise, command, or truth stands out to you?","How can you apply this to your life today?"],"questions_af":["Wat openbaar hierdie gedeelte oor God?","Watter belofte, gebod of waarheid val vir jou op?","Hoe kan jy dit vandag in jou lewe toepas?"]},{"day":4,"title_en":"Matthew 10–12","title_af":"Matteus 10–12","passages":[{"book_id":40,"chapter":10},{"book_id":40,"chapter":11},{"book_id":40,"chapter":12}],"commentary_intro_en":"New Testament reading for today. Each section summarizes a chapter so you can follow the flow of the text.","commentary_intro_af":"Nuwe Testament leeswerk vir vandag. Elke afdeling som ''n hoofstuk op sodat jy die vloei van die teks kan volg.","commentary_section