 oor Evangelies heen."}],"highlights_en":["Jesus'' identity and authority","Kingdom teaching","Calls to follow"],"highlights_af":["Jesus se identiteit en gesag","Koninkryk-lering","Oproepe om te volg"]}],"commentary_en":"New Testament reading for today. Each section summarizes a chapter so you can follow the flow of the text.\n\nMark 15\nMark 15. The Gospels reveal Jesus — His teaching, authority, compassion, and mission. Ask: Who is Jesus here, and what is He calling me to believe and do? Read Mark 15 yourself and verify each statement against the verses in your Bible version.\n\nJesus'' identity and authority\nThe text of Mark 15 records or illustrates: Jesus'' identity and authority. Re-read those verses and note exactly what Scripture states.\n\nKingdom teaching\nThe text of Mark 15 records or illustrates: Kingdom teaching. Re-read those verses and note exactly what Scripture states.\n\nCalls to follow\nThe text of Mark 15 records or illustrates: Calls to follow. Re-read those verses and note exactly what Scripture states.\n\nWhat God wants us to know:\nGod wants us to know who Jesus is and what he calls people to believe and do through his words, actions, and authority.\n\nWhy:\nGospel chapters record what Jesus taught, healed, commanded, or revealed about the kingdom. Focus on what the chapter says Jesus did and said—not later tradition.\n\nSimilar elsewhere:\nBook 41 14: Compare with Book 41 14, which immediately precedes this chapter in the same book — notice what events or themes continue or change.\nParallel Gospels: Many events in Matthew, Mark, Luke, and John appear in more than one Gospel with matching or overlapping details. Compare the same episode across Gospels to see what each writer records.\n\nMark 16\nMark 16. The Gospels reveal Jesus — His teaching, authority, compassion, and mission. Ask: Who is Jesus here, and what is He calling me to believe and do? Read Mark 16 yourself and verify each statement against the verses in your Bible version.\n\nJesus'' identity and authority\nThe text of Mark 16 records or illustrates: Jesus'' identity and authority. Re-read those verses and note exactly what Scripture states.\n\nKingdom teaching\nThe text of Mark 16 records or illustrates: Kingdom teaching. Re-read those verses and note exactly what Scripture states.\n\nCalls to follow\nThe text of Mark 16 records or illustrates: Calls to follow. Re-read those verses and note exactly what Scripture states.\n\nWhat God wants us to know:\nGod wants us to know who Jesus is and what he calls people to believe and do through his words, actions, and authority.\n\nWhy:\nGospel chapters record what Jesus taught, healed, commanded, or revealed about the kingdom. Focus on what the chapter says Jesus did and said—not later tradition.\n\nSimilar elsewhere:\nBook 41 15: Compare with Book 41 15, which immediately precedes this chapter in the same book — notice what events or themes continue or change.\nParallel Gospels: Many events in Matthew, Mark, Luke, and John appear in more than one Gospel with matching or overlapping details. Compare the same episode across Gospels to see what each writer records.\n\nLuke 1\nLuke 1. The Gospels reveal Jesus — His teaching, authority, compassion, and mission. Ask: Who is Jesus here, and what is He calling me to believe and do? Read Luke 1 yourself and verify each statement against the verses in your Bible version.\n\nJesus'' identity and authority\nThe text of Luke 1 records or illustrates: Jesus'' identity and authority. Re-read those verses and note exactly what Scripture states.\n\nKingdom teaching\nThe text of Luke 1 records or illustrates: Kingdom teaching. Re-read those verses and note exactly what Scripture states.\n\nCalls to follow\nThe text of Luke 1 records or illustrates: Calls to follow. Re-read those verses and note exactly what Scripture states.\n\nWhat God wants us to know:\nGod wants us to know who Jesus is and what he calls people to believe and do through his words, actions, and authority.\n\nWhy:\nGospel chapters record what Jesus taught, healed, commanded, or revealed about the kingdom. Focus on what the chapter says Jesus did and said—not later tradition.\n\nSimilar elsewhere:\nParallel Gospels: Many events in Matthew, Mark, Luke, and John appear in more than one Gospel with matching or overlapping details. Compare the same episode across Gospels to see what each writer records.","commentary_af":"Nuwe Testament leeswerk vir vandag. Elke afdeling som ''n hoofstuk op sodat jy die vloei van die teks kan volg.\n\nMarkus 15\nMarkus 15. Die Evangelies openbaar Jesus — Sy lering, gesag, barmhartigheid en sending. Vra: Wie is Jesus hier, en wat roep Hy my om te glo en te doen? Lees Markus 15 self en kontroleer elke stelling teen die verse in jou Bybelweergawe.\n\nJesus se identiteit en gesag\nDie teks van Markus 15 noem of illustreer: Jesus se identiteit en gesag. Lees daardie verse weer en skryf presies op wat die Bybel sê — nie wat jy dink nie.\n\nKoninkryk-lering\nDie teks van Markus 15 noem of illustreer: Koninkryk-lering. Lees daardie verse weer en skryf presies op wat die Bybel sê — nie wat jy dink nie.\n\nOproepe om te volg\nDie teks van Markus 15 noem of illustreer: Oproepe om te volg. Lees daardie verse weer en skryf presies op wat die Bybel sê — nie wat jy dink nie.\n\nWhat God wants us to know:\nGod wil hê ons moet weet wie Jesus is en wat Hy mense roep om te glo en te doen deur sy woorde, dade en gesag.\n\nWhy:\nEvangelie-hoofstukke beskryf wat Jesus geleer, genees, beveel of openbaar het. Fokus op wat die hoofstuk sê Jesus gedoen en gesê het.\n\nSimilar elsewhere:\nBook 41 14: Compare with Book 41 14, wat direct voor hierdie hoofstuk kom — let op wat voortgaan of verander.\nParallelle Evangelies: Baie gebeure in Matteus, Markus, Lukas en Johannes verskyn in meer as een Evangelie. Vergelyk dieselfde episode oor Evangelies heen.\n\nMarkus 16\nMarkus 16. Die Evangelies openbaar Jesus — Sy lering, gesag, barmhartigheid en sending. Vra: Wie is Jesus hier, en wat roep Hy my om te glo en te doen? Lees Markus 16 self en kontroleer elke stelling teen die verse in jou Bybelweergawe.\n\nJesus se identiteit en gesag\nDie teks van Markus 16 noem of illustreer: Jesus se identiteit en gesag. Lees daardie verse weer en skryf presies op wat die Bybel sê — nie wat jy dink nie.\n\nKoninkryk-lering\nDie teks van Markus 16 noem of illustreer: Koninkryk-lering. Lees daardie verse weer en skryf presies op wat die Bybel sê — nie wat jy dink nie.\n\nOproepe om te volg\nDie teks van Markus 16 noem of illustreer: Oproepe om te volg. Lees daardie verse weer en skryf presies op wat die Bybel sê — nie wat jy dink nie.\n\nWhat God wants us to know:\nGod wil hê ons moet weet wie Jesus is en wat Hy mense roep om te glo en te doen deur sy woorde, dade en gesag.\n\nWhy:\nEvangelie-hoofstukke beskryf wat Jesus geleer, genees, beveel of openbaar het. Fokus op wat die hoofstuk sê Jesus gedoen en gesê het.\n\nSimilar elsewhere:\nBook 41 15: Compare with Book 41 15, wat direct voor hierdie hoofstuk kom — let op wat voortgaan of verander.\nParallelle Evangelies: Baie gebeure in Matteus, Markus, Lukas en Johannes verskyn in meer as een Evangelie. Vergelyk dieselfde episode oor Evangelies heen.\n\nLukas 1\nLukas 1. Die Evangelies openbaar Jesus — Sy lering, gesag, barmhartigheid en sending. Vra: Wie is Jesus hier, en wat roep Hy my om te glo en te doen? Lees Lukas 1 self en kontroleer elke stelling teen die verse in jou Bybelweergawe.\n\nJesus se identiteit en gesag\nDie teks van Lukas 1 noem of illustreer: Jesus se identiteit en gesag. Lees daardie verse weer en skryf presies op wat die Bybel sê — nie wat jy dink nie.\n\nKoninkryk-lering\nDie teks van Lukas 1 noem of illustreer: Koninkryk-lering. Lees daardie verse weer en skryf presies op wat die Bybel sê — nie wat jy dink nie.\n\nOproepe om te volg\nDie teks van Lukas 1 noem of illustreer: Oproepe om te volg. Lees daardie verse weer en skryf presies op wat die Bybel sê — nie wat jy dink nie.\n\nWhat God wants us to know:\nGod wil hê ons moet weet wie Jesus is en wat Hy mense roep om te glo en te doen deur sy woorde, dade en gesag.\n\nWhy:\nEvangelie-hoofstukke beskryf wat Jesus geleer, genees, beveel of openbaar het. Fokus op wat die hoofstuk sê Jesus gedoen en gesê het.\n\nSimilar elsewhere:\nParallelle Evangelies: Baie gebeure in Matteus, Markus, Lukas en Johannes verskyn in meer as een Evangelie. Vergelyk dieselfde episode oor Evangelies heen.","questions_en":["What does this passage reveal about God?","What promise, command, or truth stands out to you?","How can you apply this to your life today?"],"questions_af":["Wat openbaar hierdie gedeelte oor God?","Watter belofte, gebod of waarheid val vir jou op?","Hoe kan jy dit vandag in jou lewe toepas?"]},{"day":16,"title_en":"Luke 2–4","title_af":"Lukas 2–4","passages":[{"book_id":42,"chapter":2},{"book_id":42,"chapter":3},{"book_id":42,"chapter":4}],"commentary_intro_en":"New Testament reading for today. Each section summarizes a chapter so you can follow the flow of the text.","commentary_intro_af":"Nuwe Testament leeswerk vir vandag. Elke afdeling som ''n hoofstuk op sodat jy die vloei van die teks kan volg.","commentary_sections":[{"book_id":42,"chapter":2,"heading_en":"Luke 2","heading_af":"Lukas 2","summary_en":"Luke 2. The Gospels reveal Jesus — His teaching, authority, compassion, and mission. Ask: Who is Jesus here, and what is He calling me to believe and do? Read Luke 2 yourself and verify each statement against the verses in your Bible version.","summary_af":"Lukas 2. Die Evangelies openbaar Jesus — Sy lering, gesag, barmhartigheid en sending. Vra: Wie is Jesus hier, en wat roep Hy my om te glo en te doen? Lees Lukas 2 self en kontroleer elke stelling teen die verse in jou Bybelweergawe.","study_points_en":[{"title":"Jesus'' identity and authority","verses":"","detail":"The text of Luke 2 records or illustrates: Jesus'' identity and authority. Re-read those verses and note exactly