ty.","teaching_why_en":"Gospel chapters record what Jesus taught, healed, commanded, or revealed about the kingdom. Focus on what the chapter says Jesus did and said—not later tradition.","teaching_af":"God wil hê ons moet weet wie Jesus is en wat Hy mense roep om te glo en te doen deur sy woorde, dade en gesag.","teaching_why_af":"Evangelie-hoofstukke beskryf wat Jesus geleer, genees, beveel of openbaar het. Fokus op wat die hoofstuk sê Jesus gedoen en gesê het.","cross_references_en":[{"ref":"John 20","comparison":"Compare with John 20, which immediately precedes this chapter in the same book — notice what events or themes continue or change."},{"ref":"Parallel Gospels","comparison":"Many events in Matthew, Mark, Luke, and John appear in more than one Gospel with matching or overlapping details. Compare the same episode across Gospels to see what each writer records."}],"cross_references_af":[{"ref":"Johannes 20","comparison":"Compare with Johannes 20, wat direct voor hierdie hoofstuk kom — let op wat voortgaan of verander."},{"ref":"Parallelle Evangelies","comparison":"Baie gebeure in Matteus, Markus, Lukas en Johannes verskyn in meer as een Evangelie. Vergelyk dieselfde episode oor Evangelies heen."}],"highlights_en":["Jesus'' identity and authority","Kingdom teaching","Calls to follow"],"highlights_af":["Jesus se identiteit en gesag","Koninkryk-lering","Oproepe om te volg"]},{"book_id":44,"chapter":1,"heading_en":"Acts 1","heading_af":"Handeling 1","summary_en":"Acts 1. The Spirit-empowered spread of the Gospel. Notice courage, community life, prayer, and how the church responds to persecution. Read Acts 1 yourself and verify each statement against the verses in your Bible version.","summary_af":"Handeling 1. Die Gees-bemagtigde verspreiding van die Evangelie. Let op moed, gemeenskaplewe, gebed en hoe die kerk op vervolging reageer. Lees Handeling 1 self en kontroleer elke stelling teen die verse in jou Bybelweergawe.","study_points_en":[{"title":"Holy Spirit''s power","verses":"","detail":"The text of Acts 1 records or illustrates: Holy Spirit''s power. Re-read those verses and note exactly what Scripture states."},{"title":"Bold witness","verses":"","detail":"The text of Acts 1 records or illustrates: Bold witness. Re-read those verses and note exactly what Scripture states."},{"title":"Growing community","verses":"","detail":"The text of Acts 1 records or illustrates: Growing community. Re-read those verses and note exactly what Scripture states."}],"study_points_af":[{"title":"Heilige Gees se krag","verses":"","detail":"Die teks van Handeling 1 noem of illustreer: Heilige Gees se krag. Lees daardie verse weer en skryf presies op wat die Bybel sê — nie wat jy dink nie."},{"title":"Dapper getuienis","verses":"","detail":"Die teks van Handeling 1 noem of illustreer: Dapper getuienis. Lees daardie verse weer en skryf presies op wat die Bybel sê — nie wat jy dink nie."},{"title":"Groeiende gemeenskap","verses":"","detail":"Die teks van Handeling 1 noem of illustreer: Groeiende gemeenskap. Lees daardie verse weer en skryf presies op wat die Bybel sê — nie wat jy dink nie."}],"teaching_en":"God wants us to know that the risen Christ continues his work through the Spirit, the apostles, and the growing church.","teaching_why_en":"Acts records preaching, conversions, miracles, and persecution. Notice how the Spirit empowers witness and how the church responds in this chapter.","teaching_af":"God wil hê ons moet weet dat die opgestane Christus voortwerk deur die Gees, die apostels en die groeiende kerk.","teaching_why_af":"Handeling beskryf preek, bekering, wonderwerke en vervolging. Let hoe die Gees getuienis bemagtig en hoe die kerk reageer.","cross_references_en":[],"cross_references_af":[],"highlights_en":["Holy Spirit''s power","Bold witness","Growing community"],"highlights_af":["Heilige Gees se krag","Dapper getuienis","Groeiende gemeenskap"]}],"commentary_en":"New Testament reading for today. Each section summarizes a chapter so you can follow the flow of the text.\n\nJohn 20\nJohn 20. The Gospels reveal Jesus — His teaching, authority, compassion, and mission. Ask: Who is Jesus here, and what is He calling me to believe and do? Read John 20 yourself and verify each statement against the verses in your Bible version.\n\nJesus'' identity and authority\nThe text of John 20 records or illustrates: Jesus'' identity and authority. Re-read those verses and note exactly what Scripture states.\n\nKingdom teaching\nThe text of John 20 records or illustrates: Kingdom teaching. Re-read those verses and note exactly what Scripture states.\n\nCalls to follow\nThe text of John 20 records or illustrates: Calls to follow. Re-read those verses and note exactly what Scripture states.\n\nWhat God wants us to know:\nGod wants us to know who Jesus is and what he calls people to believe and do through his words, actions, and authority.\n\nWhy:\nGospel chapters record what Jesus taught, healed, commanded, or revealed about the kingdom. Focus on what the chapter says Jesus did and said—not later tradition.\n\nSimilar elsewhere:\nJohn 19: Compare with John 19, which immediately precedes this chapter in the same book — notice what events or themes continue or change.\nParallel Gospels: Many events in Matthew, Mark, Luke, and John appear in more than one Gospel with matching or overlapping details. Compare the same episode across Gospels to see what each writer records.\n\nJohn 21\nJohn 21. The Gospels reveal Jesus — His teaching, authority, compassion, and mission. Ask: Who is Jesus here, and what is He calling me to believe and do? Read John 21 yourself and verify each statement against the verses in your Bible version.\n\nJesus'' identity and authority\nThe text of John 21 records or illustrates: Jesus'' identity and authority. Re-read those verses and note exactly what Scripture states.\n\nKingdom teaching\nThe text of John 21 records or illustrates: Kingdom teaching. Re-read those verses and note exactly what Scripture states.\n\nCalls to follow\nThe text of John 21 records or illustrates: Calls to follow. Re-read those verses and note exactly what Scripture states.\n\nWhat God wants us to know:\nGod wants us to know who Jesus is and what he calls people to believe and do through his words, actions, and authority.\n\nWhy:\nGospel chapters record what Jesus taught, healed, commanded, or revealed about the kingdom. Focus on what the chapter says Jesus did and said—not later tradition.\n\nSimilar elsewhere:\nJohn 20: Compare with John 20, which immediately precedes this chapter in the same book — notice what events or themes continue or change.\nParallel Gospels: Many events in Matthew, Mark, Luke, and John appear in more than one Gospel with matching or overlapping details. Compare the same episode across Gospels to see what each writer records.\n\nActs 1\nActs 1. The Spirit-empowered spread of the Gospel. Notice courage, community life, prayer, and how the church responds to persecution. Read Acts 1 yourself and verify each statement against the verses in your Bible version.\n\nHoly Spirit''s power\nThe text of Acts 1 records or illustrates: Holy Spirit''s power. Re-read those verses and note exactly what Scripture states.\n\nBold witness\nThe text of Acts 1 records or illustrates: Bold witness. Re-read those verses and note exactly what Scripture states.\n\nGrowing community\nThe text of Acts 1 records or illustrates: Growing community. Re-read those verses and note exactly what Scripture states.\n\nWhat God wants us to know:\nGod wants us to know that the risen Christ continues his work through the Spirit, the apostles, and the growing church.\n\nWhy:\nActs records preaching, conversions, miracles, and persecution. Notice how the Spirit empowers witness and how the church responds in this chapter.","commentary_af":"Nuwe Testament leeswerk vir vandag. Elke afdeling som ''n hoofstuk op sodat jy die vloei van die teks kan volg.\n\nJohannes 20\nJohannes 20. Die Evangelies openbaar Jesus — Sy lering, gesag, barmhartigheid en sending. Vra: Wie is Jesus hier, en wat roep Hy my om te glo en te doen? Lees Johannes 20 self en kontroleer elke stelling teen die verse in jou Bybelweergawe.\n\nJesus se identiteit en gesag\nDie teks van Johannes 20 noem of illustreer: Jesus se identiteit en gesag. Lees daardie verse weer en skryf presies op wat die Bybel sê — nie wat jy dink nie.\n\nKoninkryk-lering\nDie teks van Johannes 20 noem of illustreer: Koninkryk-lering. Lees daardie verse weer en skryf presies op wat die Bybel sê — nie wat jy dink nie.\n\nOproepe om te volg\nDie teks van Johannes 20 noem of illustreer: Oproepe om te volg. Lees daardie verse weer en skryf presies op wat die Bybel sê — nie wat jy dink nie.\n\nWhat God wants us to know:\nGod wil hê ons moet weet wie Jesus is en wat Hy mense roep om te glo en te doen deur sy woorde, dade en gesag.\n\nWhy:\nEvangelie-hoofstukke beskryf wat Jesus geleer, genees, beveel of openbaar het. Fokus op wat die hoofstuk sê Jesus gedoen en gesê het.\n\nSimilar elsewhere:\nJohannes 19: Compare with Johannes 19, wat direct voor hierdie hoofstuk kom — let op wat voortgaan of verander.\nParallelle Evangelies: Baie gebeure in Matteus, Markus, Lukas en Johannes verskyn in meer as een Evangelie. Vergelyk dieselfde episode oor Evangelies heen.\n\nJohannes 21\nJohannes 21. Die Evangelies openbaar Jesus — Sy lering, gesag, barmhartigheid en sending. Vra: Wie is Jesus hier, en wat roep Hy my om te glo en te doen? Lees Johannes 21 self en kontroleer elke stelling teen die verse in jou Bybelweergawe.\n\nJesus se identiteit en gesag\nDie teks van Johannes 21 noem of illustreer: Jesus se identiteit en gesag. Lees daardie verse weer en skryf presies op wat die Bybel sê — nie wat jy dink nie.\n\nKoninkryk-lering\nDie teks van Johannes 21 noem of illustreer: Koninkryk-lering. Lees daardie verse weer en skryf presies op wat die Bybel sê — nie wat jy dink nie.\n\nOproepe om te volg\nDie teks van Johannes 21 noem of illustreer: Oproepe om te volg. Lees daardie verse weer en skryf presies op wat die Bybel sê — nie wat jy dink nie.\n\nWhat God wants us to know:\nGod wil hê ons moet weet wie Jesus is en wat Hy mense roep om te glo en te doen deur sy woorde, dade en gesag.\n\nWhy:\nEvangelie-hoofstukke beskryf wat Jesus geleer, genees, beveel of openbaar het. Fokus op wat die hoofstuk sê Jesus gedoen en gesê het.\n\nSimilar elsewhere:\nJohannes 20: Compare with Johannes 20, wat direct voor hierdie hoofstuk kom — let op wat voortgaan of verander.\nParallelle Evangelies: Baie gebeure in Matteus, Markus, Lukas en Johannes verskyn in meer as een Evangelie. Vergelyk dieselfde episode oor Evangelies heen.\n\nHandeling 1\nHandeling 1. Die Gees-bemagtigde verspreiding van die Evangelie. Let op moed, gemeenskaplewe, gebed en hoe die kerk op vervolging reageer. Lees Handeling 1 self en kontroleer elke stelling teen die verse in jou Bybelweergawe.\n\nHeilige Gees se krag\nDie teks van Handeling 1 noem of illustreer: Heilige Gees se krag. Lees daardie verse weer en skryf presies op wat die Bybel sê — nie wat jy dink nie.\n\nDapper getuienis\nDie teks van Handeling 1 noem of illustreer: Dapper getuienis. Lees daardie verse weer en skryf presies op wat die Bybel sê — nie wat jy dink nie.\n\nGroeiende gemeenskap\nDie teks van Handeling 1 noem of illustreer: Groeiende gemeenskap. Lees daardie verse weer en skryf presies op wat die Bybel sê — nie wat jy dink nie.\n\nWhat God wants us to know:\nGod wil hê ons moet weet dat die opgestane Christus voortwerk deur die Gees, die apostels en die groeiende kerk.\n\nWhy:\nHandeling beskryf preek, bekering, wonderwerke en vervolging. Let hoe die Gees getuienis bemagtig en hoe die kerk reageer.","questions_en":["What does this passage reveal about God?","What promise, command, or truth stands out to you?","How can you apply this to your life today?"],"questions_af":["Wat openbaar hierdie gedeelte oor God?","Watter belofte, gebod of waarheid val vir jou op?",