e growing church.\n\nWhy:\nActs records preaching, conversions, miracles, and persecution. Notice how the Spirit empowers witness and how the church responds in this chapter.\n\nSimilar elsewhere:\nBook 44 1: Compare with Book 44 1, which immediately precedes this chapter in the same book — notice what events or themes continue or change.\n\nActs 3\nActs 3. The Spirit-empowered spread of the Gospel. Notice courage, community life, prayer, and how the church responds to persecution. Read Acts 3 yourself and verify each statement against the verses in your Bible version.\n\nHoly Spirit''s power\nThe text of Acts 3 records or illustrates: Holy Spirit''s power. Re-read those verses and note exactly what Scripture states.\n\nBold witness\nThe text of Acts 3 records or illustrates: Bold witness. Re-read those verses and note exactly what Scripture states.\n\nGrowing community\nThe text of Acts 3 records or illustrates: Growing community. Re-read those verses and note exactly what Scripture states.\n\nWhat God wants us to know:\nGod wants us to know that the risen Christ continues his work through the Spirit, the apostles, and the growing church.\n\nWhy:\nActs records preaching, conversions, miracles, and persecution. Notice how the Spirit empowers witness and how the church responds in this chapter.\n\nSimilar elsewhere:\nBook 44 2: Compare with Book 44 2, which immediately precedes this chapter in the same book — notice what events or themes continue or change.\n\nActs 4\nActs 4. The Spirit-empowered spread of the Gospel. Notice courage, community life, prayer, and how the church responds to persecution. Read Acts 4 yourself and verify each statement against the verses in your Bible version.\n\nHoly Spirit''s power\nThe text of Acts 4 records or illustrates: Holy Spirit''s power. Re-read those verses and note exactly what Scripture states.\n\nBold witness\nThe text of Acts 4 records or illustrates: Bold witness. Re-read those verses and note exactly what Scripture states.\n\nGrowing community\nThe text of Acts 4 records or illustrates: Growing community. Re-read those verses and note exactly what Scripture states.\n\nWhat God wants us to know:\nGod wants us to know that the risen Christ continues his work through the Spirit, the apostles, and the growing church.\n\nWhy:\nActs records preaching, conversions, miracles, and persecution. Notice how the Spirit empowers witness and how the church responds in this chapter.\n\nSimilar elsewhere:\nBook 44 3: Compare with Book 44 3, which immediately precedes this chapter in the same book — notice what events or themes continue or change.","commentary_af":"Nuwe Testament leeswerk vir vandag. Elke afdeling som ''n hoofstuk op sodat jy die vloei van die teks kan volg.\n\nHandeling 2\nPinkster — Heilige Gees vul gelowiges; Petrus preek; drieduisend gered. Die kerk word in krag gebore. Lees Handeling 2 self en kontroleer elke stelling teen die verse in jou Bybelweergawe.\n\nGees soos vuurtong\nDie teks van Handeling 2 noem of illustreer: Gees soos vuurtong. Lees daardie verse weer en skryf presies op wat die Bybel sê — nie wat jy dink nie.\n\nPetrus se preek — gekruisig en opgestaan\nDie teks van Handeling 2 noem of illustreer: Petrus se preek — gekruisig en opgestaan. Lees daardie verse weer en skryf presies op wat die Bybel sê — nie wat jy dink nie.\n\nBekeer en doop\nDie teks van Handeling 2 noem of illustreer: Bekeer en doop. Lees daardie verse weer en skryf presies op wat die Bybel sê — nie wat jy dink nie.\n\nWhat God wants us to know:\nGod wil hê ons moet weet dat die opgestane Christus voortwerk deur die Gees, die apostels en die groeiende kerk.\n\nWhy:\nHandeling beskryf preek, bekering, wonderwerke en vervolging. Let hoe die Gees getuienis bemagtig en hoe die kerk reageer.\n\nSimilar elsewhere:\nBook 44 1: Compare with Book 44 1, wat direct voor hierdie hoofstuk kom — let op wat voortgaan of verander.\n\nHandeling 3\nHandeling 3. Die Gees-bemagtigde verspreiding van die Evangelie. Let 