prayer, and how the church responds to persecution. Read Acts 20 yourself and verify each statement against the verses in your Bible version.\n\nHoly Spirit''s power\nThe text of Acts 20 records or illustrates: Holy Spirit''s power. Re-read those verses and note exactly what Scripture states.\n\nBold witness\nThe text of Acts 20 records or illustrates: Bold witness. Re-read those verses and note exactly what Scripture states.\n\nGrowing community\nThe text of Acts 20 records or illustrates: Growing community. Re-read those verses and note exactly what Scripture states.\n\nWhat God wants us to know:\nGod wants us to know that the risen Christ continues his work through the Spirit, the apostles, and the growing church.\n\nWhy:\nActs records preaching, conversions, miracles, and persecution. Notice how the Spirit empowers witness and how the church responds in this chapter.\n\nSimilar elsewhere:\nBook 44 19: Compare with Book 44 19, which immediately precedes this chapter in the same book — notice what events or themes continue or change.\n\nActs 21\nActs 21. The Spirit-empowered spread of the Gospel. Notice courage, community life, prayer, and how the church responds to persecution. Read Acts 21 yourself and verify each statement against the verses in your Bible version.\n\nHoly Spirit''s power\nThe text of Acts 21 records or illustrates: Holy Spirit''s power. Re-read those verses and note exactly what Scripture states.\n\nBold witness\nThe text of Acts 21 records or illustrates: Bold witness. Re-read those verses and note exactly what Scripture states.\n\nGrowing community\nThe text of Acts 21 records or illustrates: Growing community. Re-read those verses and note exactly what Scripture states.\n\nWhat God wants us to know:\nGod wants us to know that the risen Christ continues his work through the Spirit, the apostles, and the growing church.\n\nWhy:\nActs records preaching, conversions, miracles, and persecution. Notice how the Spirit empowers witness and how the church responds in this chapter.\n\nSimilar elsewhere:\nBook 44 20: Compare with Book 44 20, which immediately precedes this chapter in the same book — notice what events or themes continue or change.\n\nActs 22\nActs 22. The Spirit-empowered spread of the Gospel. Notice courage, community life, prayer, and how the church responds to persecution. Read Acts 22 yourself and verify each statement against the verses in your Bible version.\n\nHoly Spirit''s power\nThe text of Acts 22 records or illustrates: Holy Spirit''s power. Re-read those verses and note exactly what Scripture states.\n\nBold witness\nThe text of Acts 22 records or illustrates: Bold witness. Re-read those verses and note exactly what Scripture states.\n\nGrowing community\nThe text of Acts 22 records or illustrates: Growing community. Re-read those verses and note exactly what Scripture states.\n\nWhat God wants us to know:\nGod wants us to know that the risen Christ continues his work through the Spirit, the apostles, and the growing church.\n\nWhy:\nActs records preaching, conversions, miracles, and persecution. Notice how the Spirit empowers witness and how the church responds in this chapter.\n\nSimilar elsewhere:\nBook 44 21: Compare with Book 44 21, which immediately precedes this chapter in the same book — notice what events or themes continue or change.","commentary_af":"Nuwe Testament leeswerk vir vandag. Elke afdeling som ''n hoofstuk op sodat jy die vloei van die teks kan volg.\n\nHandeling 20\nHandeling 20. Die Gees-bemagtigde verspreiding van die Evangelie. Let op moed, gemeenskaplewe, gebed en hoe die kerk op vervolging reageer. Lees Handeling 20 self en kontroleer elke stelling teen die verse in jou Bybelweergawe.\n\nHeilige Gees se krag\nDie teks van Handeling 20 noem of illustreer: Heilige Gees se krag. Lees daardie verse weer en skryf presies op wat die Bybel sê — nie wat jy dink nie.\n\nDapper getuienis\nDie teks van Handeling 20 noem of illustreer: Dapper getuienis. Lees daardie ve