mans 13\nRomans 13. Paul teaches doctrine and Christian living. Connect theological truth to practical obedience in church, family, and daily relationships. Read Romans 13 yourself and verify each statement against the verses in your Bible version.\n\nGospel truth\nThe text of Romans 13 records or illustrates: Gospel truth. Re-read those verses and note exactly what Scripture states.\n\nLife in the Spirit\nThe text of Romans 13 records or illustrates: Life in the Spirit. Re-read those verses and note exactly what Scripture states.\n\nPractical ethics\nThe text of Romans 13 records or illustrates: Practical ethics. Re-read those verses and note exactly what Scripture states.\n\nWhat God wants us to know:\nGod wants believers to know gospel truth and how it should shape church life, holiness, and love for others.\n\nWhy:\nPaul''s letters argue from what Christ has done to how Christians should live. Find the doctrinal statement in this chapter and the conduct it connects to.\n\nSimilar elsewhere:\nRomans 12: Compare with Romans 12, which immediately precedes this chapter in the same book — notice what events or themes continue or change.\n\nRomans 14\nRomans 14. Paul teaches doctrine and Christian living. Connect theological truth to practical obedience in church, family, and daily relationships. Read Romans 14 yourself and verify each statement against the verses in your Bible version.\n\nGospel truth\nThe text of Romans 14 records or illustrates: Gospel truth. Re-read those verses and note exactly what Scripture states.\n\nLife in the Spirit\nThe text of Romans 14 records or illustrates: Life in the Spirit. Re-read those verses and note exactly what Scripture states.\n\nPractical ethics\nThe text of Romans 14 records or illustrates: Practical ethics. Re-read those verses and note exactly what Scripture states.\n\nWhat God wants us to know:\nGod wants believers to know gospel truth and how it should shape church life, holiness, and love for others.\n\nWhy:\nPaul''s letters argue from what Christ has done to how Christians should live. Find the doctrinal statement in this chapter and the conduct it connects to.\n\nSimilar elsewhere:\nRomans 13: Compare with Romans 13, which immediately precedes this chapter in the same book — notice what events or themes continue or change.\n\nRomans 15\nRomans 15. Paul teaches doctrine and Christian living. Connect theological truth to practical obedience in church, family, and daily relationships. Read Romans 15 yourself and verify each statement against the verses in your Bible version.\n\nGospel truth\nThe text of Romans 15 records or illustrates: Gospel truth. Re-read those verses and note exactly what Scripture states.\n\nLife in the Spirit\nThe text of Romans 15 records or illustrates: Life in the Spirit. Re-read those verses and note exactly what Scripture states.\n\nPractical ethics\nThe text of Romans 15 records or illustrates: Practical ethics. Re-read those verses and note exactly what Scripture states.\n\nWhat God wants us to know:\nGod wants believers to know gospel truth and how it should shape church life, holiness, and love for others.\n\nWhy:\nPaul''s letters argue from what Christ has done to how Christians should live. Find the doctrinal statement in this chapter and the conduct it connects to.\n\nSimilar elsewhere:\nRomans 14: Compare with Romans 14, which immediately precedes this chapter in the same book — notice what events or themes continue or change.","commentary_af":"Nuwe Testament leeswerk vir vandag. Elke afdeling som ''n hoofstuk op sodat jy die vloei van die teks kan volg.\n\nRomeine 13\nRomeine 13. Paulus leer leerstelling en Christelike lewe. Verbind teologiese waarheid met praktiese gehoorsaamheid in kerk, gesin en daaglikse verhoudings. Lees Romeine 13 self en kontroleer elke stelling teen die verse in jou Bybelweergawe.\n\nEvangelie-waarheid\nDie teks van Romeine 13 noem of illustreer: Evangelie-waarheid. Lees daardie verse weer en skryf presies op wat die Bybel sê — nie wat jy dink nie.\n\nLewe in die Gees\nDie teks van Romeine 13 noem of illustreer: Lewe in die Gees. Lees daardie verse weer en skryf presies op wat die Bybel sê — nie wat jy dink nie.\n\nPraktiese etiek\nDie teks van Romeine 13 noem of illustreer: Praktiese etiek. Lees daardie verse weer en skryf presies op wat die Bybel sê — nie wat jy dink nie.\n\nWhat God wants us to know:\nGod wil gelowiges laat weet evangelie-waarheid en hoe dit kerklewe, heiligheid en liefde moet vorm.\n\nWhy:\nPaulus redeneer van wat Christus gedoen het na hoe Christene moet leef. Soek die leerstelling in hierdie hoofstuk en die lewe wat dit verbind.\n\nSimilar elsewhere:\nRomeine 12: Compare with Romeine 12, wat direct voor hierdie hoofstuk kom — let op wat voortgaan of verander.\n\nRomeine 14\nRomeine 14. Paulus leer leerstelling en Christelike lewe. Verbind teologiese waarheid met praktiese gehoorsaamheid in kerk, gesin en daaglikse verhoudings. Lees Romeine 14 self en kontroleer elke stelling teen die verse in jou Bybelweergawe.\n\nEvangelie-waarheid\nDie teks van Romeine 14 noem of illustreer: Evangelie-waarheid. Lees daardie verse weer en skryf presies op wat die Bybel sê — nie wat jy dink nie.\n\nLewe in die Gees\nDie teks van Romeine 14 noem of illustreer: Lewe in die Gees. Lees daardie verse weer en skryf presies op wat die Bybel sê — nie wat jy dink nie.\n\nPraktiese etiek\nDie teks van Romeine 14 noem of illustreer: Praktiese etiek. Lees daardie verse weer en skryf presies op wat die Bybel sê — nie wat jy dink nie.\n\nWhat God wants us to know:\nGod wil gelowiges laat weet evangelie-waarheid en hoe dit kerklewe, heiligheid en liefde moet vorm.\n\nWhy:\nPaulus redeneer van wat Christus gedoen het na hoe Christene moet leef. Soek die leerstelling in hierdie hoofstuk en die lewe wat dit verbind.\n\nSimilar elsewhere:\nRomeine 13: Compare with Romeine 13, wat direct voor hierdie hoofstuk kom — let op wat voortgaan of verander.\n\nRomeine 15\nRomeine 15. Paulus leer leerstelling en Christelike lewe. Verbind teologiese waarheid met praktiese gehoorsaamheid in kerk, gesin en daaglikse verhoudings. Lees Romeine 15 self en kontroleer elke stelling teen die verse in jou Bybelweergawe.\n\nEvangelie-waarheid\nDie teks van Romeine 15 noem of illustreer: Evangelie-waarheid. Lees daardie verse weer en skryf presies op wat die Bybel sê — nie wat jy dink nie.\n\nLewe in die Gees\nDie teks van Romeine 15 noem of illustreer: Lewe in die Gees. Lees daardie verse weer en skryf presies op wat die Bybel sê — nie wat jy dink nie.\n\nPraktiese etiek\nDie teks van Romeine 15 noem of illustreer: Praktiese etiek. Lees daardie verse weer en skryf presies op wat die Bybel sê — nie wat jy dink nie.\n\nWhat God wants us to know:\nGod wil gelowiges laat weet evangelie-waarheid en hoe dit kerklewe, heiligheid en liefde moet vorm.\n\nWhy:\nPaulus redeneer van wat Christus gedoen het na hoe Christene moet leef. Soek die leerstelling in hierdie hoofstuk en die lewe wat dit verbind.\n\nSimilar elsewhere:\nRomeine 14: Compare with Romeine 14, wat direct voor hierdie hoofstuk kom — let op wat voortgaan of verander.","questions_en":["What does this passage reveal about God?","What promise, command, or truth stands out to you?","How can you apply this to your life today?"],"questions_af":["Wat openbaar hierdie gedeelte oor God?","Watter belofte, gebod of waarheid val vir jou op?","Hoe kan jy dit vandag in jou lewe toepas?"]},{"day":45,"title_en":"Romans 16 – 1 Corinthians 2","title_af":"Romeine 16 – 1 Korintiërs 2","passages":[{"book_id":45,"chapter":16},{"book_id":46,"chapter":1},{"book_id":46,"chapter":2}],"commentary_intro_en":"New Testament reading for today. Each section summarizes a chapter so you can follow the flow of the text.","commentary_intro_af":"Nuwe Testament leeswerk vir vandag. Elke afdeling som ''n hoofstuk op sodat jy die vloei van die teks kan volg.","commentary_sections":[{"book_id":45,"chapter":16,"heading_en":"Romans 16","heading_af":"Romeine 16","