Paulus redeneer van wat Christus gedoen het na hoe Christene moet leef. Soek die leerstelling in hierdie hoofstuk en die lewe wat dit verbind.","cross_references_en":[{"ref":"Book 51 1","comparison":"Compare with Book 51 1, which immediately precedes this chapter in the same book — notice what events or themes continue or change."}],"cross_references_af":[{"ref":"Book 51 1","comparison":"Compare with Book 51 1, wat direct voor hierdie hoofstuk kom — let op wat voortgaan of verander."}],"highlights_en":["Gospel truth","Life in the Spirit","Practical ethics"],"highlights_af":["Evangelie-waarheid","Lewe in die Gees","Praktiese etiek"]}],"commentary_en":"New Testament reading for today. Each section summarizes a chapter so you can follow the flow of the text.\n\nBook 50 4\nBook 50 4. Paul teaches doctrine and Christian living. Connect theological truth to practical obedience in church, family, and daily relationships. Read Book 50 4 yourself and verify each statement against the verses in your Bible version.\n\nGospel truth\nThe text of Book 50 4 records or illustrates: Gospel truth. Re-read those verses and note exactly what Scripture states.\n\nLife in the Spirit\nThe text of Book 50 4 records or illustrates: Life in the Spirit. Re-read those verses and note exactly what Scripture states.\n\nPractical ethics\nThe text of Book 50 4 records or illustrates: Practical ethics. Re-read those verses and note exactly what Scripture states.\n\nWhat God wants us to know:\nGod wants believers to know gospel truth and how it should shape church life, holiness, and love for others.\n\nWhy:\nPaul''s letters argue from what Christ has done to how Christians should live. Find the doctrinal statement in this chapter and the conduct it connects to.\n\nSimilar elsewhere:\nBook 50 3: Compare with Book 50 3, which immediately precedes this chapter in the same book — notice what events or themes continue or change.\n\nBook 51 1\nBook 51 1. Paul teaches doctrine and Christian living. Connect theological truth to practical obedience in church, family, and daily relationships. Read Book 51 1 yourself and verify each statement against the verses in your Bible version.\n\nGospel truth\nThe text of Book 51 1 records or illustrates: Gospel truth. Re-read those verses and note exactly what Scripture states.\n\nLife in the Spirit\nThe text of Book 51 1 records or illustrates: Life in the Spirit. Re-read those verses and note exactly what Scripture states.\n\nPractical ethics\nThe text of Book 51 1 records or illustrates: Practical ethics. Re-read those verses and note exactly what Scripture states.\n\nWhat God wants us to know:\nGod wants believers to know gospel truth and how it should shape church life, holiness, and love for others.\n\nWhy:\nPaul''s letters argue from what Christ has done to how Christians should live. Find the doctrinal statement in this chapter and the conduct it connects to.\n\nBook 51 2\nBook 51 2. Paul teaches doctrine and Christian living. Connect theological truth to practical obedience in church, family, and daily relationships. Read Book 51 2 yourself and verify each statement against the verses in your Bible version.\n\nGospel truth\nThe text of Book 51 2 records or illustrates: Gospel truth. Re-read those verses and note exactly what Scripture states.\n\nLife in the Spirit\nThe text of Book 51 2 records or illustrates: Life in the Spirit. Re-read those verses and note exactly what Scripture states.\n\nPractical ethics\nThe text of Book 51 2 records or illustrates: Practical ethics. Re-read those verses and note exactly what Scripture states.\n\nWhat God wants us to know:\nGod wants believers to know gospel truth and how it should shape church life, holiness, and love for others.\n\nWhy:\nPaul''s letters argue from what Christ has done to how Christians should live. Find the doctrinal statement in this chapter and the conduct it connects to.\n\nSimilar elsewhere:\nBook 51 1: Compare with Book 51 1, which immediately precedes this chapter in the same book — notice what events or themes continue or change.","commentary_af":"Nuwe Testament leeswerk vir vandag. Elke afdeling som ''n hoofstuk op sodat jy die vloei van die teks kan volg.\n\nBoek 50 4\nBoek 50 4. Paulus leer leerstelling en Christelike lewe. Verbind teologiese waarheid met praktiese gehoorsaamheid in kerk, gesin en daaglikse verhoudings. Lees Boek 50 4 self en kontroleer elke stelling teen die verse in jou Bybelweergawe.\n\nEvangelie-waarheid\nDie teks van Boek 50 4 noem of illustreer: Evangelie-waarheid. Lees daardie verse weer en skryf presies op wat die Bybel sê — nie wat jy dink nie.\n\nLewe in die Gees\nDie teks van Boek 50 4 noem of illustreer: Lewe in die Gees. Lees daardie verse weer en skryf presies op wat die Bybel sê — nie wat jy dink nie.\n\nPraktiese etiek\nDie teks van Boek 50 4 noem of illustreer: Praktiese etiek. Lees daardie verse weer en skryf presies op wat die Bybel sê — nie wat jy dink nie.\n\nWhat God wants us to know:\nGod wil gelowiges laat weet evangelie-waarheid en hoe dit kerklewe, heiligheid en liefde moet vorm.\n\nWhy:\nPaulus redeneer van wat Christus gedoen het na hoe Christene moet leef. Soek die leerstelling in hierdie hoofstuk en die lewe wat dit verbind.\n\nSimilar elsewhere:\nBook 50 3: Compare with Book 50 3, wat direct voor hierdie hoofstuk kom — let op wat voortgaan of verander.\n\nBoek 51 1\nBoek 51 1. Paulus leer leerstelling en Christelike lewe. Verbind teologiese waarheid met praktiese gehoorsaamheid in kerk, gesin en daaglikse verhoudings. Lees Boek 51 1 self en kontroleer elke stelling teen die verse in jou Bybelweergawe.\n\nEvangelie-waarheid\nDie teks van Boek 51 1 noem of illustreer: Evangelie-waarheid. Lees daardie verse weer en skryf presies op wat die Bybel sê — nie wat jy dink nie.\n\nLewe in die Gees\nDie teks van Boek 51 1 noem of illustreer: Lewe in die Gees. Lees daardie verse weer en skryf presies op wat die Bybel sê — nie wat jy dink nie.\n\nPraktiese etiek\nDie teks van Boek 51 1 noem of illustreer: Praktiese etiek. Lees daardie verse weer en skryf presies op wat die Bybel sê — nie wat jy dink nie.\n\nWhat God wants us to know:\nGod wil gelowiges laat weet evangelie-waarheid en hoe dit kerklewe, heiligheid en liefde moet vorm.\n\nWhy:\nPaulus redeneer van wat Christus gedoen het na hoe Christene moet leef. Soek die leerstelling in hierdie hoofstuk en die lewe wat dit verbind.\n\nBoek 51 2\nBoek 51 2. Paulus leer leerstelling en Christelike lewe. Verbind teologiese waarheid met praktiese gehoorsaamheid in kerk, gesin en daaglikse verhoudings. Lees Boek 51 2 self en kontroleer elke stelling teen die verse in jou Bybelweergawe.\n\nEvangelie-waarheid\nDie teks van Boek 51 2 noem of illustreer: Evangelie-waarheid. Lees daardie verse weer en skryf presies op wat die Bybel sê — nie wat jy dink nie.\n\nLewe in die Gees\nDie teks van Boek 51 2 noem of illustreer: Lewe in die Gees. Lees daardie verse weer en skryf presies op wat die Bybel sê — nie wat jy dink nie.\n\nPraktiese etiek\nDie teks van Boek 51 2 noem of illustreer: Praktiese etiek. Lees daardie verse weer en skryf presies op wat die Bybel sê — nie wat jy dink nie.\n\nWhat God wants us to know:\nGod wil gelowiges laat weet evangelie-waarheid en hoe dit kerklewe, heiligheid en liefde moet vorm.\n\nWhy:\nPaulus redeneer van wat Christus gedoen het na hoe Christene moet leef. Soek die leerstelling in hierdie hoofstuk en die lewe wat dit verbind.\n\nSimilar elsewhere:\nBook 51 1: Compare with Book 51 1, wat direct voor hierdie hoofstuk kom — let op wat voortgaan of verander.","questions_en":["What does this passage reveal about God?","What promise, command, or truth stands out to you?","How can you apply this to your life today?"],"questions_af":["Wat openbaar hierdie gedeelte oor God?","Watter belofte, gebod of waarheid val vir jou op?","Hoe kan jy dit vandag in jou lewe toepas?"]},{"day":61,"title_en":"Colossians 3 – 1 Thessalonians 1","title_af":"Kolossense 3 – 1 Tessalonisense 1","pa