","Liefde en eenheid","Hoop in Christus se wederkoms"]}],"commentary_en":"New Testament reading for today. Each section summarizes a chapter so you can follow the flow of the text.\n\nBook 58 13\nBook 58 13. Pastoral encouragement for faith under pressure. Look for calls to endurance, love, holiness, and confident hope in Christ. Read Book 58 13 yourself and verify each statement against the verses in your Bible version.\n\nEndurance in trials\nThe text of Book 58 13 records or illustrates: Endurance in trials. Re-read those verses and note exactly what Scripture states.\n\nLove and unity\nThe text of Book 58 13 records or illustrates: Love and unity. Re-read those verses and note exactly what Scripture states.\n\nHope in Christ''s return\nThe text of Book 58 13 records or illustrates: Hope in Christ''s return. Re-read those verses and note exactly what Scripture states.\n\nWhat God wants us to know:\nGod wants his people to remain faithful under pressure, love one another, and hold to hope in Christ.\n\nWhy:\nThese letters encourage endurance and holy living. Notice exhortations in this chapter and the reason the writer gives for obeying them.\n\nSimilar elsewhere:\nBook 58 12: Compare with Book 58 12, which immediately precedes this chapter in the same book — notice what events or themes continue or change.\n\nBook 59 1\nBook 59 1. Pastoral encouragement for faith under pressure. Look for calls to endurance, love, holiness, and confident hope in Christ. Read Book 59 1 yourself and verify each statement against the verses in your Bible version.\n\nEndurance in trials\nThe text of Book 59 1 records or illustrates: Endurance in trials. Re-read those verses and note exactly what Scripture states.\n\nLove and unity\nThe text of Book 59 1 records or illustrates: Love and unity. Re-read those verses and note exactly what Scripture states.\n\nHope in Christ''s return\nThe text of Book 59 1 records or illustrates: Hope in Christ''s return. Re-read those verses and note exactly what Scripture states.\n\nWhat God wants us to know:\nGod wants his people to remain faithful under pressure, love one another, and hold to hope in Christ.\n\nWhy:\nThese letters encourage endurance and holy living. Notice exhortations in this chapter and the reason the writer gives for obeying them.\n\nBook 59 2\nBook 59 2. Pastoral encouragement for faith under pressure. Look for calls to endurance, love, holiness, and confident hope in Christ. Read Book 59 2 yourself and verify each statement against the verses in your Bible version.\n\nEndurance in trials\nThe text of Book 59 2 records or illustrates: Endurance in trials. Re-read those verses and note exactly what Scripture states.\n\nLove and unity\nThe text of Book 59 2 records or illustrates: Love and unity. Re-read those verses and note exactly what Scripture states.\n\nHope in Christ''s return\nThe text of Book 59 2 records or illustrates: Hope in Christ''s return. Re-read those verses and note exactly what Scripture states.\n\nWhat God wants us to know:\nGod wants his people to remain faithful under pressure, love one another, and hold to hope in Christ.\n\nWhy:\nThese letters encourage endurance and holy living. Notice exhortations in this chapter and the reason the writer gives for obeying them.\n\nSimilar elsewhere:\nBook 59 1: Compare with Book 59 1, which immediately precedes this chapter in the same book — notice what events or themes continue or change.","commentary_af":"Nuwe Testament leeswerk vir vandag. Elke afdeling som ''n hoofstuk op sodat jy die vloei van die teks kan volg.\n\nBoek 58 13\nBoek 58 13. Pastorale bemoediging vir geloof onder druk. Soek oproepe tot volharding, liefde, heiligheid en versekerde hoop in Christus. Lees Boek 58 13 self en kontroleer elke stelling teen die verse in jou Bybelweergawe.\n\nVolharding in beproewing\nDie teks van Boek 58 13 noem of illustreer: Volharding in beproewing. Lees daardie verse weer en skryf presies op wat die Bybel sê — nie wat jy dink nie.\n\nLiefde en eenheid\nDie teks van Boek 58 13 noem of illustreer: Liefde en eenheid. Lees daardie verse weer en skryf presies op wat die Bybel sê — nie wat jy dink nie.\n\nHoop in Christus se wederkoms\nDie teks van Boek 58 13 noem of illustreer: Hoop in Christus se wederkoms. Lees daardie verse weer en skryf presies op wat die Bybel sê — nie wat jy dink nie.\n\nWhat God wants us to know:\nGod wil sy volk laat bly volhard onder druk, mekaar liefhê, en hoop in Christus hou.\n\nWhy:\nHierdie briewe moedig volharding en heilige lewe aan. Let op aansporings in hierdie hoofstuk en die rede wat die skrywer gee.\n\nSimilar elsewhere:\nBook 58 12: Compare with Book 58 12, wat direct voor hierdie hoofstuk kom — let op wat voortgaan of verander.\n\nBoek 59 1\nBoek 59 1. Pastorale bemoediging vir geloof onder druk. Soek oproepe tot volharding, liefde, heiligheid en versekerde hoop in Christus. Lees Boek 59 1 self en kontroleer elke stelling teen die verse in jou Bybelweergawe.\n\nVolharding in beproewing\nDie teks van Boek 59 1 noem of illustreer: Volharding in beproewing. Lees daardie verse weer en skryf presies op wat die Bybel sê — nie wat jy dink nie.\n\nLiefde en eenheid\nDie teks van Boek 59 1 noem of illustreer: Liefde en eenheid. Lees daardie verse weer en skryf presies op wat die Bybel sê — nie wat jy dink nie.\n\nHoop in Christus se wederkoms\nDie teks van Boek 59 1 noem of illustreer: Hoop in Christus se wederkoms. Lees daardie verse weer en skryf presies op wat die Bybel sê — nie wat jy dink nie.\n\nWhat God wants us to know:\nGod wil sy volk laat bly volhard onder druk, mekaar liefhê, en hoop in Christus hou.\n\nWhy:\nHierdie briewe moedig volharding en heilige lewe aan. Let op aansporings in hierdie hoofstuk en die rede wat die skrywer gee.\n\nBoek 59 2\nBoek 59 2. Pastorale bemoediging vir geloof onder druk. Soek oproepe tot volharding, liefde, heiligheid en versekerde hoop in Christus. Lees Boek 59 2 self en kontroleer elke stelling teen die verse in jou Bybelw