ist''s return"],"highlights_af":["Volharding in beproewing","Liefde en eenheid","Hoop in Christus se wederkoms"]}],"commentary_en":"New Testament reading for today. Each section summarizes a chapter so you can follow the flow of the text.\n\nBook 60 4\nBook 60 4. Pastoral encouragement for faith under pressure. Look for calls to endurance, love, holiness, and confident hope in Christ. Read Book 60 4 yourself and verify each statement against the verses in your Bible version.\n\nEndurance in trials\nThe text of Book 60 4 records or illustrates: Endurance in trials. Re-read those verses and note exactly what Scripture states.\n\nLove and unity\nThe text of Book 60 4 records or illustrates: Love and unity. Re-read those verses and note exactly what Scripture states.\n\nHope in Christ''s return\nThe text of Book 60 4 records or illustrates: Hope in Christ''s return. Re-read those verses and note exactly what Scripture states.\n\nWhat God wants us to know:\nGod wants his people to remain faithful under pressure, love one another, and hold to hope in Christ.\n\nWhy:\nThese letters encourage endurance and holy living. Notice exhortations in this chapter and the reason the writer gives for obeying them.\n\nSimilar elsewhere:\nBook 60 3: Compare with Book 60 3, which immediately precedes this chapter in the same book — notice what events or themes continue or change.\n\nBook 60 5\nBook 60 5. Pastoral encouragement for faith under pressure. Look for calls to endurance, love, holiness, and confident hope in Christ. Read Book 60 5 yourself and verify each statement against the verses in your Bible version.\n\nEndurance in trials\nThe text of Book 60 5 records or illustrates: Endurance in trials. Re-read those verses and note exactly what Scripture states.\n\nLove and unity\nThe text of Book 60 5 records or illustrates: Love and unity. Re-read those verses and note exactly what Scripture states.\n\nHope in Christ''s return\nThe text of Book 60 5 records or illustrates: Hope in Christ''s return. Re-read those verses and note exactly what Scripture states.\n\nWhat God wants us to know:\nGod wants his people to remain faithful under pressure, love one another, and hold to hope in Christ.\n\nWhy:\nThese letters encourage endurance and holy living. Notice exhortations in this chapter and the reason the writer gives for obeying them.\n\nSimilar elsewhere:\nBook 60 4: Compare with Book 60 4, which immediately precedes this chapter in the same book — notice what events or themes continue or change.\n\nBook 61 1\nBook 61 1. Pastoral encouragement for faith under pressure. Look for calls to endurance, love, holiness, and confident hope in Christ. Read Book 61 1 yourself and verify each statement against the verses in your Bible version.\n\nEndurance in trials\nThe text of Book 61 1 records or illustrates: Endurance in trials. Re-read those verses and note exactly what Scripture states.\n\nLove and unity\nThe text of Book 61 1 records or illustrates: Love and unity. Re-read those verses and note exactly what Scripture states.\n\nHope in Christ''s return\nThe text of Book 61 1 records or illustrates: Hope in Christ''s return. Re-read those verses and note exactly what Scripture states.\n\nWhat God wants us to know:\nGod wants his people to remain faithful under pressure, love one another, and hold to hope in Christ.\n\nWhy:\nThese letters encourage endurance and holy living. Notice exhortations in this chapter and the reason the writer gives for obeying them.","commentary_af":"Nuwe Testament leeswerk vir vandag. Elke afdeling som ''n hoofstuk op sodat jy die vloei van die teks kan volg.\n\nBoek 60 4\nBoek 60 4. Pastorale bemoediging vir geloof onder druk. Soek oproepe tot volharding, liefde, heiligheid en versekerde hoop in Christus. Lees Boek 60 4 self en kontroleer elke stelling teen die verse in jou Bybelweergawe.\n\nVolharding in beproewing\nDie teks van Boek 60 4 noem of illustreer: Volharding in beproewing. Lees daardie verse weer en skryf presies op wat die Bybel sê — nie wat jy dink nie.\n\nLiefde en eenheid\nDie teks van Boek 60 4 noem of illustreer: Liefde en eenheid. Lees daardie verse weer en skryf presies op wat die Bybel sê — nie wat jy dink nie.\n\nHoop in Christus se wederkoms\nDie teks van Boek 60 4 noem of illustreer: Hoop in Christus se wederkoms. Lees daardie verse weer en skryf presies op wat die Bybel sê — nie wat jy dink nie.\n\nWhat God wants us to know:\nGod wil sy volk laat bly volhard onder druk, mekaar liefhê, en hoop in Christus hou.\n\nWhy:\nHierdie briewe moedig volharding en heilige lewe aan. Let op aansporings in hierdie hoofstuk en die rede wat die skrywer gee.\n\nSimilar elsewhere:\nBook 60 3: Compare with Book 60 3, wat direct voor hierdie hoofstuk kom — let op wat voortgaan of verander.\n\nBoek 60 5\nBoek 60 5. Pastorale bemoediging vir geloof onder druk. Soek oproepe tot volharding, liefde, heiligheid en versekerde hoop in Christus. Lees Boek 60 5 self en kontroleer elke stelling teen die verse in jou Bybelweergawe.\n\nVolharding in beproewing\nDie teks van Boek 60 5 noem of illustreer: Volharding in beproewing. Lees daardie verse weer en skryf presies op wat die Bybel sê — nie wat jy dink nie.\n\nLiefde en eenheid\nDie teks van Boek 60 5 noem of illustreer: Liefde en eenheid. Lees daardie verse weer en skryf presies op wat die Bybel sê — nie wat jy dink nie.\n\nHoop in Christus se wederkoms\nDie teks van Boek 60 5 noem of illustreer: Hoop in Christus se wederkoms. Lees daardie verse weer en skryf presies op wat die Bybel sê — nie wat jy dink nie.\n\nWhat God wants us to know:\nGod wil sy volk laat bly volhard onder druk, mekaar liefhê, en hoop in Christus hou.\n\nWhy:\nHierdie briewe moedig volharding en heilige lewe aan. Let op aansporings in hierdie hoofstuk en die rede wat die skrywer gee.\n\nSimilar elsewhere:\nBook 60 4: Compare with Book 60 4, wat direct voor hierdie hoofstuk kom — let op wat voortgaan of verander.\n\nBoek 61 1\nBoek 61 1. Pastorale bemoediging vir ge