ent against the verses in your Bible version.\n\nGod''s sovereignty in history\nThe text of Book 14 19 records or illustrates: God''s sovereignty in history. Re-read those verses and note exactly what Scripture states.\n\nFaithful vs. unfaithful leaders\nThe text of Book 14 19 records or illustrates: Faithful vs. unfaithful leaders. Re-read those verses and note exactly what Scripture states.\n\nRepentance and restoration\nThe text of Book 14 19 records or illustrates: Repentance and restoration. Re-read those verses and note exactly what Scripture states.\n\nWhat God wants us to know:\nGod wants us to see that he works through history—using leaders, correcting rebellion, and keeping his promises across generations.\n\nWhy:\nHistorical books record outcomes when people follow or abandon God''s command. Notice who leads, what they do, and what the chapter says happened as a result.\n\nSimilar elsewhere:\nBook 14 18: Compare with Book 14 18, which immediately precedes this chapter in the same book — notice what events or themes continue or change.\n\nBook 14 20\nBook 14 20. Historical narrative showing God''s guidance through victory, failure, and restoration. Notice leadership, prayer, and the consequences of turning from God. Read Book 14 20 yourself and verify each statement against the verses in your Bible version.\n\nGod''s sovereignty in history\nThe text of Book 14 20 records or illustrates: God''s sovereignty in history. Re-read those verses and note exactly what Scripture states.\n\nFaithful vs. unfaithful leaders\nThe text of Book 14 20 records or illustrates: Faithful vs. unfaithful leaders. Re-read those verses and note exactly what Scripture states.\n\nRepentance and restoration\nThe text of Book 14 20 records or illustrates: Repentance and restoration. Re-read those verses and note exactly what Scripture states.\n\nWhat God wants us to know:\nGod wants us to see that he works through history—using leaders, correcting rebellion, and keeping his promises across generations.\n\nWhy:\nHistorical books record outcomes when people follow or abandon God''s command. Notice who leads, what they do, and what the chapter says happened as a result.\n\nSimilar elsewhere:\nBook 14 19: Compare with Book 14 19, which immediately precedes this chapter in the same book — notice what events or themes continue or change.\n\nBook 14 21\nBook 14 21. Historical narrative showing God''s guidance through victory, failure, and restoration. Notice leadership, prayer, and the consequences of turning from God. Read Book 14 21 yourself and verify each statement against the verses in your Bible version.\n\nGod''s sovereignty in history\nThe text of Book 14 21 records or illustrates: God''s sovereignty in history. Re-read those verses and note exactly what Scripture states.\n\nFaithful vs. unfaithful leaders\nThe text of Book 14 21 records or illustrates: Faithful vs. unfaithful leaders. Re-read those verses and note exactly what Scripture states.\n\nRepentance and restoration\nThe text of Book 14 21 records or illustrates: Repentance and restoration. Re-read those verses and note exactly what Scripture states.\n\nWhat God wants us to know:\nGod wants us to see that he works through history—using leaders, correcting rebellion, and keeping his promises across generations.\n\nWhy:\nHistorical books record outcomes when people follow or abandon God''s command. Notice who leads, what they do, and what the chapter says happened as a result.\n\nSimilar elsewhere:\nBook 14 20: Compare with Book 14 20, which immediately precedes this chapter in the same book — notice what events or themes continue or change.","commentary_af":"Jy lees deur die hele Bybel. Elke hoofstuk-opsomming hieronder help jou die hoofverhaal te begryp voordat jy die verse lees.\n\nBoek 14 19\nBoek 14 19. Geskiedenisverhaal wat God se leiding wys deur oorwinning, mislukking en herstel. Let op leierskap, gebed en die gevolge van wegdraai van God. Lees Boek 14 19 self en kontroleer elke stelling teen die verse in jou Bybelweergawe.\n\nGod se soewereiniteit in geskiedenis\nDie teks van Boek 14 19 noem of illustreer: God se soewereiniteit in geskiedenis. Lees daardie verse weer en skryf presies op wat die Bybel sê — nie wat jy dink nie.\n\nGetroue vs. ontroue leiers\nDie teks van Boek 14 19 noem of illustreer: Getroue vs. ontroue leiers. Lees daardie verse weer en skryf presies op wat die Bybel sê — nie wat jy dink nie.\n\nBerou en herstel\nDie teks van Boek 14 19 noem of illustreer: Berou en herstel. Lees daardie verse weer en skryf presies op wat die Bybel sê — nie wat jy dink nie.\n\nWhat God wants us to know:\nGod wil hê ons moet sien dat Hy deur geskiedenis werk—leiers gebruik, rebelle regstel, en beloftes oor geslagte heen hou.\n\nWhy:\nGeskiedenisboeke beskryf uitkomste wanneer mense God se gebod volg of verlaat. Let wie lei, wat hulle doen, en wat die hoofstuk sê het gebeur.\n\nSimilar elsewhere:\nBook 14 18: Compare with Book 14 18, wat direct voor hierdie hoofstuk kom — let op wat voortgaan of verander.\n\nBoek 14 20\nBoek 14 20. Geskiedenisverhaal wat God se leiding wys deur oorwinning, mislukking en herstel. Let op leierskap, gebed en die gevolge van wegdraai van God. Lees Boek 14 20 self en kontroleer elke stelling teen die verse in jou Bybelweergawe.\n\nGod se soewereiniteit in geskiedenis\nDie teks van Boek 14 20 noem of illustreer: God se soewereiniteit in geskiedenis. Lees daardie verse weer en skryf presies op wat die Bybel sê — nie wat jy dink nie.\n\nGetroue vs. ontroue leiers\nDie teks van Boek 14 20 noem of illustreer: Getroue vs. ontroue leiers. Lees daardie verse weer en skryf presies op wat die Bybel sê — nie wat jy dink nie.\n\nBerou en herstel\nDie teks van Boek 14 20 noem of illustreer: Berou en herstel. Lees daardie verse weer en skryf presies op wat die Bybel sê — nie wat jy dink nie.\n\nWhat God wants us to know:\nGod wil hê ons moet sien dat Hy deur geskiedenis werk—leiers gebruik, rebelle regstel, en beloftes oor geslagte heen hou.\n\nWhy:\nGeskiedenisboeke beskryf uitkomste wanneer mense God se gebod volg of verlaat. Let wie lei, wat hulle doen, en wat die hoofstuk sê het gebeur.\n\nSimilar elsewhere:\nBook 14 19: Compare with Book 14 19, wat direct voor hierdie hoofstuk kom — let op wat voortgaan of verander.\n\nBoek 14 21\nBoek 14 21. Geskiedenisverhaal wat God se leiding wys deur oorwinning, mislukking en herstel. Let op leierskap, gebed en die gevolge van wegdraai van God. Lees Boek 14 21 self en kontroleer elke stelling teen die verse in jou Bybelweergawe.\n\nGod se soewereiniteit in geskiedenis\nDie teks van Boek 14 21 noem of illustreer: God se soewereiniteit in geskiedenis. Lees daardie verse weer en skryf presies op wat die Bybel sê — nie wat jy dink nie.\n\nGetroue vs. ontroue leiers\nDie teks van Boek 14 21 noem of illustreer: Getroue vs. ontroue leiers. Lees daardie verse weer en skryf presies op wat die Bybel sê — nie wat jy dink nie.\n\nBerou en herstel\nDie teks van Boek 14 21 noem of illustreer: Berou en herstel. Lees daardie verse weer en skryf presies op wat die Bybel sê — nie wat jy dink nie.\n\nWhat God wants us to know:\nGod wil hê ons moet sien dat Hy deur geskiedenis werk—leiers gebruik, rebelle regstel, en beloftes oor geslagte heen hou.\n\nWhy:\nGeskiedenisboeke beskryf uitkomste wanneer mense God se gebod volg of verlaat. Let wie lei, wat hulle doen, en wat die hoofstuk sê het gebeur.\n\nSimilar elsewhere:\nBook 14 20: Compare with Book 14 20, wat direct voor hierdie hoofstuk kom — let op wat voortgaan of verander.","questions_en":["What does this passage reveal about God?","What promise, command, or truth stands out to you?","How can you apply this to your life today?"],"questions_af":["Wat openbaar hierdie gedeelte oor God?","Watter belofte, gebod of waarheid val vir jou op?","Hoe kan jy dit vandag in jou lewe toepas?"]},{"day":99,"title_en":"2 Chronicles 22–24","title_af":"2 Kronieke 22–24","passages":[{"book_id":14,"chapter":22},{"book_id":14,"cha