","Faithful vs. unfaithful leaders","Repentance and restoration"],"highlights_af":["God se soewereiniteit in geskiedenis","Getroue vs. ontroue leiers","Berou en herstel"]}],"commentary_en":"You are reading through the whole Bible. Each chapter summary below helps you grasp the main story before you read the verses.\n\nBook 17 2\nBook 17 2. Historical narrative showing God''s guidance through victory, failure, and restoration. Notice leadership, prayer, and the consequences of turning from God. Read Book 17 2 yourself and verify each statement against the verses in your Bible version.\n\nGod''s sovereignty in history\nThe text of Book 17 2 records or illustrates: God''s sovereignty in history. Re-read those verses and note exactly what Scripture states.\n\nFaithful vs. unfaithful leaders\nThe text of Book 17 2 records or illustrates: Faithful vs. unfaithful leaders. Re-read those verses and note exactly what Scripture states.\n\nRepentance and restoration\nThe text of Book 17 2 records or illustrates: Repentance and restoration. Re-read those verses and note exactly what Scripture states.\n\nWhat God wants us to know:\nGod wants us to see that he works through history—using leaders, correcting rebellion, and keeping his promises across generations.\n\nWhy:\nHistorical books record outcomes when people follow or abandon God''s command. Notice who leads, what they do, and what the chapter says happened as a result.\n\nSimilar elsewhere:\nBook 17 1: Compare with Book 17 1, which immediately precedes this chapter in the same book — notice what events or themes continue or change.\n\nBook 17 3\nBook 17 3. Historical narrative showing God''s guidance through victory, failure, and restoration. Notice leadership, prayer, and the consequences of turning from God. Read Book 17 3 yourself and verify each statement against the verses in your Bible version.\n\nGod''s sovereignty in history\nThe text of Book 17 3 records or illustrates: God''s sovereignty in history. Re-read those verses and note exactly what Scripture states.\n\nFaithful vs. unfaithful leaders\nThe text of Book 17 3 records or illustrates: Faithful vs. unfaithful leaders. Re-read those verses and note exactly what Scripture states.\n\nRepentance and restoration\nThe text of Book 17 3 records or illustrates: Repentance and restoration. Re-read those verses and note exactly what Scripture states.\n\nWhat God wants us to know:\nGod wants us to see that he works through history—using leaders, correcting rebellion, and keeping his promises across generations.\n\nWhy:\nHistorical books record outcomes when people follow or abandon God''s command. Notice who leads, what they do, and what the chapter says happened as a result.\n\nSimilar elsewhere:\nBook 17 2: Compare with Book 17 2, which immediately precedes this chapter in the same book — notice what events or themes continue or change.\n\nBook 17 4\nBook 17 4. Historical narrative showing God''s guidance through victory, failure, and restoration. Notice leadership, prayer, and the consequences of turning from God. Read Book 17 4 yourself and verify each statement against the verses in your Bible version.\n\nGod''s sovereignty in history\nThe text of Book 17 4 records or illustrates: God''s sovereignty in history. Re-read those verses and note exactly what Scripture states.\n\nFaithful vs. unfaithful leaders\nThe text of Book 17 4 records or illustrates: Faithful vs. unfaithful leaders. Re-read those verses and note exactly what Scripture states.\n\nRepentance and restoration\nThe text of Book 17 4 records or illustrates: Repentance and restoration. Re-read those verses and note exactly what Scripture states.\n\nWhat God wants us to know:\nGod wants us to see that he works through history—using leaders, correcting rebellion, and keeping his promises across generations.\n\nWhy:\nHistorical books record outcomes when people follow or abandon God''s command. Notice who leads, what they do, and what the chapter says happened as a result.\n\nSimilar elsewhere:\nBook 17 3: Compare with Book 17 3, which immediately precedes this chapter in the same book — notice what events or themes continue or change.","commentary_af":"Jy lees deur die hele Bybel. Elke hoofstuk-opsomming hieronder help jou die hoofverhaal te begryp voordat jy die verse lees.\n\nBoek 17 2\nBoek 17 2. Geskiedenisverhaal wat God se leiding wys deur oorwinning, mislukking en herstel. Let op leierskap, gebed en die gevolge van wegdraai van God. Lees Boek 17 2 self en kontroleer elke stelling teen die verse in jou Bybelweergawe.\n\nGod se soewereiniteit in geskiedenis\nDie teks van Boek 17 2 noem of illustreer: God se soewereiniteit in geskiedenis. Lees daardie verse weer en skryf presies op wat die Bybel sê — nie wat jy dink nie.\n\nGetroue vs. ontroue leiers\nDie teks van Boek 17 2 noem of illustreer: Getroue vs. ontroue leiers. Lees daardie verse weer en skryf presies op wat die Bybel sê — nie wat jy dink nie.\n\nBerou en herstel\nDie teks van Boek 17 2 noem of illustreer: Berou en herstel. Lees daardie verse weer en skryf presies op wat die Bybel sê — nie wat jy dink nie.\n\nWhat God wants us to know:\nGod wil hê ons moet sien dat Hy deur geskiedenis werk—leiers gebruik, rebelle regstel, en beloftes oor geslagte heen hou.\n\nWhy:\nGeskiedenisboeke beskryf uitkomste wanneer mense God se gebod volg of verlaat. Let wie lei, wat hulle doen, en wat die hoofstuk sê het gebeur.\n\nSimilar elsewhere:\nBook 17 1: Compare with Book 17 1, wat direct voor hierdie hoofstuk kom — let op wat voortgaan of verander.\n\nBoek 17 3\nBoek 17 3. Geskiedenisverhaal wat God se leiding wys deur oorwinning, mislukking en herstel. Let op leierskap, gebed en die gevolge van wegdraai van God. Lees Boek 17 3 self en kontroleer elke stelling teen die verse in jou Bybelweergawe.\n\nGod se soewereiniteit in geskiedenis\nDie teks van Boek 17 3 noem of illustreer: God se soewereiniteit in geskiedenis. Lees daardie verse weer en skryf presies op wat die Bybel sê — nie wat jy dink nie.\n\nGetroue vs. ontroue leiers\nDie teks van Boek 17 3 noem of illustreer: Getroue vs. ontroue leiers. Lees daardie verse weer en skryf presies op wat die Bybel sê — nie wat jy dink nie.\n\nBerou en herstel\nDie teks van Boek 17 3 noem of illustreer: Berou en herstel. Lees daardie verse weer en skryf presies op wat die Bybel sê — nie wat jy dink nie.\n\nWhat God wants us to know:\nGod wil hê ons moet sien dat Hy deur geskiedenis werk—leiers gebruik, rebelle regstel, en beloftes oor geslagte heen hou.\n\nWhy:\nGeskiedenisboeke beskryf uitkomste wanneer mense God se gebod volg of verlaat. Let wie lei, wat hulle doen, en wat die hoofstuk sê het gebeur.\n\nSimilar elsewhere:\nBook 17 2: Compare with Book 17 2, wat direct voor hierdie hoofstuk kom — let op wat voortgaan of verander.\n\nBoek 17 4\nBoek 17 4. Geskiedenisverhaal wat God se leiding wys deur oorwinning, mislukking en herstel. Let op leierskap, gebed en die gevolge van wegdraai van God. Lees Boek 17 4 self en kontroleer elke stelling teen die verse in jou Bybelweergawe.\n\nGod se soewereiniteit in geskiedenis\nDie teks van Boek 17 4 noem of illustreer: God se soewereiniteit in geskiedenis. Lees daardie verse weer en skryf presies op wat die Bybel sê — nie wat jy dink nie.\n\nGetroue vs. ontroue leiers\nDie teks van Boek 17 4 noem of illustreer: Getroue vs. ontroue leiers. Lees daardie verse weer en skryf presies op wat die Bybel sê — nie wat jy dink nie.\n\nBerou en herstel\nDie teks van Boek 17 4 noem of illustreer: Berou en herstel. Lees daardie verse weer en skryf presies op wat die Bybel sê — nie wat jy dink nie.\n\nWhat God wants us to know:\nGod wil hê ons moet sien dat Hy deur geskiedenis werk—leiers gebruik, rebelle regstel, en beloftes oor geslagte heen hou.\n\nWhy:\nGeskiedenisboeke beskryf uitkomste wanneer mense God se gebod volg of verlaat. Let wie lei, wat hulle doen, en wat die hoofstuk sê het gebeur.\n\nSimilar elsewhere:\nBook 17 3: Compare with Book 17 3, wat direct voor h