:7","comparison":"Wysheidsboeke herhaal dat die vrees vir die Here die begin van wysheid is (Spr 1:7). Vergelyk hoe elke psalm of spreuk dit toepas."}],"highlights_en":["Fear of the Lord","Honest self-reflection","Practical daily application"],"highlights_af":["Vrees vir die Here","Eerlike selfondersoek","Praktiese daaglikse toepassing"]}],"commentary_en":"You are reading through the whole Bible. Each chapter summary below helps you grasp the main story before you read the verses.\n\nBook 18 10\nBook 18 10. Wisdom literature for worship, prayer, and practical living. Apply its truths to your relationships, work, and inner life. Read Book 18 10 yourself and verify each statement against the verses in your Bible version.\n\nFear of the Lord\nThe text of Book 18 10 records or illustrates: Fear of the Lord. Re-read those verses and note exactly what Scripture states.\n\nHonest self-reflection\nThe text of Book 18 10 records or illustrates: Honest self-reflection. Re-read those verses and note exactly what Scripture states.\n\nPractical daily application\nThe text of Book 18 10 records or illustrates: Practical daily application. Re-read those verses and note exactly what Scripture states.\n\nWhat God wants us to know:\nGod wants us to know that true wisdom begins with reverence for him and shapes daily choices, speech, and worship.\n\nWhy:\nWisdom passages tie understanding to the fear of the Lord and practical living. Notice commands, prayers, or counsel in this chapter and what attitude toward God they assume.\n\nSimilar elsewhere:\nBook 18 9: Compare with Book 18 9, which immediately precedes this chapter in the same book — notice what events or themes continue or change.\nProverbs 1:7: Wisdom books often repeat the theme that the fear of the Lord is the beginning of wisdom (Proverbs 1:7). Compare how each psalm or proverb applies that foundation differently.\n\nBook 18 11\nBook 18 11. Wisdom literature for worship, prayer, and practical living. Apply its truths to your relationships, work, and inner life. Read Book 18 11 yourself and verify each statement against the verses in your Bible version.\n\nFear of the Lord\nThe text of Book 18 11 records or illustrates: Fear of the Lord. Re-read those verses and note exactly what Scripture states.\n\nHonest self-reflection\nThe text of Book 18 11 records or illustrates: Honest self-reflection. Re-read those verses and note exactly what Scripture states.\n\nPractical daily application\nThe text of Book 18 11 records or illustrates: Practical daily application. Re-read those verses and note exactly what Scripture states.\n\nWhat God wants us to know:\nGod wants us to know that true wisdom begins with reverence for him and shapes daily choices, speech, and worship.\n\nWhy:\nWisdom passages tie understanding to the fear of the Lord and practical living. Notice commands, prayers, or counsel in this chapter and what attitude toward God they assume.\n\nSimilar elsewhere:\nBook 18 10: Compare with Book 18 10, which immediately precedes this chapter in the same book — notice what events or themes continue or change.\nProverbs 1:7: Wisdom books often repeat the theme that the fear of the Lord is the beginning of wisdom (Proverbs 1:7). Compare how each psalm or proverb applies that foundation differently.\n\nBook 18 12\nBook 18 12. Wisdom literature for worship, prayer, and practical living. Apply its truths to your relationships, work, and inner life. Read Book 18 12 yourself and verify each statement against the verses in your Bible version.\n\nFear of the Lord\nThe text of Book 18 12 records or illustrates: Fear of the Lord. Re-read those verses and note exactly what Scripture states.\n\nHonest self-reflection\nThe text of Book 18 12 records or illustrates: Honest self-reflection. Re-read those verses and note exactly what Scripture states.\n\nPractical daily application\nThe text of Book 18 12 records or illustrates: Practical daily application. Re-read those verses and note exactly what Scripture states.\n\nWhat God wants us to know:\nGod wants us to know that true wisdom begins with reverence for him and shapes daily choices, speech, and worship.\n\nWhy:\nWisdom passages tie understanding to the fear of the Lord and practical living. Notice commands, prayers, or counsel in this chapter and what attitude toward God they assume.\n\nSimilar elsewhere:\nBook 18 11: Compare with Book 18 11, which immediately precedes this chapter in the same book — notice what events or themes continue or change.\nProverbs 1:7: Wisdom books often repeat the theme that the fear of the Lord is the beginning of wisdom (Proverbs 1:7). Compare how each psalm or proverb applies that foundation differently.","commentary_af":"Jy lees deur die hele Bybel. Elke hoofstuk-opsomming hieronder help jou die hoofverhaal te begryp voordat jy die verse lees.\n\nBoek 18 10\nBoek 18 10. Wysheidsliteratuur vir aanbidding, gebed en praktiese lewe. Pas die waarhede toe op jou verhoudings, werk en innerlike lewe. Lees Boek 18 10 self en kontroleer elke stelling teen die verse in jou Bybelweergawe.\n\nVrees vir die Here\nDie teks van Boek 18 10 noem of illustreer: Vrees vir die Here. Lees daardie verse weer en skryf presies op wat die Bybel sê — nie wat jy dink nie.\n\nEerlike selfondersoek\nDie teks van Boek 18 10 noem of illustreer: Eerlike selfondersoek. Lees daardie verse weer en skryf presies op wat die Bybel sê — nie wat jy dink nie.\n\nPraktiese daaglikse toepassing\nDie teks van Boek 18 10 noem of illustreer: Praktiese daaglikse toepassing. Lees daardie verse weer en skryf presies op wat die Bybel sê — nie wat jy dink nie.\n\nWhat God wants us to know:\nGod wil hê ons moet weet dat ware wysheid begin met eerbied vir Hom en daaglikse keuses, spraak en aanbidding vorm.\n\nWhy:\nWysheid verbind insig met die vrees vir die Here. Let op gebooie, gebede of raad in hierdie hoofstuk en watter houding teenoor God dit veronderstel.\n\nSimilar elsewhere:\nBook 18 9: Compare with Book 18 9, wat direct voor hierdie hoofstuk kom — let op wat voortgaan of verander.\nSpreuke 1:7: Wysheidsboeke herhaal dat die vrees vir die Here die begin van wysheid is (Spr 1:7). Vergelyk hoe elke psalm of spreuk dit toepas.\n\nBoek 18 11\nBoek 18 11. Wysheidsliteratuur vir aanbidding, gebed en praktiese lewe. Pas die waarhede toe op jou verhoudings, werk en innerlike lewe. Lees Boek 18 11 self en kontroleer elke stelling teen die verse in jou Bybelweergawe.\n\nVrees vir die Here\nDie teks van Boek 18 11 noem of illustreer: Vrees vir die Here. Lees daardie verse weer en skryf presies op wat die Bybel sê — nie wat jy dink nie.\n\nEerlike selfondersoek\nDie teks van Boek 18 11 noem of illustreer: Eerlike selfondersoek. Lees daardie verse weer en skryf presies op wat die Bybel sê — nie wat jy dink nie.\n\nPraktiese daaglikse toepassing\nDie teks van Boek 18 11 noem of illustreer: Praktiese daaglikse toepassing. Lees daardie verse weer en skryf presies op wat die Bybel sê — nie wat jy dink nie.\n\nWhat God wants us to know:\nGod wil hê ons moet weet dat ware wysheid begin met eerbied vir Hom en daaglikse keuses, spraak en aanbidding vorm.\n\nWhy:\nWysheid verbind insig met die vrees vir die Here. Let op gebooie, gebede of raad in hierdie hoofstuk en watter houding teenoor God dit veronderstel.\n\nSimilar elsewhere:\nBook 18 10: Compare with Book 18 10, wat direct voor hierdie hoofstuk kom — let op wat voortgaan of verander.\nSpreuke 1:7: Wysheidsboeke herhaal dat die vrees vir die Here die begin van wysheid is (Spr 1:7). Vergelyk hoe elke psalm of spreuk dit toepas.\n\nBoek 18 12\nBoek 18 12. Wysheidsliteratuur vir aanbidding, gebed en praktiese lewe. Pas die waarhede toe op jou verhoudings, werk en innerlike lewe. Lees Boek 18 12 self en kontroleer elke stelling teen die verse in jou Bybelweergawe.\n\nVrees vir die Here\nDie teks van Boek 18 12 noem of illustreer: Vrees vir die Here. Lees daardie verse weer en skryf presies op wat die Bybel sê — nie wat jy dink nie.\n\nEerlike selfondersoek\nDie teks van Boek 18 12 noem of illustreer: Eerlike selfondersoek. Lees daardie verse weer en skryf presies op wat die Bybel sê — nie wat jy dink nie.\n\nPraktiese daaglikse toepassing\nDie teks van Boek 18 12 noem of illustreer: Praktiese daaglikse toepassing. Lees daardie verse weer en skryf presies op wat die Bybel sê — nie wat jy dink nie.\n\nWhat God wants us to know:\nGod wil hê ons moet weet dat ware wysheid begin met eerbied vir Hom en daaglikse keuses, spraak en aanbidding vorm.\n\nWhy:\nWysheid verbind insig met die vrees vir die Here. Let op gebooie, gebede of raad in hierdie hoofstuk en watter houding teenoor God dit veronderstel.\n\nSimilar elsewhere:\nBook 18 11: Compare with Book 18 11, wat direct voor hierdie hoofstuk kom — let op wat voortgaan of verander.\nSpreuke 1:7: Wysheidsboeke herhaal dat die vrees vir die Here die begin van wysheid is (Spr 1:7). Vergelyk hoe elke psalm of spreuk dit toepas.","questions_en":["What does this passage reveal about God?","What promise, command, or truth stands out to you?","How can you apply this to your life today?"],"questions_af":["Wat openbaar hierdie gedeelte oor God?","Watter belofte, gebod of waarheid val vir jou op?","Hoe kan jy dit vandag in jou lewe toepas?"]},{"day":119,"title_en":"Job 13–15","title_af":"Job 13–15","passages":[{"book_id":18,"chapter":13},{"book_id":18,"chapter":14},{"book_id":18,"chapter":15}],"commentary_intro_en":"You are reading through the whole Bible. Each chapter summary below helps you grasp the main story before you read the verses.","commentary_intro_af":"Jy lees deur die hele Bybel. Elke hoofstuk-opsomming hieronder help jou die hoofverhaal te begryp voordat jy die verse lees.","commentary_sections":[{"book_id":18,"chapter":13,"heading_en":"Book 18 13","heading_af":"Boek 18 13","summary_en":"Book 18 13. Wisdom literature for worship, prayer, and practical living. Apply its truths to your relationships, work, and inner life. Read Book 18 13 yourself and verify each st