 that the fear of the Lord is the beginning of wisdom (Proverbs 1:7). Compare how each psalm or proverb applies that foundation differently."}],"cross_references_af":[{"ref":"Psalms 89","comparison":"Compare with Psalms 89, wat direct voor hierdie hoofstuk kom — let op wat voortgaan of verander."},{"ref":"Spreuke 1:7","comparison":"Wysheidsboeke herhaal dat die vrees vir die Here die begin van wysheid is (Spr 1:7). Vergelyk hoe elke psalm of spreuk dit toepas."}],"highlights_en":["Pray the psalm back to God","Notice metaphors for God","Apply its emotion honestly"],"highlights_af":["Bid die psalm terug aan God","Let op metafore vir God","Pas die emosie eerlik toe"]}],"commentary_en":"You are reading through the whole Bible. Each chapter summary below helps you grasp the main story before you read the verses.\n\nPsalms 88\nPsalm 88 expresses worship, lament, or wisdom before God. Read it as prayer — many psalms foreshadow Christ and speak to every season of the soul. Read Psalms 88 yourself and verify each statement against the verses in your Bible version.\n\nPray the psalm back to God\nThe text of Psalms 88 records or illustrates: Pray the psalm back to God. Re-read those verses and note exactly what Scripture states.\n\nNotice metaphors for God\nThe text of Psalms 88 records or illustrates: Notice metaphors for God. Re-read those verses and note exactly what Scripture states.\n\nApply its emotion honestly\nThe text of Psalms 88 records or illustrates: Apply its emotion honestly. Re-read those verses and note exactly what Scripture states.\n\nWhat God wants us to know:\nGod wants us to know that true wisdom begins with reverence for him and shapes daily choices, speech, and worship.\n\nWhy:\nWisdom passages tie understanding to the fear of the Lord and practical living. Notice commands, prayers, or counsel in this chapter and what attitude toward God they assume.\n\nSimilar elsewhere:\nPsalms 87: Compare with Psalms 87, which immediately precedes this chapter in the same book — notice what events or themes continue or change.\nProverbs 1:7: Wisdom books often repeat the theme that the fear of the Lord is the beginning of wisdom (Proverbs 1:7). Compare how each psalm or proverb applies that foundation differently.\n\nPsalms 89\nPsalm 89 expresses worship, lament, or wisdom before God. Read it as prayer — many psalms foreshadow Christ and speak to every season of the soul. Read Psalms 89 yourself and verify each statement against the verses in your Bible version.\n\nPray the psalm back to God\nThe text of Psalms 89 records or illustrates: Pray the psalm back to God. Re-read those verses and note exactly what Scripture states.\n\nNotice metaphors for God\nThe text of Psalms 89 records or illustrates: Notice metaphors for God. Re-read those verses and note exactly what Scripture states.\n\nApply its emotion honestly\nThe text of Psalms 89 records or illustrates: Apply its emotion honestly. Re-read those verses and note exactly what Scripture states.\n\nWhat God wants us to know:\nGod wants us to know that true wisdom begins with reverence for him and shapes daily choices, speech, and worship.\n\nWhy:\nWisdom passages tie understanding to the fear of the Lord and practical living. Notice commands, prayers, or counsel in this chapter and what attitude toward God they assume.\n\nSimilar elsewhere:\nPsalms 88: Compare with Psalms 88, which immediately precedes this chapter in the same book — notice what events or themes continue or change.\nProverbs 1:7: Wisdom books often repeat the theme that the fear of the Lord is the beginning of wisdom (Proverbs 1:7). Compare how each psalm or proverb applies that foundation differently.\n\nPsalms 90\nPsalm 90 expresses worship, lament, or wisdom before God. Read it as prayer — many psalms foreshadow Christ and speak to every season of the soul. Read Psalms 90 yourself and verify each statement against the verses in your Bible version.\n\nPray the psalm back to God\nThe text of Psalms 90 records or illustrates: Pray the psalm back to God. Re-read those verses and note exactly what Scripture states.\n\nNotice metaphors for God\nThe text of Psalms 90 records or illustrates: Notice metaphors for God. Re-read those verses and note exactly what Scripture states.\n\nApply its emotion honestly\nThe text of Psalms 90 records or illustrates: Apply its emotion honestly. Re-read those verses and note exactly what Scripture states.\n\nWhat God wants us to know:\nGod wants us to know that true wisdom begins with reverence for him and shapes daily choices, speech, and worship.\n\nWhy:\nWisdom passages tie understanding to the fear of the Lord and practical living. Notice commands, prayers, or counsel in this chapter and what attitude toward God they assume.\n\nSimilar elsewhere:\nPsalms 89: Compare with Psalms 89, which immediately precedes this chapter in the same book — notice what events or themes continue or change.\nProverbs 1:7: Wisdom books often repeat the theme that the fear of the Lord is the beginning of wisdom (Proverbs 1:7). Compare how each psalm or proverb applies that foundation differently.","commentary_af":"Jy lees deur die hele Bybel. Elke hoofstuk-opsomming hieronder help jou die hoofverhaal te begryp voordat jy die verse lees.\n\nPsalms 88\nPsalm 88 druk aanbidding, klagte of wysheid voor God uit. Lees dit as gebed — baie psalms wys na Christus en spreek tot elke seisoen van die siel. Lees Psalms 88 self en kontroleer elke stelling teen die verse in jou Bybelweergawe.\n\nBid die psalm terug aan God\nDie teks van Psalms 88 noem of illustreer: Bid die psalm terug aan God. Lees daardie verse weer en skryf presies op wat die Bybel sê — nie wat jy dink nie.\n\nLet op metafore vir God\nDie teks van Psalms 88 noem of illustreer: Let op metafore vir God. Lees daardie verse weer en skryf presies op wat die Bybel sê — nie wat jy dink nie.\n\nPas die emosie eerlik toe\nDie teks van Psalms 88 noem of illustreer: Pas die emosie eerlik toe. Lees daardie verse weer en skryf presies op wat die Bybel sê — nie wat jy dink nie.\n\nWhat God wants us to know:\nGod wil hê ons moet weet dat ware wysheid begin met eerbied vir Hom en daaglikse keuses, spraak en aanbidding vorm.\n\nWhy:\nWysheid verbind insig met die vrees vir die Here. Let op gebooie, gebede of raad in hierdie hoofstuk en watter houding teenoor God dit veronderstel.\n\nSimilar elsewhere:\nPsalms 87: Compare with Psalms 87, wat direct voor hierdie hoofstuk kom — let op wat voortgaan of verander.\nSpreuke 1:7: Wysheidsboeke herhaal dat die vrees vir die Here die begin van wysheid is (Spr 1:7). Vergelyk hoe elke psalm of spreuk dit toepas.\n\nPsalms 89\nPsalm 89 druk aanbidding, klagte of wysheid voor God uit. Lees dit as gebed — baie psalms wys na Christus en spreek tot elke seisoen van die siel. Lees Psalms 89 self en kontroleer elke stelling teen die verse in jou Bybelweergawe.\n\nBid die psalm terug aan God\nDie teks van Psalms 89 noem of illustreer: Bid die psalm terug aan God. Lees daardie verse weer en skryf presies op wat die Bybel sê — nie wat jy dink nie.\n\nLet op metafore vir God\nDie teks van Psalms 89 noem of illustreer: Let op metafore vir God. Lees daardie verse weer en skryf presies op wat die Bybel sê — nie wat jy dink nie.\n\nPas die emosie eerlik toe\nDie teks van Psalms 89 noem of illustreer: Pas die emosie eerlik toe. Lees daardie verse weer en skryf presies op wat die Bybel sê — nie wat jy dink nie.\n\nWhat God wants us to know:\nGod wil hê ons moet weet dat ware wysheid begin met eerbied vir Hom en daaglikse keuses, spraak en aanbidding vorm.\n\nWhy:\nWysheid verbind insig met die vrees vir die Here. Let op gebooie, gebede of raad in hierdie hoofstuk en watter houding teenoor God dit veronderstel.\n\nSimilar elsewhere:\nPsalms 88: Compare with Psalms 88, wat direct voor hierdie hoofstuk kom — let op wat voortgaan of verander.\nSpreuke 1:7: Wysheidsboeke herhaal dat die vrees vir die Here die begin van wysheid is (Spr 1:7). Vergelyk hoe elke psalm of spreuk dit toepas.\n\nPsalms 90\nPsalm 90 druk aanbidding, klagte of wysheid voor God uit. Lees dit as gebed — baie psalms wys na Christus en spreek tot elke seisoen van die siel. Lees Psalms 90 self en kontroleer elke stelling teen die verse in jou Bybelweergawe.\n\nBid die psalm terug aan God\nDie teks van Psalms 90 noem of illustreer: Bid die psalm terug aan God. Lees daardie verse weer en skryf presies op wat die Bybel sê — nie wat jy dink nie.\n\nLet op metafore vir God\nDie teks van Psalms 90 noem of illustreer: Let op metafore vir God. Lees daardie verse weer en skryf presies op wat die Bybel sê — nie wat jy dink nie.\n\nPas die emosie eerlik toe\nDie teks van Psalms 90 noem of illustreer: Pas die emosie eerlik toe. Lees daardie verse weer en skryf presies op wat die Bybel sê — nie wat jy dink nie.\n\nWhat God wants us to know:\nGod wil hê ons moet weet dat ware wysheid begin met eerbied vir Hom en daaglikse keuses, spraak en aanbidding vorm.\n\nWhy:\nWysheid verbind insig met die vrees vir die Here. Let op gebooie, gebede of raad in hierdie hoofstuk en watter houding teenoor God dit veronderstel.\n\nSimilar elsewhere:\nPsalms 89: Compare with Psalms 89, wat direct voor hierdie hoofstuk kom — let op wat voortgaan of verander.\nSpreuke 1:7: Wysheidsboeke herhaal dat die vrees vir die Here die begin van wysheid is (Spr 1:7). Vergelyk hoe elke psalm of spreuk dit toepas.","questions_en":["What does this passage reveal about God?","What promise, command, or truth stands out to you?","How can you apply this to your life today?"],"questions_af":["Wat openbaar hierdie gedeelte oor God?","Watter belofte, gebod of waarheid val vir jou op?","Hoe kan jy dit vandag in jou lewe toepas?"]},{"day":159,"title_en":"Psalms 91–93","title_af":"Psalms 91–93","passages":[{"book_id":19,"chapter":91},{"book_id":19,"chapter":92},{"book_id":19,"chapter":93}],"commentary_intro_en":"You are reading through the whole Bible. Each chapter summary below helps you grasp the main story bef