nd note exactly what Scripture states.\n\nFear of the Lord as foundation\nThe text of Proverbs 19 records or illustrates: Fear of the Lord as foundation. Re-read those verses and note exactly what Scripture states.\n\nOne principle to practice today\nThe text of Proverbs 19 records or illustrates: One principle to practice today. Re-read those verses and note exactly what Scripture states.\n\nWhat God wants us to know:\nGod wants us to know that true wisdom begins with reverence for him and shapes daily choices, speech, and worship.\n\nWhy:\nWisdom passages tie understanding to the fear of the Lord and practical living. Notice commands, prayers, or counsel in this chapter and what attitude toward God they assume.\n\nSimilar elsewhere:\nBook 20 18: Compare with Book 20 18, which immediately precedes this chapter in the same book — notice what events or themes continue or change.\nProverbs 1:7: Wisdom books often repeat the theme that the fear of the Lord is the beginning of wisdom (Proverbs 1:7). Compare how each psalm or proverb applies that foundation differently.\n\nProverbs 20\nKings detest evil; honest weights; plans succeed with counsel. Read Proverbs 20 yourself and verify each statement against the verses in your Bible version.\n\nPractical wisdom for daily choices\nThe text of Proverbs 20 records or illustrates: Practical wisdom for daily choices. Re-read those verses and note exactly what Scripture states.\n\nFear of the Lord as foundation\nThe text of Proverbs 20 records or illustrates: Fear of the Lord as foundation. Re-read those verses and note exactly what Scripture states.\n\nOne principle to practice today\nThe text of Proverbs 20 records or illustrates: One principle to practice today. Re-read those verses and note exactly what Scripture states.\n\nWhat God wants us to know:\nGod wants us to know that true wisdom begins with reverence for him and shapes daily choices, speech, and worship.\n\nWhy:\nWisdom passages tie understanding to the fear of the Lord and practical living. Notice commands, prayers, or counsel in this chapter and what attitude toward God they assume.\n\nSimilar elsewhere:\nBook 20 19: Compare with Book 20 19, which immediately precedes this chapter in the same book — notice what events or themes continue or change.\nProverbs 1:7: Wisdom books often repeat the theme that the fear of the Lord is the beginning of wisdom (Proverbs 1:7). Compare how each psalm or proverb applies that foundation differently.\n\nProverbs 21\nThe Lord weighs hearts; better righteousness than sacrifice. Read Proverbs 21 yourself and verify each statement against the verses in your Bible version.\n\nPractical wisdom for daily choices\nThe text of Proverbs 21 records or illustrates: Practical wisdom for daily choices. Re-read those verses and note exactly what Scripture states.\n\nFear of the Lord as foundation\nThe text of Proverbs 21 records or illustrates: Fear of the Lord as foundation. Re-read those verses and note exactly what Scripture states.\n\nOne principle to practice today\nThe text of Proverbs 21 records or illustrates: One principle to practice today. Re-read those verses and note exactly what Scripture states.\n\nWhat God wants us to know:\nGod wants us to know that true wisdom begins with reverence for him and shapes daily choices, speech, and worship.\n\nWhy:\nWisdom passages tie understanding to the fear of the Lord and practical living. Notice commands, prayers, or counsel in this chapter and what attitude toward God they assume.\n\nSimilar elsewhere:\nBook 20 20: Compare with Book 20 20, which immediately precedes this chapter in the same book — notice what events or themes continue or change.\nProverbs 1:7: Wisdom books often repeat the theme that the fear of the Lord is the beginning of wisdom (Proverbs 1:7). Compare how each psalm or proverb applies that foundation differently.","commentary_af":"Jy lees deur die hele Bybel. Elke hoofstuk-opsomming hieronder help jou die hoofverhaal te begryp voordat jy die verse lees.\n\nSpreuke 19\nWyn bespot; lui hande bring armoede; disiplineer jou seun. Lees Spreuke 19 self en kontroleer elke stelling teen die verse in jou Bybelweergawe.\n\nPraktiese wysheid vir daaglikse keuses\nDie teks van Spreuke 19 noem of illustreer: Praktiese wysheid vir daaglikse keuses. Lees daardie verse weer en skryf presies op wat die Bybel sê — nie wat jy dink nie.\n\nVrees vir die Here as fondament\nDie teks van Spreuke 19 noem of illustreer: Vrees vir die Here as fondament. Lees daardie verse weer en skryf presies op wat die Bybel sê — nie wat jy dink nie.\n\nEen beginsel om vandag te oefen\nDie teks van Spreuke 19 noem of illustreer: Een beginsel om vandag te oefen. Lees daardie verse weer en skryf presies op wat die Bybel sê — nie wat jy dink nie.\n\nWhat God wants us to know:\nGod wil hê ons moet weet dat ware wysheid begin met eerbied vir Hom en daaglikse keuses, spraak en aanbidding vorm.\n\nWhy:\nWysheid verbind insig met die vrees vir die Here. Let op gebooie, gebede of raad in hierdie hoofstuk en watter houding teenoor God dit veronderstel.\n\nSimilar elsewhere:\nBook 20 18: Compare with Book 20 18, wat direct voor hierdie hoofstuk kom — let op wat voortgaan of verander.\nSpreuke 1:7: Wysheidsboeke herhaal dat die vrees vir die Here die begin van wysheid is (Spr 1:7). Vergelyk hoe elke psalm of spreuk dit toepas.\n\nSpreuke 20\nKonings verfoei kwaad; eerlike gewigte; planne slaag met raad. Lees Spreuke 20 self en kontroleer elke stelling teen die verse in jou Bybelweergawe.\n\nPraktiese wysheid vir daaglikse keuses\nDie teks van Spreuke 20 noem of illustreer: Praktiese wysheid vir daaglikse keuses. Lees daardie verse weer en skryf presies op wat die Bybel sê — nie wat jy dink nie.\n\nVrees vir die Here as fondament\nDie teks van Spreuke 20 noem of illustreer: Vrees vir die Here as fondament. Lees daardie verse weer en skryf presies op wat die Bybel sê — nie wat jy dink nie.\n\nEen beginsel om vandag te oefen\nDie teks van Spreuke 20 noem of illustreer: Een beginsel om vandag te oefen. Lees daardie verse weer en skryf presies op wat die Bybel sê — nie wat jy dink nie.\n\nWhat God wants us to know:\nGod wil hê ons moet weet dat ware wysheid begin met eerbied vir Hom en daaglikse keuses, spraak en aanbidding vorm.\n\nWhy:\nWysheid verbind insig met die vrees vir die Here. Let op gebooie, gebede of raad in hierdie hoofstuk en watter houding teenoor God dit veronderstel.\n\nSimilar elsewhere:\nBook 20 19: Compare with Book 20 19, wat direct voor hierdie hoofstuk kom — let op wat voortgaan of verander.\nSpreuke 1:7: Wysheidsboeke herhaal dat die vrees vir die Here die begin van wysheid is (Spr 1:7). Vergelyk hoe elke psalm of spreuk dit toepas.\n\nSpreuke 21\nDie Here weeg harte; beter geregtigheid as offer. Lees Spreuke 21 self en kontroleer elke stelling teen die verse in jou Bybelweergawe.\n\nPraktiese wysheid vir daaglikse keuses\nDie teks van Spreuke 21 noem of illustreer: Praktiese wysheid vir daaglikse keuses. Lees daardie verse weer en skryf presies op wat die Bybel sê — nie wat jy dink nie.\n\nVrees vir die Here as fondament\nDie teks van Spreuke 21 noem of illustreer: Vrees vir die Here as fondament. Lees daardie verse weer en skryf presies op wat die Bybel sê — nie wat jy dink nie.\n\nEen beginsel om vandag te oefen\nDie teks van Spreuke 21 noem of illustreer: Een beginsel om vandag te oefen. Lees daardie verse weer en skryf presies op wat die Bybel sê — nie wat jy dink nie.\n\nWhat God wants us to know:\nGod wil hê ons moet weet dat ware wysheid begin met eerbied vir Hom en daaglikse keuses, spraak en aanbidding vorm.\n\nWhy:\nWysheid verbind insig met die vrees vir die Here. Let op gebooie, gebede of raad in hierdie hoofstuk en watter houding teenoor God dit veronderstel.\n\nSimilar elsewhere:\nBook 20 20: Compare with Book 20 20, wat direct voor hierdie hoofstuk kom — let op wat voortgaan of verander.\nSpreuke 1:7: Wysheidsboeke herhaal dat die vrees vir die Here die begin van wysheid is (Spr 1:7). Vergelyk hoe elke psalm of spreuk dit toepas.","questions_en":["What does this passage reveal about God?","What promise, command, or truth stands out to you?","How can you apply this to your life today?"],"questions_af":["Wat openbaar hierdie gedeelte oor God?","Watter belofte, gebod of waarheid val vir jou op?","Hoe kan jy dit vandag in jou lewe toepas?"]},{"day":186,"title_en":"Proverbs 22–24","title_af":"Spreuke 22–24","passages":[{"book_id":20,"chapter":22},{"book_id":20,"chapter":23},{"book_id":20,"chapter":24}],"commentary_intro_en":"You are reading through the whole Bible. Each chapter summary below helps you grasp the main story before you read the verses.","commentary_intro_af":"Jy lees deur die hele Bybel. Elke hoofstuk-opsomming hieronder help jou die hoofverhaal te begryp voordat jy die verse lees.","commentary_sections":[{"book_id":20,"chapter":22,"heading_en":"Proverbs 22","heading_af":"Spreuke 22","summary_en":"Train a child in the way; lazy borrow; generous blessed. Read Proverbs 22 yourself and verify each statement against the verses in your Bible version.","summary_af":"Lei ''n kind op die pad; lui leen; gulle geseën. Lees Spreuke 22 self en kontroleer elke stelling teen die verse in jou Bybelweergawe.","study_points_en":[{"title":"Practical wisdom for daily choices","verses":"","detail":"The text of Proverbs 22 records or illustrates: Practical wisdom for daily choices. Re-read those verses and note exactly what Scripture states."},{"title":"Fear of the Lord as foundation","verses":"","detail":"The text of Proverbs 22 records or illustrates: Fear of the Lord as foundation. Re-read those verses and note exactly what Scripture states."},{"title":"One principle to practice today","verses":"","detail":"The text of Proverbs 22 records or illustrates: One principle to practice today. Re-read those verses and note exactly what Scripture states."}],"study_points_af":[{"title":"Praktiese wysheid vir daaglikse keuses","verses":"","detail":"