ope for the future"],"highlights_af":["Sonde en berou","God se heilige standaarde","Hoop vir die toekoms"]}],"commentary_en":"You are reading through the whole Bible. Each chapter summary below helps you grasp the main story before you read the verses.\n\nBook 26 1\nBook 26 1. Prophetic word calling God''s people to covenant faithfulness. Listen for judgment, hope, and promises pointing to Messiah and restoration. Read Book 26 1 yourself and verify each statement against the verses in your Bible version.\n\nSin and repentance\nThe text of Book 26 1 records or illustrates: Sin and repentance. Re-read those verses and note exactly what Scripture states.\n\nGod''s holy standards\nThe text of Book 26 1 records or illustrates: God''s holy standards. Re-read those verses and note exactly what Scripture states.\n\nHope for the future\nThe text of Book 26 1 records or illustrates: Hope for the future. Re-read those verses and note exactly what Scripture states.\n\nWhat God wants us to know:\nGod wants his people to know that he calls them back to faithfulness, warns of judgment, and often pairs correction with hope.\n\nWhy:\nProphetic chapters usually contain God''s speech—accusation, command, or promise. Identify what God says he will do and what he asks his people to do.\n\nBook 26 2\nBook 26 2. Prophetic word calling God''s people to covenant faithfulness. Listen for judgment, hope, and promises pointing to Messiah and restoration. Read Book 26 2 yourself and verify each statement against the verses in your Bible version.\n\nSin and repentance\nThe text of Book 26 2 records or illustrates: Sin and repentance. Re-read those verses and note exactly what Scripture states.\n\nGod''s holy standards\nThe text of Book 26 2 records or illustrates: God''s holy standards. Re-read those verses and note exactly what Scripture states.\n\nHope for the future\nThe text of Book 26 2 records or illustrates: Hope for the future. Re-read those verses and note exactly what Scripture states.\n\nWhat God wants us to know:\nGod wants his people to know that he calls them back to faithfulness, warns of judgment, and often pairs correction with hope.\n\nWhy:\nProphetic chapters usually contain God''s speech—accusation, command, or promise. Identify what God says he will do and what he asks his people to do.\n\nSimilar elsewhere:\nBook 26 1: Compare with Book 26 1, which immediately precedes this chapter in the same book — notice what events or themes continue or change.\n\nBook 26 3\nBook 26 3. Prophetic word calling God''s people to covenant faithfulness. Listen for judgment, hope, and promises pointing to Messiah and restoration. Read Book 26 3 yourself and verify each statement against the verses in your Bible version.\n\nSin and repentance\nThe text of Book 26 3 records or illustrates: Sin and repentance. Re-read those verses and note exactly what Scripture states.\n\nGod''s holy standards\nThe text of Book 26 3 records or illustrates: God''s holy standards. Re-read those verses and note exactly what Scripture states.\n\nHope for the future\nThe text of Book 26 3 records or illustrates: Hope for the future. Re-read those verses and note exactly what Scripture states.\n\nWhat God wants us to know:\nGod wants his people to know that he calls them back to faithfulness, warns of judgment, and often pairs correction with hope.\n\nWhy:\nProphetic chapters usually contain God''s speech—accusation, command, or promise. Identify what God says he will do and what he asks his people to do.\n\nSimilar elsewhere:\nBook 26 2: Compare with Book 26 2, which immediately precedes this chapter in the same book — notice what events or themes continue or change.","commentary_af":"Jy lees deur die hele Bybel. Elke hoofstuk-opsomming hieronder help jou die hoofverhaal te begryp voordat jy die verse lees.\n\nBoek 26 1\nBoek 26 1. Profetiese woord wat God se volk roep tot verbondstrousheid. Luister vir vonnis, hoop en beloftes wat wys na Messias en herstel. Lees Boek 26 1 self