 continue or change."}],"cross_references_af":[{"ref":"Book 44 1","comparison":"Compare with Book 44 1, wat direct voor hierdie hoofstuk kom — let op wat voortgaan of verander."}],"highlights_en":["Spirit like tongues of fire","Peter''s sermon — crucified and risen","Repent and be baptized"],"highlights_af":["Gees soos vuurtong","Petrus se preek — gekruisig en opgestaan","Bekeer en doop"]},{"book_id":44,"chapter":3,"heading_en":"Acts 3","heading_af":"Handeling 3","summary_en":"Acts 3. The Spirit-empowered spread of the Gospel. Notice courage, community life, prayer, and how the church responds to persecution. Read Acts 3 yourself and verify each statement against the verses in your Bible version.","summary_af":"Handeling 3. Die Gees-bemagtigde verspreiding van die Evangelie. Let op moed, gemeenskaplewe, gebed en hoe die kerk op vervolging reageer. Lees Handeling 3 self en kontroleer elke stelling teen die verse in jou Bybelweergawe.","study_points_en":[{"title":"Holy Spirit''s power","verses":"","detail":"The text of Acts 3 records or illustrates: Holy Spirit''s power. Re-read those verses and note exactly what Scripture states."},{"title":"Bold witness","verses":"","detail":"The text of Acts 3 records or illustrates: Bold witness. Re-read those verses and note exactly what Scripture states."},{"title":"Growing community","verses":"","detail":"The text of Acts 3 records or illustrates: Growing community. Re-read those verses and note exactly what Scripture states."}],"study_points_af":[{"title":"Heilige Gees se krag","verses":"","detail":"Die teks van Handeling 3 noem of illustreer: Heilige Gees se krag. Lees daardie verse weer en skryf presies op wat die Bybel sê — nie wat jy dink nie."},{"title":"Dapper getuienis","verses":"","detail":"Die teks van Handeling 3 noem of illustreer: Dapper getuienis. Lees daardie verse weer en skryf presies op wat die Bybel sê — nie wat jy dink nie."},{"title":"Groeiende gemeenskap","verses":"","detail":"Die teks van Handeling 3 noem of illustreer: Groeiende gemeenskap. Lees daardie verse weer en skryf presies op wat die Bybel sê — nie wat jy dink nie."}],"teaching_en":"God wants us to know that the risen Christ continues his work through the Spirit, the apostles, and the growing church.","teaching_why_en":"Acts records preaching, conversions, miracles, and persecution. Notice how the Spirit empowers witness and how the church responds in this chapter.","teaching_af":"God wil hê ons moet weet dat die opgestane Christus voortwerk deur die Gees, die apostels en die groeiende kerk.","teaching_why_af":"Handeling beskryf preek, bekering, wonderwerke en vervolging. Let hoe die Gees getuienis bemagtig en hoe die kerk reageer.","cross_references_en":[{"ref":"Book 44 2","comparison":"Compare with Book 44 2, which immediately precedes this chapter in the same book — notice what events or themes continue or change."}],"cross_references_af":[{"ref":"Book 44 2","comparison":"Compare with Book 44 2, wat direct voor hierdie hoofstuk kom — let op wat voortgaan of verander."}],"highlights_en":["Holy Spirit''s power","Bold witness","Growing community"],"highlights_af":["Heilige Gees se krag","Dapper getuienis","Groeiende gemeenskap"]}],"commentary_en":"You are reading through the whole Bible. Each chapter summary below helps you grasp the main story before you read the verses.\n\nActs 1\nActs 1. The Spirit-empowered spread of the Gospel. Notice courage, community life, prayer, and how the church responds to persecution. Read Acts 1 yourself and verify each statement against the verses in your Bible version.\n\nHoly Spirit''s power\nThe text of Acts 1 records or illustrates: Holy Spirit''s power. Re-read those verses and note exactly what Scripture states.\n\nBold witness\nThe text of Acts 1 records or illustrates: Bold witness. Re-read those verses and note exactly what Scripture states.\n\nGrowing community\nThe text of Acts 1 records or illustrates: Growing community. Re-read those verses and note exactly what Scripture states.\n\nWhat God wants us to know:\nGod wants us to know that the risen Christ continues his work through the Spirit, the apostles, and the growing church.\n\nWhy:\nActs records preaching, conversions, miracles, and persecution. Notice how the Spirit empowers witness and how the church responds in this chapter.\n\nActs 2\nPentecost — Holy Spirit fills believers; Peter preaches; three thousand saved. The church is born in power. Read Acts 2 yourself and verify each statement against the verses in your Bible version.\n\nSpirit like tongues of fire\nThe text of Acts 2 records or illustrates: Spirit like tongues of fire. Re-read those verses and note exactly what Scripture states.\n\nPeter''s sermon — crucified and risen\nThe text of Acts 2 records or illustrates: Peter''s sermon — crucified and risen. Re-read those verses and note exactly what Scripture states.\n\nRepent and be baptized\nThe text of Acts 2 records or illustrates: Repent and be baptized. Re-read those verses and note exactly what Scripture states.\n\nWhat God wants us to know:\nGod wants us to know that the risen Christ continues his work through the Spirit, the apostles, and the growing church.\n\nWhy:\nActs records preaching, conversions, miracles, and persecution. Notice how the Spirit empowers witness and how the church responds in this chapter.\n\nSimilar elsewhere:\nBook 44 1: Compare with Book 44 1, which immediately precedes this chapter in the same book — notice what events or themes continue or change.\n\nActs 3\nActs 3. The Spirit-empowered spread of the Gospel. Notice courage, community life, prayer, and how the church responds to persecution. Read Acts 3 yourself and verify each statement against the verses in your Bible version.\n\nHoly Spirit''s power\nThe text of Acts 3 records or illustrates: Holy Spirit''s power. Re-read those verses and note exactly what Scripture states.\n\nBold witness\nThe text of Acts 3 records or illustrates: Bold witness. Re-read those verses and note exactly what Scripture states.\n\nGrowing community\nThe text of Acts 3 records or illustrates: Growing community. Re-read those verses and note exactly what Scripture states.\n\nWhat God wants us to know:\nGod wants us to know that the risen Christ continues his work through the Spirit, the apostles, and the growing church.\n\nWhy:\nActs records preaching, conversions, miracles, and persecution. Notice how the Spirit empowers witness and how the church responds in this chapter.\n\nSimilar elsewhere:\nBook 44 2: Compare with Book 44 2, which immediately precedes this chapter in the same book — notice what events or themes continue or change.","commentary_af":"Jy lees deur die hele Bybel. Elke hoofstuk-opsomming hieronder help jou die hoofverhaal te begryp voordat jy die verse lees.\n\nHandeling 1\nHandeling 1. Die Gees-bemagtigde verspreiding van die Evangelie. Let op moed, gemeenskaplewe, gebed en hoe die kerk op vervolging reageer. Lees Handeling 1 self en kontroleer elke stelling teen die verse in jou Bybelweergawe.\n\nHeilige Gees se krag\nDie teks van Handeling 1 noem of illustreer: Heilige Gees se krag. Lees daardie verse weer en skryf presies op wat die Bybel sê — nie wat jy dink nie.\n\nDapper getuienis\nDie teks van Handeling 1 noem of illustreer: Dapper getuienis. Lees daardie verse weer en skryf presies op wat die Bybel sê — nie wat jy dink nie.\n\nGroeiende gemeenskap\nDie teks van Handeling 1 noem of illustreer: Groeiende gemeenskap. Lees daardie verse weer en skryf presies op wat die Bybel sê — nie wat jy dink nie.\n\nWhat God wants us to know:\nGod wil hê ons moet weet dat die opgestane Christus voortwerk deur die Gees, die apostels en die groeiende kerk.\n\nWhy:\nHandeling beskryf preek, bekering, wonderwerke en vervolging. Let hoe die Gees getuienis bemagtig en hoe die kerk reageer.\n\nHandeling 2\nPinkster — Heilige Gees vul gelowiges; Petrus preek; drieduisend gered. Die kerk word in krag gebore. Lees Handeling 2 self en kontroleer elke stelling teen die verse in jou Bybelweergawe.\n\nGees soos vuurtong\nDie teks van Handeling 2 noem of illustreer: Gees soos vuurtong. Lees daardie verse weer en skryf presies op wat die Bybel sê — nie wat jy dink nie.\n\nPetrus se preek — gekruisig en opgestaan\nDie teks van Handeling 2 noem of illustreer: Petrus se preek — gekruisig en opgestaan. Lees daardie verse weer en skryf presies op wat die Bybel sê — nie wat jy dink nie.\n\nBekeer en doop\nDie teks van Handeling 2 noem of illustreer: Bekeer en doop. Lees daardie verse weer en skryf presies op wat die Bybel sê — nie wat jy dink nie.\n\nWhat God wants us to know:\nGod wil hê ons moet weet dat die opgestane Christus voortwerk deur die Gees, die apostels en die groeiende kerk.\n\nWhy:\nHandeling beskryf preek, bekering, wonderwerke en vervolging. Let hoe die Gees getuienis bemagtig en hoe die kerk reageer.\n\nSimilar elsewhere:\nBook 44 1: Compare with Book 44 1, wat direct voor hierdie hoofstuk kom — let op wat voortgaan of verander.\n\nHandeling 3\nHandeling 3. Die Gees-bemagtigde verspreiding van die Evangelie. Let op moed, gemeenskaplewe, gebed en hoe die kerk op vervolging reageer. Lees Handeling 3 self en kontroleer elke stelling teen die verse in jou Bybelweergawe.\n\nHeilige Gees se krag\nDie teks van Handeling 3 noem of illustreer: Heilige Gees se krag. Lees daardie verse weer en skryf presies op wat die Bybel sê — nie wat jy dink nie.\n\nDapper getuienis\nDie teks van Handeling 3 noem of illustreer: Dapper getuienis. Lees daardie verse weer en skryf presies op wat die Bybel sê — nie wat jy dink nie.\n\nGroeiende gemeenskap\nDie teks van Handeling 3 noem of illustreer: Groeiende gemeenskap. Lees daardie verse weer en skryf presies op wat die Bybel sê — nie wat jy dink nie.\n\nWhat God wants us to know:\nGod wil hê ons moet weet dat die opgestane Christus voortwerk deur die Gees, die apostels en die groeiende kerk.\n\nWhy:\nHandeling beskryf preek, bekering, wonderwerke en vervolging. Let hoe die Gees getuien