n\nActs 7\nActs 7. The Spirit-empowered spread of the Gospel. Notice courage, community life, prayer, and how the church responds to persecution. Read Acts 7 yourself and verify each statement against the verses in your Bible version.\n\nHoly Spirit''s power\nThe text of Acts 7 records or illustrates: Holy Spirit''s power. Re-read those verses and note exactly what Scripture states.\n\nBold witness\nThe text of Acts 7 records or illustrates: Bold witness. Re-read those verses and note exactly what Scripture states.\n\nGrowing community\nThe text of Acts 7 records or illustrates: Growing community. Re-read those verses and note exactly what Scripture states.\n\nWhat God wants us to know:\nGod wants us to know that the risen Christ continues his work through the Spirit, the apostles, and the growing church.\n\nWhy:\nActs records preaching, conversions, miracles, and persecution. Notice how the Spirit empowers witness and how the church responds in this chapter.\n\nSimilar elsewhere:\nBook 44 6: Compare with Book 44 6, which immediately precedes this chapter in the same book — notice what events or themes continue or change.\n\nActs 8\nActs 8. The Spirit-empowered spread of the Gospel. Notice courage, community life, prayer, and how the church responds to persecution. Read Acts 8 yourself and verify each statement against the verses in your Bible version.\n\nHoly Spirit''s power\nThe text of Acts 8 records or illustrates: Holy Spirit''s power. Re-read those verses and note exactly what Scripture states.\n\nBold witness\nThe text of Acts 8 records or illustrates: Bold witness. Re-read those verses and note exactly what Scripture states.\n\nGrowing community\nThe text of Acts 8 records or illustrates: Growing community. Re-read those verses and note exactly what Scripture states.\n\nWhat God wants us to know:\nGod wants us to know that the risen Christ continues his work through the Spirit, the apostles, and the growing church.\n\nWhy:\nActs records preaching, conversions, miracles, and persecution. Notice how the Spirit empowers witness and how the church responds in this chapter.\n\nSimilar elsewhere:\nBook 44 7: Compare with Book 44 7, which immediately precedes this chapter in the same book — notice what events or themes continue or change.\n\nActs 9\nActs 9. The Spirit-empowered spread of the Gospel. Notice courage, community life, prayer, and how the church responds to persecution. Read Acts 9 yourself and verify each statement against the verses in your Bible version.\n\nHoly Spirit''s power\nThe text of Acts 9 records or illustrates: Holy Spirit''s power. Re-read those verses and note exactly what Scripture states.\n\nBold witness\nThe text of Acts 9 records or illustrates: Bold witness. Re-read those verses and note exactly what Scripture states.\n\nGrowing community\nThe text of Acts 9 records or illustrates: Growing community. Re-read those verses and note exactly what Scripture states.\n\nWhat God wants us to know:\nGod wants us to know that the risen Christ continues his work through the Spirit, the apostles, and the growing church.\n\nWhy:\nActs records preaching, conversions, miracles, and persecution. Notice how the Spirit empowers witness and how the church responds in this chapter.\n\nSimilar elsewhere:\nBook 44 8: Compare with Book 44 8, which immediately precedes this chapter in the same book — notice what events or themes continue or change.","commentary_af":"Jy lees deur die hele Bybel. Elke hoofstuk-opsomming hieronder help jou die hoofverhaal te begryp voordat jy die verse lees.\n\nHandeling 7\nHandeling 7. Die Gees-bemagtigde verspreiding van die Evangelie. Let op moed, gemeenskaplewe, gebed en hoe die kerk op vervolging reageer. Lees Handeling 7 self en kontroleer elke stelling teen die verse in jou Bybelweergawe.\n\nHeilige Gees se krag\nDie teks van Handeling 7 noem of illustreer: Heilige Gees se krag. Lees daardie verse weer en skryf presies op wat die Bybel sê — nie wat jy dink nie.\n\nDapper getuienis\nDie teks van Handeling 7 noem of illustreer: Dapper getuienis. Lees daardie verse weer en skryf presies op wat die Bybel sê — nie wat jy dink nie.\n\nGroeiende gemeenskap\nDie teks van Handeling 7 noem of illustreer: Groeiende gemeenskap. Lees daardie verse weer en skryf presies op wat die Bybel sê — nie wat jy dink nie.\n\nWhat God wants us to know:\nGod wil hê ons moet weet dat die opgestane Christus voortwerk deur die Gees, die apostels en die groeiende kerk.\n\nWhy:\nHandeling beskryf preek, bekering, wonderwerke en vervolging. Let hoe die Gees getuienis bemagtig en hoe die kerk reageer.\n\nSimilar elsewhere:\nBook 44 6: Compare with Book 44 6, wat direct voor hierdie hoofstuk kom — let op wat voortgaan of verander.\n\nHandeling 8\nHandeling 8. Die Gees-bemagtigde verspreiding van die Evangelie. Let op moed, gemeenskaplewe, gebed en hoe die kerk op vervolging reageer. Lees Handeling 8 self en kontroleer elke stelling teen die verse in jou Bybelweergawe.\n\nHeilige Gees se krag\nDie teks van Handeling 8 noem of illustreer: Heilige Gees se krag. Lees daardie verse weer en skryf presies op wat die Bybel sê — nie wat jy dink nie.\n\nDapper getuienis\nDie teks van Handeling 8 noem of illustreer: Dapper getuienis. Lees daardie verse weer en skryf presies op wat die Bybel sê — nie wat jy dink nie.\n\nGroeiende gemeenskap\nDie teks van Handeling 8 noem of illustreer: Groeiende gemeenskap. Lees daardie verse weer en skryf presies op wat die Bybel sê — nie wat jy dink nie.\n\nWhat God wants us to know:\nGod wil hê ons moet weet dat die opgestane Christus voortwerk deur die Gees, die apostels en die groeiende kerk.\n\nWhy:\nHandeling beskryf preek, bekering, wonderwerke en vervolging. Let hoe die Gees getuienis bemagtig en hoe die kerk reageer.\n\nSimilar elsewhere:\nBook 44 7: Compare with Book 44 7, wat direct voor hierdie hoofstuk kom — let op wat voortgaan of verander.\n\nHandeling 9\nHandeling 9. Die Gees-bemagtigde verspreiding van die Evangelie. Let op moed, gemee