tes.\n\nBold witness\nThe text of Acts 16 records or illustrates: Bold witness. Re-read those verses and note exactly what Scripture states.\n\nGrowing community\nThe text of Acts 16 records or illustrates: Growing community. Re-read those verses and note exactly what Scripture states.\n\nWhat God wants us to know:\nGod wants us to know that the risen Christ continues his work through the Spirit, the apostles, and the growing church.\n\nWhy:\nActs records preaching, conversions, miracles, and persecution. Notice how the Spirit empowers witness and how the church responds in this chapter.\n\nSimilar elsewhere:\nBook 44 15: Compare with Book 44 15, which immediately precedes this chapter in the same book — notice what events or themes continue or change.\n\nActs 17\nActs 17. The Spirit-empowered spread of the Gospel. Notice courage, community life, prayer, and how the church responds to persecution. Read Acts 17 yourself and verify each statement against the verses in your Bible version.\n\nHoly Spirit''s power\nThe text of Acts 17 records or illustrates: Holy Spirit''s power. Re-read those verses and note exactly what Scripture states.\n\nBold witness\nThe text of Acts 17 records or illustrates: Bold witness. Re-read those verses and note exactly what Scripture states.\n\nGrowing community\nThe text of Acts 17 records or illustrates: Growing community. Re-read those verses and note exactly what Scripture states.\n\nWhat God wants us to know:\nGod wants us to know that the risen Christ continues his work through the Spirit, the apostles, and the growing church.\n\nWhy:\nActs records preaching, conversions, miracles, and persecution. Notice how the Spirit empowers witness and how the church responds in this chapter.\n\nSimilar elsewhere:\nBook 44 16: Compare with Book 44 16, which immediately precedes this chapter in the same book — notice what events or themes continue or change.\n\nActs 18\nActs 18. The Spirit-empowered spread of the Gospel. Notice courage, community life, prayer, and how the church responds to persecution. Read Acts 18 yourself and verify each statement against the verses in your Bible version.\n\nHoly Spirit''s power\nThe text of Acts 18 records or illustrates: Holy Spirit''s power. Re-read those verses and note exactly what Scripture states.\n\nBold witness\nThe text of Acts 18 records or illustrates: Bold witness. Re-read those verses and note exactly what Scripture states.\n\nGrowing community\nThe text of Acts 18 records or illustrates: Growing community. Re-read those verses and note exactly what Scripture states.\n\nWhat God wants us to know:\nGod wants us to know that the risen Christ continues his work through the Spirit, the apostles, and the growing church.\n\nWhy:\nActs records preaching, conversions, miracles, and persecution. Notice how the Spirit empowers witness and how the church responds in this chapter.\n\nSimilar elsewhere:\nBook 44 17: Compare with Book 44 17, which immediately precedes this chapter in the same book — notice what events or themes continue or change.","commentary_af":"Jy lees deur die hele Bybel. Elke hoofstuk-opsomming hieronder help jou die hoofverhaal te begryp voordat jy die verse lees.\n\nHandeling 16\nHandeling 16. Die Gees-bemagtigde verspreiding van die Evangelie. Let op moed, gemeenskaplewe, gebed en hoe die kerk op vervolging reageer. Lees Handeling 16 self en kontroleer elke stelling teen die verse in jou Bybelweergawe.\n\nHeilige Gees se krag\nDie teks van Handeling 16 noem of illustreer: Heilige Gees se krag. Lees daardie verse weer en skryf presies op wat die Bybel sê — nie wat jy dink nie.\n\nDapper getuienis\nDie teks van Handeling 16 noem of illustreer: Dapper getuienis. Lees daardie verse weer en skryf presies op wat die Bybel sê — nie wat jy dink nie.\n\nGroeiende gemeenskap\nDie teks van Handeling 16 noem of illustreer: Groeiende gemeenskap. Lees daardie verse weer en skryf presies op wat die Bybel sê — nie wat jy dink nie.\n\nWhat God wants us to know:\