pirit''s power. Re-read those verses and note exactly what Scripture states.\n\nBold witness\nThe text of Acts 28 records or illustrates: Bold witness. Re-read those verses and note exactly what Scripture states.\n\nGrowing community\nThe text of Acts 28 records or illustrates: Growing community. Re-read those verses and note exactly what Scripture states.\n\nWhat God wants us to know:\nGod wants us to know that the risen Christ continues his work through the Spirit, the apostles, and the growing church.\n\nWhy:\nActs records preaching, conversions, miracles, and persecution. Notice how the Spirit empowers witness and how the church responds in this chapter.\n\nSimilar elsewhere:\nBook 44 27: Compare with Book 44 27, which immediately precedes this chapter in the same book — notice what events or themes continue or change.\n\nRomans 1\nPaul introduces the gospel as God''s power for salvation. Humanity''s universal sin; righteousness revealed apart from law. Read Romans 1 yourself and verify each statement against the verses in your Bible version.\n\nThe gospel is God''s power\nThe text of Romans 1 records or illustrates: The gospel is God''s power. Re-read those verses and note exactly what Scripture states.\n\nNone righteous, no not one\nThe text of Romans 1 records or illustrates: None righteous, no not one. Re-read those verses and note exactly what Scripture states.\n\nRighteousness through faith\nThe text of Romans 1 records or illustrates: Righteousness through faith. Re-read those verses and note exactly what Scripture states.\n\nWhat God wants us to know:\nGod wants believers to know gospel truth and how it should shape church life, holiness, and love for others.\n\nWhy:\nPaul''s letters argue from what Christ has done to how Christians should live. Find the doctrinal statement in this chapter and the conduct it connects to.\n\nRomans 2\nRomans 2. Paul teaches doctrine and Christian living. Connect theological truth to practical obedience in church, family, and daily relationships. Read Romans 2 yourself and verify each statement against the verses in your Bible version.\n\nGospel truth\nThe text of Romans 2 records or illustrates: Gospel truth. Re-read those verses and note exactly what Scripture states.\n\nLife in the Spirit\nThe text of Romans 2 records or illustrates: Life in the Spirit. Re-read those verses and note exactly what Scripture states.\n\nPractical ethics\nThe text of Romans 2 records or illustrates: Practical ethics. Re-read those verses and note exactly what Scripture states.\n\nWhat God wants us to know:\nGod wants believers to know gospel truth and how it should shape church life, holiness, and love for others.\n\nWhy:\nPaul''s letters argue from what Christ has done to how Christians should live. Find the doctrinal statement in this chapter and the conduct it connects to.\n\nSimilar elsewhere:\nRomans 1: Compare with Romans 1, which immediately precedes this chapter in the same book — notice what events or themes continue or change.","commentary_af":"Jy lees deur die hele Bybel. Elke hoofstuk-opsomming hieronder help jou die hoofverhaal te begryp voordat jy die verse lees.\n\nHandeling 28\nHandeling 28. Die Gees-bemagtigde verspreiding van die Evangelie. Let op moed, gemeenskaplewe, gebed en hoe die kerk op vervolging reageer. Lees Handeling 28 self en kontroleer elke stelling teen die verse in jou Bybelweergawe.\n\nHeilige Gees se krag\nDie teks van Handeling 28 noem of illustreer: Heilige Gees se krag. Lees daardie verse weer en skryf presies op wat die Bybel sê — nie wat jy dink nie.\n\nDapper getuienis\nDie teks van Handeling 28 noem of illustreer: Dapper getuienis. Lees daardie verse weer en skryf presies op wat die Bybel sê — nie wat jy dink nie.\n\nGroeiende gemeenskap\nDie teks van Handeling 28 noem of illustreer: Groeiende gemeenskap. Lees daardie verse weer en skryf presies op wat die Bybel sê — nie wat jy dink nie.\n\nWhat God wants us to know:\nGod wil hê ons moet weet dat die opgestane Christus voortwerk deur die Gees, die apostels en die groeiende kerk.\n\nWhy:\nHandeling beskryf preek, bekering, wonderwerke en vervolging. Let hoe die Gees getuienis bemagtig en hoe die kerk reageer.\n\nSimilar elsewhere:\nBook 44 27: Compare with Book 44 27, wat direct voor hierdie hoofstuk kom — let op wat voortgaan of verander.\n\nRomeine 1\nPaul stel die evangelie voor as God se krag vir redding. Mensdom se universele sonde; geregtigheid openbaar buite die wet. Lees Romeine 1 self en kontroleer elke stelling teen die verse in jou Bybelweergawe.\n\nDie evangelie is God se krag\nDie teks van Romeine 1 noem of illustreer: Die evangelie is God se krag. Lees daardie verse weer en skryf presies op wat die Bybel sê — nie wat jy dink nie.\n\nGeen regverdiges, selfs nie een nie\nDie teks van Romeine 1 noem of illustreer: Geen regverdiges, selfs nie een nie. Lees daardie verse weer en skryf presies op wat die Bybel sê — nie wat jy dink nie.\n\nGeregtigheid deur geloof\nDie teks van Romeine 1 noem of illustreer: Geregtigheid deur geloof. Lees daardie verse weer en skryf presies op wat die Bybel sê — nie wat jy dink nie.\n\nWhat God wants us to know:\nGod wil gelowiges laat weet evangelie-waarheid en hoe dit kerklewe, heiligheid en liefde moet vorm.\n\nWhy:\nPaulus redeneer van wat Christus gedoen het na hoe Christene moet leef. Soek die leerstelling in hierdie hoofstuk en die lewe wat dit verbind.\n\nRomeine 2\nRomeine 2. Paulus leer leerstelling en Christelike lewe. Verbind teologiese waarheid met praktiese gehoorsaamheid in kerk, gesin en daaglikse verhoudings. Lees Romeine 2 self en kontroleer elke stelling teen die verse in jou Bybelweergawe.\n\nEvangelie-waarheid\nDie teks van Romeine 2 noem of illustreer: Evangelie-waarheid. Lees daardie verse weer en skryf presies op wat die Bybel sê — nie wat jy dink nie.\n\nLewe in die Gees\nDie teks van Romeine 2 noem of illustreer: Lewe in die Gees. Lees daardie verse weer en skryf presies op wat die Bybel sê — nie wat jy dink nie.\n\nPraktiese etiek\nDie teks van Romeine 2 noem of illustreer: Praktiese etiek. Lees daardie verse weer en skryf presies op wat die Bybel sê — nie wat jy dink nie.\n\nWhat God wants us to know:\nGod wil gelowiges laat weet evangelie-waarheid en hoe dit kerklewe, heiligheid en liefde moet vorm.\n\nWhy:\nPaulus redeneer van wat Christus gedoen het na hoe Christene moet leef. Soek die leerstelling in hierdie hoofstuk en die lewe wat dit verbind.\n\nSimilar elsewhere:\nRomeine 1: Compare with Romeine 1, wat direct voor hierdie hoofstuk kom — let op wat voortgaan of verander.","questions_en":["What does this passage reveal about God?","What promise, command, or truth stands out to you?","How can you apply this to your life today?"],"questions_af":["Wat openbaar hierdie gedeelte oor God?","Watter belofte, gebod of waarheid val vir jou op?","Hoe kan jy dit vandag in jou lewe toepas?"]},{"day":319,"title_en":"Romans 3–5","title_af":"Romeine 3–5","passages":[{"book_id":45,"chapter":3},{"book_id":45,"chapter":4},{"book_id":45,"chapter":5}],"commentary_intro_en":"You are reading through the whole Bible. Each chapter summary below helps you grasp the main story before you read the verses.","commentary_intro_af":"Jy lees deur die hele Bybel. Elke hoofstuk-opsomming hieronder help jou die hoofverhaal te begryp voordat jy die verse lees.","commentary_sections":[{"book_id":45,"chapter":3,"heading_en":"Romans 3","heading_af":"Romeine 3","summary_en":"Romans 3. Paul teaches doctrine and Christian living. Connect theological truth to practical obedience in church, family, and daily relationships. Read Romans 3 yourself and verify each statement against the verses in your Bible version.","summary_af":"Romeine 3. Paulus leer leerstelling en Christelike lewe. Verbind teologiese waarheid met praktiese gehoorsaamheid in kerk, gesin en daaglikse verhoudings. Lees Romeine 3 self en kontroleer elke stelling teen die verse in jou Bybelweergawe.","study_points_en":[{"title":"Gospel truth