nWhat God wants us to know:\nGod wants believers to know gospel truth and how it should shape church life, holiness, and love for others.\n\nWhy:\nPaul''s letters argue from what Christ has done to how Christians should live. Find the doctrinal statement in this chapter and the conduct it connects to.\n\nSimilar elsewhere:\nBook 46 1: Compare with Book 46 1, which immediately precedes this chapter in the same book — notice what events or themes continue or change.\n\nBook 46 3\nBook 46 3. Paul teaches doctrine and Christian living. Connect theological truth to practical obedience in church, family, and daily relationships. Read Book 46 3 yourself and verify each statement against the verses in your Bible version.\n\nGospel truth\nThe text of Book 46 3 records or illustrates: Gospel truth. Re-read those verses and note exactly what Scripture states.\n\nLife in the Spirit\nThe text of Book 46 3 records or illustrates: Life in the Spirit. Re-read those verses and note exactly what Scripture states.\n\nPractical ethics\nThe text of Book 46 3 records or illustrates: Practical ethics. Re-read those verses and note exactly what Scripture states.\n\nWhat God wants us to know:\nGod wants believers to know gospel truth and how it should shape church life, holiness, and love for others.\n\nWhy:\nPaul''s letters argue from what Christ has done to how Christians should live. Find the doctrinal statement in this chapter and the conduct it connects to.\n\nSimilar elsewhere:\nBook 46 2: Compare with Book 46 2, which immediately precedes this chapter in the same book — notice what events or themes continue or change.\n\nBook 46 4\nBook 46 4. Paul teaches doctrine and Christian living. Connect theological truth to practical obedience in church, family, and daily relationships. Read Book 46 4 yourself and verify each statement against the verses in your Bible version.\n\nGospel truth\nThe text of Book 46 4 records or illustrates: Gospel truth. Re-read those verses and note exactly what Scripture states.\n\nLife in the Spirit\nThe text of Book 46 4 records or illustrates: Life in the Spirit. Re-read those verses and note exactly what Scripture states.\n\nPractical ethics\nThe text of Book 46 4 records or illustrates: Practical ethics. Re-read those verses and note exactly what Scripture states.\n\nWhat God wants us to know:\nGod wants believers to know gospel truth and how it should shape church life, holiness, and love for others.\n\nWhy:\nPaul''s letters argue from what Christ has done to how Christians should live. Find the doctrinal statement in this chapter and the conduct it connects to.\n\nSimilar elsewhere:\nBook 46 3: Compare with Book 46 3, which immediately precedes this chapter in the same book — notice what events or themes continue or change.","commentary_af":"Jy lees deur die hele Bybel. Elke hoofstuk-opsomming hieronder help jou die hoofverhaal te begryp voordat jy die verse lees.\n\nBoek 46 2\nBoek 46 2. Paulus leer leerstelling en Christelike lewe. Verbind teologiese waarheid met praktiese gehoorsaamheid in kerk, gesin en daaglikse verhoudings. Lees Boek 46 2 self en kontroleer elke stelling teen die verse in jou Bybelweergawe.\n\nEvangelie-waarheid\nDie teks van Boek 46 2 noem of illustreer: Evangelie-waarheid. Lees daardie verse weer en skryf presies op wat die Bybel sê — nie wat jy dink nie.\n\nLewe in die Gees\nDie teks van Boek 46 2 noem of illustreer: Lewe in die Gees. Lees daardie verse weer en skryf presies op wat die Bybel sê — nie wat jy dink nie.\n\nPraktiese etiek\nDie teks van Boek 46 2 noem of illustreer: Praktiese etiek. Lees daardie verse weer en skryf presies op wat die Bybel sê — nie wat jy dink nie.\n\nWhat God wants us to know:\nGod wil gelowiges laat weet evangelie-waarheid en hoe dit kerklewe, heiligheid en liefde moet vorm.\n\nWhy:\nPaulus redeneer van wat Christus gedoen het na hoe Christene moet leef. Soek die leerstelling in hierdie hoofstuk en die lewe wat dit verbind.\n\nSimilar elsewhere:\nBook 46 1: