 or illustrates: Hope in Christ''s return. Re-read those verses and note exactly what Scripture states.\n\nWhat God wants us to know:\nGod wants his people to remain faithful under pressure, love one another, and hold to hope in Christ.\n\nWhy:\nThese letters encourage endurance and holy living. Notice exhortations in this chapter and the reason the writer gives for obeying them.\n\nSimilar elsewhere:\nBook 62 3: Compare with Book 62 3, which immediately precedes this chapter in the same book — notice what events or themes continue or change.\n\nBook 62 5\nBook 62 5. Pastoral encouragement for faith under pressure. Look for calls to endurance, love, holiness, and confident hope in Christ. Read Book 62 5 yourself and verify each statement against the verses in your Bible version.\n\nEndurance in trials\nThe text of Book 62 5 records or illustrates: Endurance in trials. Re-read those verses and note exactly what Scripture states.\n\nLove and unity\nThe text of Book 62 5 records or illustrates: Love and unity. Re-read those verses and note exactly what Scripture states.\n\nHope in Christ''s return\nThe text of Book 62 5 records or illustrates: Hope in Christ''s return. Re-read those verses and note exactly what Scripture states.\n\nWhat God wants us to know:\nGod wants his people to remain faithful under pressure, love one another, and hold to hope in Christ.\n\nWhy:\nThese letters encourage endurance and holy living. Notice exhortations in this chapter and the reason the writer gives for obeying them.\n\nSimilar elsewhere:\nBook 62 4: Compare with Book 62 4, which immediately precedes this chapter in the same book — notice what events or themes continue or change.\n\nBook 63 1\nBook 63 1. Pastoral encouragement for faith under pressure. Look for calls to endurance, love, holiness, and confident hope in Christ. Read Book 63 1 yourself and verify each statement against the verses in your Bible version.\n\nEndurance in trials\nThe text of Book 63 1 records or illustrates