h the certainty that God wins and His people inherit eternal life. Read Revelation 11 yourself and verify each statement against the verses in your Bible version.\n\nChrist the victorious Lamb\nThe text of Revelation 11 records or illustrates: Christ the victorious Lamb. Re-read those verses and note exactly what Scripture states.\n\nJudgment and mercy\nThe text of Revelation 11 records or illustrates: Judgment and mercy. Re-read those verses and note exactly what Scripture states.\n\nNew creation hope\nThe text of Revelation 11 records or illustrates: New creation hope. Re-read those verses and note exactly what Scripture states.\n\nWhat God wants us to know:\nGod wants us to know that Christ reigns, justice will be done, and God will renew creation for his people.\n\nWhy:\nRevelation uses visions of throne, Lamb, judgment, and new creation. Identify what this chapter records about Christ''s authority and the future God promises.\n\nSimilar elsewhere:\nBook 66 10: Compare with Book 66 10, which immediately precedes this chapter in the same book — notice what events or themes continue or change.\n\nRevelation 12\nRevelation 12. Apocalyptic vision of Christ''s victory and final renewal. Balance symbolic imagery with the certainty that God wins and His people inherit eternal life. Read Revelation 12 yourself and verify each statement against the verses in your Bible version.\n\nChrist the victorious Lamb\nThe text of Revelation 12 records or illustrates: Christ the victorious Lamb. Re-read those verses and note exactly what Scripture states.\n\nJudgment and mercy\nThe text of Revelation 12 records or illustrates: Judgment and mercy. Re-read those verses and note exactly what Scripture states.\n\nNew creation hope\nThe text of Revelation 12 records or illustrates: New creation hope. Re-read those verses and note exactly what Scripture states.\n\nWhat God wants us to know:\nGod wants us to know that Christ reigns, justice will be done, and God will renew creation for his people.\n\nWhy:\nRevelation uses visions of throne, Lamb, judgment, and new creation. Identify what this chapter records about Christ''s authority and the future God promises.\n\nSimilar elsewhere:\nBook 66 11: Compare with Book 66 11, which immediately precedes this chapter in the same book — notice what events or themes continue or change.\n\nRevelation 13\nRevelation 13. Apocalyptic vision of Christ''s victory and final renewal. Balance symbolic imagery with the certainty that God wins and His people inherit eternal life. Read Revelation 13 yourself and verify each statement against the verses in your Bible version.\n\nChrist the victorious Lamb\nThe text of Revelation 13 records or illustrates: Christ the victorious Lamb. Re-read those verses and note exactly what Scripture states.\n\nJudgment and mercy\nThe text of Revelation 13 records or illustrates: Judgment and mercy. Re-read those verses and note exactly what Scripture states.\n\nNew creation hope\nThe text of Revelation 13 records or illustrates: New creation hope. Re-read those verses and note exactly what Scripture states.\n\nWhat God wants us to know:\nGod wants us to know that Christ reigns, justice will be done, and God will renew creation for his people.\n\nWhy:\nRevelation uses visions of throne, Lamb, judgment, and new creation. Identify what this chapter records about Christ''s authority and the future God promises.\n\nSimilar elsewhere:\nBook 66 12: Compare with Book 66 12, which immediately precedes this chapter in the same book — notice what events or themes continue or change.","commentary_af":"Jy lees deur die hele Bybel. Elke hoofstuk-opsomming hieronder help jou die hoofverhaal te begryp voordat jy die verse lees.\n\nOpenbaring 11\nOpenbaring 11. Apokaliptiese visie van Christus se oorwinning en finale vernuwing. Balanseer simboliese beelde met die sekerheid dat God wen en Sy volk erf ewige lewe. Lees Openbaring 11 self en kontroleer elke stelling teen die verse in jou Bybelweergawe.\n\nChristus die oorwinnaar-Lam\nDie teks van Openbaring 11 noem of illustreer: Christus die oorwinnaar-Lam. Lees daardie verse weer en skryf presies op wat die Bybel sê — nie wat jy dink nie.\n\nVonnis en barmhartigheid\nDie teks van Openbaring 11 noem of illustreer: Vonnis en barmhartigheid. Lees daardie verse weer en skryf presies op wat die Bybel sê — nie wat jy dink nie.\n\nNuwe-skepping hoop\nDie teks van Openbaring 11 noem of illustreer: Nuwe-skepping hoop. Lees daardie verse weer en skryf presies op wat die Bybel sê — nie wat jy dink nie.\n\nWhat God wants us to know:\nGod wil hê ons moet weet dat Christus regeer, geregtigheid geskied, en God die skepping vir sy volk sal vernuwe.\n\nWhy:\nOpenbaring gebruik visies van troon, Lam, vonnis en nuwe skepping. Identifiseer wat hierdie hoofstuk oor Christus se gesag en die toekoms rekord.\n\nSimilar elsewhere:\nBook 66 10: Compare with Book 66 10, wat direct voor hierdie hoofstuk kom — let op wat voortgaan of verander.\n\nOpenbaring 12\nOpenbaring 12. Apokaliptiese visie van Christus se oorwinning en finale vernuwing. Balanseer simboliese beelde met die sekerheid dat God wen en Sy volk erf ewige lewe. Lees Openbaring 12 self en kontroleer elke stelling teen die verse in jou Bybelweergawe.\n\nChristus die oorwinnaar-Lam\nDie teks van Openbaring 12 noem of illustreer: Christus die oorwinnaar-Lam. Lees daardie verse weer en skryf presies op wat die Bybel sê — nie wat jy dink nie.\n\nVonnis en barmhartigheid\nDie teks van Openbaring 12 noem of illustreer: Vonnis en barmhartigheid. Lees daardie verse weer en skryf presies op wat die Bybel sê — nie wat jy dink nie.\n\nNuwe-skepping hoop\nDie teks van Openbaring 12 noem of illustreer: Nuwe-skepping hoop. Lees daardie verse weer en skryf presies op wat die Bybel sê — nie wat jy dink nie.\n\nWhat God wants us to know:\nGod wil hê ons moet weet dat Christus regeer, geregtigheid geskied, en God die skepping vir sy volk sal vernuwe.\n\nWhy:\nOpenbaring gebruik visies van troon, La