es continue or change.\nProverbs 1:7: Wisdom books often repeat the theme that the fear of the Lord is the beginning of wisdom (Proverbs 1:7). Compare how each psalm or proverb applies that foundation differently.\n\nProverbs 10\nRighteous speech vs. wicked mouth; diligent hands bring wealth. Read Proverbs 10 yourself and verify each statement against the verses in your Bible version.\n\nPractical wisdom for daily choices\nThe text of Proverbs 10 records or illustrates: Practical wisdom for daily choices. Re-read those verses and note exactly what Scripture states.\n\nFear of the Lord as foundation\nThe text of Proverbs 10 records or illustrates: Fear of the Lord as foundation. Re-read those verses and note exactly what Scripture states.\n\nOne principle to practice today\nThe text of Proverbs 10 records or illustrates: One principle to practice today. Re-read those verses and note exactly what Scripture states.\n\nWhat God wants us to know:\nGod wants us to know that true wisdom begins with reverence for him and shapes daily choices, speech, and worship.\n\nWhy:\nWisdom passages tie understanding to the fear of the Lord and practical living. Notice commands, prayers, or counsel in this chapter and what attitude toward God they assume.\n\nSimilar elsewhere:\nBook 20 9: Compare with Book 20 9, which immediately precedes this chapter in the same book — notice what events or themes continue or change.\nProverbs 1:7: Wisdom books often repeat the theme that the fear of the Lord is the beginning of wisdom (Proverbs 1:7). Compare how each psalm or proverb applies that foundation differently.\n\nProverbs 11\nHonest scales; pride before destruction; gossip like choice food. Read Proverbs 11 yourself and verify each statement against the verses in your Bible version.\n\nPractical wisdom for daily choices\nThe text of Proverbs 11 records or illustrates: Practical wisdom for daily choices. Re-read those verses and note exactly what Scripture states.\n\nFear of the Lord as foundation\nThe text of Proverbs 11 records or illustrates: Fear of the Lord as foundation. Re-read those verses and note exactly what Scripture states.\n\nOne principle to practice today\nThe text of Proverbs 11 records or illustrates: One principle to practice today. Re-read those verses and note exactly what Scripture states.\n\nWhat God wants us to know:\nGod wants us to know that true wisdom begins with reverence for him and shapes daily choices, speech, and worship.\n\nWhy:\nWisdom passages tie understanding to the fear of the Lord and practical living. Notice commands, prayers, or counsel in this chapter and what attitude toward God they assume.\n\nSimilar elsewhere:\nBook 20 10: Compare with Book 20 10, which immediately precedes this chapter in the same book — notice what events or themes continue or change.\nProverbs 1:7: Wisdom books often repeat the theme that the fear of the Lord is the beginning of wisdom (Proverbs 1:7). Compare how each psalm or proverb applies that foundation differently.","commentary_af":"Ou Testament verhaal en lering. Gebruik die hoofstuk-opsommings om God se verbondverhaal deur die geskiedenis te volg.\n\nSpreuke 7\nWysheid roep in strate; wie haar verwerp, staan ondergang te wag. Lees Spreuke 7 self en kontroleer elke stelling teen die verse in jou Bybelweergawe.\n\nPraktiese wysheid vir daaglikse keuses\nDie teks van Spreuke 7 noem of illustreer: Praktiese wysheid vir daaglikse keuses. Lees daardie verse weer en skryf presies op wat die Bybel sê — nie wat jy dink nie.\n\nVrees vir die Here as fondament\nDie teks van Spreuke 7 noem of illustreer: Vrees vir die Here as fondament. Lees daardie verse weer en skryf presies op wat die Bybel sê — nie wat jy dink nie.\n\nEen beginsel om vandag te oefen\nDie teks van Spreuke 7 noem of illustreer: Een beginsel om vandag te oefen. Lees daardie verse weer en skryf presies op wat die Bybel sê — nie wat jy dink nie.\n\nWhat God wants us to know:\nGod wil hê ons moet weet dat ware wysheid begin met eerbied vir Hom en daaglikse keuses, spraak en aanbidding vorm.\n\nWhy:\nWysheid verbind insig met die vrees vir die Here. Let op gebooie, gebede of raad in hierdie hoofstuk en watter houding teenoor God dit veronderstel.\n\nSimilar elsewhere:\nBook 20 6: Compare with Book 20 6, wat direct voor hierdie hoofstuk kom — let op wat voortgaan of verander.\nSpreuke 1:7: Wysheidsboeke herhaal dat die vrees vir die Here die begin van wysheid is (Spr 1:7). Vergelyk hoe elke psalm of spreuk dit toepas.\n\nSpreuke 8\nWysheid se waarde oortref silwer; sy was by God by die skepping. Lees Spreuke 8 self en kontroleer elke stelling teen die verse in jou Bybelweergawe.\n\nPraktiese wysheid vir daaglikse keuses\nDie teks van Spreuke 8 noem of illustreer: Praktiese wysheid vir daaglikse keuses. Lees daardie verse weer en skryf presies op wat die Bybel sê — nie wat jy dink nie.\n\nVrees vir die Here as fondament\nDie teks van Spreuke 8 noem of illustreer: Vrees vir die Here as fondament. Lees daardie verse weer en skryf presies op wat die Bybel sê — nie wat jy dink nie.\n\nEen beginsel om vandag te oefen\nDie teks van Spreuke 8 noem of illustreer: Een beginsel om vandag te oefen. Lees daardie verse weer en skryf presies op wat die Bybel sê — nie wat jy dink nie.\n\nWhat God wants us to know:\nGod wil hê ons moet weet dat ware wysheid begin met eerbied vir Hom en daaglikse keuses, spraak en aanbidding vorm.\n\nWhy:\nWysheid verbind insig met die vrees vir die Here. Let op gebooie, gebede of raad in hierdie hoofstuk en watter houding teenoor God dit veronderstel.\n\nSimilar elsewhere:\nBook 20 7: Compare with Book 20 7, wat direct voor hierdie hoofstuk kom — let op wat voortgaan of verander.\nSpreuke 1:7: Wysheidsboeke herhaal dat die vrees vir die Here die begin van wysheid is (Spr 1:7). Vergelyk hoe elke psalm of spreuk dit toepas.\n\nSpreuke 9\nWysheid bou haar huis; dwaasheid nooi na die dood. Lees Spreuke 9 self en kontroleer elke stelling teen die verse in jou Bybelweergawe.\n\