gebooie, gebede of raad in hierdie hoofstuk en watter houding teenoor God dit veronderstel.","cross_references_en":[{"ref":"Book 22 2","comparison":"Compare with Book 22 2, which immediately precedes this chapter in the same book — notice what events or themes continue or change."},{"ref":"Proverbs 1:7","comparison":"Wisdom books often repeat the theme that the fear of the Lord is the beginning of wisdom (Proverbs 1:7). Compare how each psalm or proverb applies that foundation differently."}],"cross_references_af":[{"ref":"Book 22 2","comparison":"Compare with Book 22 2, wat direct voor hierdie hoofstuk kom — let op wat voortgaan of verander."},{"ref":"Spreuke 1:7","comparison":"Wysheidsboeke herhaal dat die vrees vir die Here die begin van wysheid is (Spr 1:7). Vergelyk hoe elke psalm of spreuk dit toepas."}],"highlights_en":["Fear of the Lord","Honest self-reflection","Practical daily application"],"highlights_af":["Vrees vir die Here","Eerlike selfondersoek","Praktiese daaglikse toepassing"]}],"commentary_en":"Old Testament narrative and teaching. Use the chapter summaries to track God''s covenant story across history.\n\nBook 21 11\nBook 21 11. Wisdom literature for worship, prayer, and practical living. Apply its truths to your relationships, work, and inner life. Read Book 21 11 yourself and verify each statement against the verses in your Bible version.\n\nFear of the Lord\nThe text of Book 21 11 records or illustrates: Fear of the Lord. Re-read those verses and note exactly what Scripture states.\n\nHonest self-reflection\nThe text of Book 21 11 records or illustrates: Honest self-reflection. Re-read those verses and note exactly what Scripture states.\n\nPractical daily application\nThe text of Book 21 11 records or illustrates: Practical daily application. Re-read those verses and note exactly what Scripture states.\n\nWhat God wants us to know:\nGod wants us to know that true wisdom begins with reverence for him and shapes daily choices, speech, and worship.\n\nWhy:\nWisdom passages tie understanding to the fear of the Lord and practical living. Notice commands, prayers, or counsel in this chapter and what attitude toward God they assume.\n\nSimilar elsewhere:\nBook 21 10: Compare with Book 21 10, which immediately precedes this chapter in the same book — notice what events or themes continue or change.\nProverbs 1:7: Wisdom books often repeat the theme that the fear of the Lord is the beginning of wisdom (Proverbs 1:7). Compare how each psalm or proverb applies that foundation differently.\n\nBook 21 12\nBook 21 12. Wisdom literature for worship, prayer, and practical living. Apply its truths to your relationships, work, and inner life. Read Book 21 12 yourself and verify each statement against the verses in your Bible version.\n\nFear of the Lord\nThe text of Book 21 12 records or illustrates: Fear of the Lord. Re-read those verses and note exactly what Scripture states.\n\nHonest self-reflection\nThe text of Book 21 12 records or illustrates: Honest self-reflection. Re-read those verses and note exactly what Scripture states.\n\nPractical daily application\nThe text of Book 21 12 records or illustrates: Practical daily application. Re-read those verses and note exactly what Scripture states.\n\nWhat God wants us to know:\nGod wants us to know that true wisdom begins with reverence for him and shapes daily choices, speech, and worship.\n\nWhy:\nWisdom passages tie understanding to the fear of the Lord and practical living. Notice commands, prayers, or counsel in this chapter and what attitude toward God they assume.\n\nSimilar elsewhere:\nBook 21 11: Compare with Book 21 11, which immediately precedes this chapter in the same book — notice what events or themes continue or change.\nProverbs 1:7: Wisdom books often repeat the theme that the fear of the Lord is the beginning of wisdom (Proverbs 1:7). Compare how each psalm or proverb applies that foundation differently.\n\nBook 22 1\nBook 22 1. Wisdom literature for