h reverence for him and shapes daily choices, speech, and worship.\n\nWhy:\nWisdom passages tie understanding to the fear of the Lord and practical living. Notice commands, prayers, or counsel in this chapter and what attitude toward God they assume.\n\nSimilar elsewhere:\nBook 22 1: Compare with Book 22 1, which immediately precedes this chapter in the same book — notice what events or themes continue or change.\nProverbs 1:7: Wisdom books often repeat the theme that the fear of the Lord is the beginning of wisdom (Proverbs 1:7). Compare how each psalm or proverb applies that foundation differently.\n\nBook 22 3\nBook 22 3. Wisdom literature for worship, prayer, and practical living. Apply its truths to your relationships, work, and inner life. Read Book 22 3 yourself and verify each statement against the verses in your Bible version.\n\nFear of the Lord\nThe text of Book 22 3 records or illustrates: Fear of the Lord. Re-read those verses and note exactly what Scripture states.\n\nHonest self-reflection\nThe text of Book 22 3 records or illustrates: Honest self-reflection. Re-read those verses and note exactly what Scripture states.\n\nPractical daily application\nThe text of Book 22 3 records or illustrates: Practical daily application. Re-read those verses and note exactly what Scripture states.\n\nWhat God wants us to know:\nGod wants us to know that true wisdom begins with reverence for him and shapes daily choices, speech, and worship.\n\nWhy:\nWisdom passages tie understanding to the fear of the Lord and practical living. Notice commands, prayers, or counsel in this chapter and what attitude toward God they assume.\n\nSimilar elsewhere:\nBook 22 2: Compare with Book 22 2, which immediately precedes this chapter in the same book — notice what events or themes continue or change.\nProverbs 1:7: Wisdom books often repeat the theme that the fear of the Lord is the beginning of wisdom (Proverbs 1:7). Compare how each psalm or proverb applies that foundation differently.","commentary_af":"Ou Testament verhaal en lering. Gebruik die hoofstuk-opsommings om God se verbondverhaal deur die geskiedenis te volg.\n\nBoek 21 11\nBoek 21 11. Wysheidsliteratuur vir aanbidding, gebed en praktiese lewe. Pas die waarhede toe op jou verhoudings, werk en innerlike lewe. Lees Boek 21 11 self en kontroleer elke stelling teen die verse in jou Bybelweergawe.\n\nVrees vir die Here\nDie teks van Boek 21 11 noem of illustreer: Vrees vir die Here. Lees daardie verse weer en skryf presies op wat die Bybel sê — nie wat jy dink nie.\n\nEerlike selfondersoek\nDie teks van Boek 21 11 noem of illustreer: Eerlike selfondersoek. Lees daardie verse weer en skryf presies op wat die Bybel sê — nie wat jy dink nie.\n\nPraktiese daaglikse toepassing\nDie teks van Boek 21 11 noem of illustreer: Praktiese daaglikse toepassing. Lees daardie verse weer en skryf presies op wat die Bybel sê — nie wat jy dink nie.\n\nWhat God wants us to know:\nGod wil hê ons moet weet dat ware wysheid begin met eerbied vir Hom en daaglikse keuses, spraak en aanbidding vorm.\n\nWhy:\nWysheid verbind insig met die vrees vir die Here. Let op gebooie, gebede of raad in hierdie hoofstuk en watter houding teenoor God dit veronderstel.\n\nSimilar elsewhere:\nBook 21 10: Compare with Book 21 10, wat direct voor hierdie hoofstuk kom — let op wat voortgaan of verander.\nSpreuke 1:7: Wysheidsboeke herhaal dat die vrees vir die Here die begin van wysheid is (Spr 1:7). Vergelyk hoe elke psalm of spreuk dit toepas.\n\nBoek 21 12\nBoek 21 12. Wysheidsliteratuur vir aanbidding, gebed en praktiese lewe. Pas die waarhede toe op jou verhoudings, werk en innerlike lewe. Lees Boek 21 12 self en kontroleer elke stelling teen die verse in jou Bybelweergawe.\n\nVrees vir die Here\nDie teks van Boek 21 12 noem of illustreer: Vrees vir die Here. Lees daardie verse weer en skryf presies op wat die Bybel sê — nie wat jy dink nie.\n\nEerlike selfondersoek\nDie teks van Boek 21 12 noem of illustreer: Eerlike selfo