f Book 28 8 records or illustrates: Hope for the future. Re-read those verses and note exactly what Scripture states.\n\nWhat God wants us to know:\nGod wants his people to know that he calls them back to faithfulness, warns of judgment, and often pairs correction with hope.\n\nWhy:\nProphetic chapters usually contain God''s speech—accusation, command, or promise. Identify what God says he will do and what he asks his people to do.\n\nSimilar elsewhere:\nBook 28 7: Compare with Book 28 7, which immediately precedes this chapter in the same book — notice what events or themes continue or change.\n\nBook 28 9\nBook 28 9. Prophetic word calling God''s people to covenant faithfulness. Listen for judgment, hope, and promises pointing to Messiah and restoration. Read Book 28 9 yourself and verify each statement against the verses in your Bible version.\n\nSin and repentance\nThe text of Book 28 9 records or illustrates: Sin and repentance. Re-read those verses and note exactly what Scripture states.\n\nGod''s holy standards\nThe text of Book 28 9 records or illustrates: God''s holy standards. Re-read those verses and note exactly what Scripture states.\n\nHope for the future\nThe text of Book 28 9 records or illustrates: Hope for the future. Re-read those verses and note exactly what Scripture states.\n\nWhat God wants us to know:\nGod wants his people to know that he calls them back to faithfulness, warns of judgment, and often pairs correction with hope.\n\nWhy:\nProphetic chapters usually contain God''s speech—accusation, command, or promise. Identify what God says he will do and what he asks his people to do.\n\nSimilar elsewhere:\nBook 28 8: Compare with Book 28 8, which immediately precedes this chapter in the same book — notice what events or themes continue or change.\n\nBook 28 10\nBook 28 10. Prophetic word calling God''s people to covenant faithfulness. Listen for judgment, hope, and promises pointing to Messiah and restoration. Read Book 28 10 yourself and verify each statement against the verses in your Bible version.\n\nSin and repentance\nThe text of Book 28 10 records or illustrates: Sin and repentance. Re-read those verses and note exactly what Scripture states.\n\nGod''s holy standards\nThe text of Book 28 10 records or illustrates: God''s holy standards. Re-read those verses and note exactly what Scripture states.\n\nHope for the future\nThe text of Book 28 10 records or illustrates: Hope for the future. Re-read those verses and note exactly what Scripture states.\n\nWhat God wants us to know:\nGod wants his people to know that he calls them back to faithfulness, warns of judgment, and often pairs correction with hope.\n\nWhy:\nProphetic chapters usually contain God''s speech—accusation, command, or promise. Identify what God says he will do and what he asks his people to do.\n\nSimilar elsewhere:\nBook 28 9: Compare with Book 28 9, which immediately precedes this chapter in the same book — notice what events or themes continue or change.\n\nBook 28 11\nBook 28 11. Prophetic word calling God''s people to covenant faithfulness. Listen for judgment, hope, and promises pointing to Messiah and restoration. Read Book 28 11 yourself and verify each statement against the verses in your Bible version.\n\nSin and repentance\nThe text of Book 28 11 records or illustrates: Sin and repentance. Re-read those verses and note exactly what Scripture states.\n\nGod''s holy standards\nThe text of Book 28 11 records or illustrates: God''s holy standards. Re-read those verses and note exactly what Scripture states.\n\nHope for the future\nThe text of Book 28 11 records or illustrates: Hope for the future. Re-read those verses and note exactly what Scripture states.\n\nWhat God wants us to know:\nGod wants his people to know that he calls them back to faithfulness, warns of judgment, and often pairs correction with hope.\n\nWhy:\nProphetic chapters usually contain God''s speech—accusation, command, or promise. Identify what God says he will do and what he asks his people to do.\n\nSimilar elsewhere:\nBook 28 10: Compare with Book 28 10, which immediately precedes this chapter in the same book — notice what events or themes continue or change.\n\nBook 28 12\nBook 28 12. Prophetic word calling God''s people to covenant faithfulness. Listen for judgment, hope, and promises pointing to Messiah and restoration. Read Book 28 12 yourself and verify each statement against the verses in your Bible version.\n\nSin and repentance\nThe text of Book 28 12 records or illustrates: Sin and repentance. Re-read those verses and note exactly what Scripture states.\n\nGod''s holy standards\nThe text of Book 28 12 records or illustrates: God''s holy standards. Re-read those verses and note exactly what Scripture states.\n\nHope for the future\nThe text of Book 28 12 records or illustrates: Hope for the future. Re-read those verses and note exactly what Scripture states.\n\nWhat God wants us to know:\nGod wants his people to know that he calls them back to faithfulness, warns of judgment, and often pairs correction with hope.\n\nWhy:\nProphetic chapters usually contain God''s speech—accusation, command, or promise. Identify what God says he will do and what he asks his people to do.\n\nSimilar elsewhere:\nBook 28 11: Compare with Book 28 11, which immediately precedes this chapter in the same book — notice what events or themes continue or change.","commentary_af":"Ou Testament verhaal en lering. Gebruik die hoofstuk-opsommings om God se verbondverhaal deur die geskiedenis te volg.\n\nBoek 28 8\nBoek 28 8. Profetiese woord wat God se volk roep tot verbondstrousheid. Luister vir vonnis, hoop en beloftes wat wys na Messias en herstel. Lees Boek 28 8 self en kontroleer elke stelling teen die verse in jou Bybelweergawe.\n\nSonde en berou\nDie teks van Boek 28 8 noem of illustreer: Sonde en berou. Lees daardie verse weer en skryf presies op wat die Bybel sê — nie wat jy dink nie.\n\nGod se heilige standaarde\nDie teks van Boek 28 8 noem of illustreer: God se heilige standaarde. Lees daardie verse weer en skryf presies op wat die Bybel sê — nie wat jy dink nie.\n\nHoop vir die toekoms\nDie teks van Boek 28 8 noem of illustreer: Hoop vir die toekoms. Lees daardie verse weer en skryf presies op wat die Bybel sê — nie wat jy dink nie.\n\nWhat God wants us to know:\nGod wil sy volk laat weet dat Hy hulle terugroep na trou, waarsku vir vonnis, en korreksie dikwels met hoop paar.\n\nWhy:\nProfetiese hoofstukke bevat gewoonlik God se spraak—beskuldiging, gebod of belofte. Identifiseer wat God sê Hy sal doen en wat Hy van sy volk vra.\n\nSimilar elsewhere:\nBook 28 7: Compare with Book 28 7, wat direct voor hierdie hoofstuk kom — let op wat voortgaan of verander.\n\nBoek 28 9\nBoek 28 9. Profetiese woord wat God se volk roep tot verbondstrousheid. Luister vir vonnis, hoop en beloftes wat wys na Messias en herstel. Lees Boek 28 9 self en kontroleer elke stelling teen die verse in jou Bybelweergawe.\n\nSonde en berou\nDie teks van Boek 28 9 noem of illustreer: Sonde en berou. Lees daardie verse weer en skryf presies op wat die Bybel sê — nie wat jy dink nie.\n\nGod se heilige standaarde\nDie teks van Boek 28 9 noem of illustreer: God se heilige standaarde. Lees daardie verse weer en skryf presies op wat die Bybel sê — nie wat jy dink nie.\n\nHoop vir die toekoms\nDie teks van Boek 28 9 noem of illustreer: Hoop vir die toekoms. Lees daardie verse weer en skryf presies op wat die Bybel sê — nie wat jy dink nie.\n\nWhat God wants us to know:\nGod wil sy volk laat weet dat Hy hulle terugroep na trou, waarsku vir vonnis, en korreksie dikwels met hoop paar.\n\nWhy:\nProfetiese hoofstukke bevat gewoonlik God se spraak—beskuldiging, gebod of belofte. Identifiseer wat God sê Hy sal doen en wat Hy van sy volk vra.\n\nSimilar elsewhere:\nBook 28 8: Compare with Book 28 8, wat direct voor hierdie hoofstuk kom — let op wat voortgaan of verander.\n\nBoek 28 10\nBoek 28 10. Profetiese woord wat God se volk r