    'nt',
    '[{"day":1,"title_en":"Romans 1","title_af":"Romeine 1","passages":[{"book_id":45,"chapter":1}],"commentary_intro_en":"Today''s themed reading: Romans 1. Study each chapter section below as you read.","commentary_intro_af":"Vandag se tematiese leeswerk: Romeine 1. Bestudeer elke hoofstuk-afdeling hieronder terwyl jy lees.","commentary_sections":[{"book_id":45,"chapter":1,"heading_en":"Romans 1","heading_af":"Romeine 1","summary_en":"Paul introduces the gospel as God''s power for salvation. Humanity''s universal sin; righteousness revealed apart from law. Read Romans 1 yourself and verify each statement against the verses in your Bible version.","summary_af":"Paul stel die evangelie voor as God se krag vir redding. Mensdom se universele sonde; geregtigheid openbaar buite die wet. Lees Romeine 1 self en kontroleer elke stelling teen die verse in jou Bybelweergawe.","study_points_en":[{"title":"The gospel is God''s power","verses":"","detail":"The text of Romans 1 records or illustrates: The gospel is God''s power. Re-read those verses and note exactly what Scripture states."},{"title":"None righteous, no not one","verses":"","detail":"The text of Romans 1 records or illustrates: None righteous, no not one. Re-read those verses and note exactly what Scripture states."},{"title":"Righteousness through faith","verses":"","detail":"The text of Romans 1 records or illustrates: Righteousness through faith. Re-read those verses and note exactly what Scripture states."}],"study_points_af":[{"title":"Die evangelie is God se krag","verses":"","detail":"Die teks van Romeine 1 noem of illustreer: Die evangelie is God se krag. Lees daardie verse weer en skryf presies op wat die Bybel sê — nie wat jy dink nie."},{"title":"Geen regverdiges, selfs nie een nie","verses":"","detail":"Die teks van Romeine 1 noem of illustreer: Geen regverdiges, selfs nie een nie. Lees daardie verse weer en skryf presies op wat die Bybel sê — nie wat jy dink nie."},{"title":"Geregtigheid deur geloof","verses":"","detail":"Die teks van Romeine 1 noem of illustreer: Geregtigheid deur geloof. Lees daardie verse weer en skryf presies op wat die Bybel sê — nie wat jy dink nie."}],"teaching_en":"God wants believers to know gospel truth and how it should shape church life, holiness, and love for others.","teaching_why_en":"Paul''s letters argue from what Christ has done to how Christians should live. Find the doctrinal statement in this chapter and the conduct it connects to.","teaching_af":"God wil gelowiges laat weet evangelie-waarheid en hoe dit kerklewe, heiligheid en liefde moet vorm.","teaching_why_af":"Paulus redeneer van wat Christus gedoen het na hoe Christene moet leef. Soek die leerstelling in hierdie hoofstuk en die lewe wat dit verbind.","cross_references_en":[],"cross_references_af":[],"highlights_en":["The gospel is God''s power","None righteous, no not one","Righteousness through faith"],"highlights_af":["Die evangelie is God se krag","Geen regverdiges, selfs nie een nie","Geregtigheid deur geloof"]}],"commentary_en":"Today''s themed reading: Romans 1. Study each chapter section below as you read.\n\nRomans 1\nPaul introduces the gospel as God''s power for salvation. Humanity''s universal sin; righteousness revealed apart from law. Read Romans 1 yourself and verify each statement against the verses in your Bible version.\n\nThe gospel is God''s power\nThe text of Romans 1 records or illustrates: The gospel is God''s power. Re-read those verses and note exactly what Scripture states.\n\nNone righteous, no not one\nThe text of Romans 1 records or illustrates: None righteous, no not one. Re-read those verses and note exactly what Scripture states.\n\nRighteousness through faith\nThe text of Romans 1 records or illustrates: Righteousness through faith. Re-read those verses and note exactly what Scripture states.\n\nWhat God wants us to know:\nGod wants believers to know gospel truth and how it should shape church life, holiness, and love for others.\n\nWhy:\nPaul''s letters argue from what Christ has done to how Christians should live. Find the doctrinal statement in this chapter and the conduct it connects to.","commentary_af":"Vandag se tematiese leeswerk: Romeine 1. Bestudeer elke hoofstuk-afdeling hieronder terwyl jy lees.\n\nRomeine 1\nPaul stel die evangelie voor as God se krag vir redding. Mensdom se universele sonde; geregtigheid openbaar buite die wet. Lees Romeine 1 self en kontroleer elke stelling teen die verse in jou Bybelweergawe.\n\nDie evangelie is God se krag\nDie teks van Romeine 1 noem of illustreer: Die evangelie is God se krag. Lees daardie verse weer en skryf presies op wat die Bybel sê — nie wat jy dink nie.\n\nGeen regverdiges, selfs nie een nie\nDie teks van Romeine 1 noem of illustreer: Geen regverdiges, selfs nie een nie. Lees daardie verse weer en skryf presies op wat die Bybel sê — nie wat jy dink nie.\n\nGeregtigheid deur geloof\nDie teks van Romeine 1 noem of illustreer: Geregtigheid deur geloof. Lees daardie verse weer en skryf presies op wat die Bybel sê — nie wat jy dink nie.\n\nWhat God wants us to know:\nGod wil gelowiges laat weet evangelie-waarheid en hoe dit kerklewe, heiligheid en liefde moet vorm.\n\nWhy:\nPaulus redeneer van wat Christus gedoen het na hoe Christene moet leef. Soek die leerstelling in hierdie hoofstuk en die lewe wat dit verbind.","questions_en":["What does this passage reveal about God?","What promise, command, or truth stands out to you?","How can you apply this to your life today?"],"questions_af":["Wat openbaar hierdie gedeelte oor God?","Watter belofte, gebod of waarheid val vir jou op?","Hoe kan jy dit vandag in jou lewe toepas?"]},{"day":2,"title_en":"Romans 2","title_af":"Romeine 2","passages":[{"book_id":45,"chapter":2}],"commentary_intro_en":"Today''s themed reading: Romans 2. Study each chapter section below as you read.","commentary_intro_af":"Vandag se tematiese leeswerk: Romeine 2. Bestudeer elke hoofstuk-afdeling hieronder terwyl jy lees.","comm