    '[{"day":1,"title_en":"John 1","title_af":"Johannes 1","passages":[{"book_id":43,"chapter":1}],"commentary_intro_en":"Today''s themed reading: John 1. Study each chapter section below as you read.","commentary_intro_af":"Vandag se tematiese leeswerk: Johannes 1. Bestudeer elke hoofstuk-afdeling hieronder terwyl jy lees.","commentary_sections":[{"book_id":43,"chapter":1,"heading_en":"John 1","heading_af":"Johannes 1","summary_en":"John opens with the eternal Word — Jesus as Creator and Light. John the Baptist prepares the way; Jesus calls the first disciples. Read John 1 yourself and verify each statement against the verses in your Bible version.","summary_af":"Johannes open met die ewige Woord — Jesus as Skepper en Lig. Johannes die Doper berei die pad; Jesus roep die eerste dissipels. Lees Johannes 1 self en kontroleer elke stelling teen die verse in jou Bybelweergawe.","study_points_en":[{"title":"In the beginning was the Word","verses":"","detail":"The text of John 1 records or illustrates: In the beginning was the Word. Re-read those verses and note exactly what Scripture states."},{"title":"Light shines in darkness","verses":"","detail":"The text of John 1 records or illustrates: Light shines in darkness. Re-read those verses and note exactly what Scripture states."},{"title":"Come and see","verses":"","detail":"The text of John 1 records or illustrates: Come and see. Re-read those verses and note exactly what Scripture states."}],"study_points_af":[{"title":"In die begin was die Woord","verses":"","detail":"Die teks van Johannes 1 noem of illustreer: In die begin was die Woord. Lees daardie verse weer en skryf presies op wat die Bybel sê — nie wat jy dink nie."},{"title":"Lig skyn in duisternis","verses":"","detail":"Die teks van Johannes 1 noem of illustreer: Lig skyn in duisternis. Lees daardie verse weer en skryf presies op wat die Bybel sê — nie wat jy dink nie."},{"title":"Kom en sien","verses":"","detail":"Die teks van Johannes 1 noem of illustreer: Kom en sien. Lees daardie verse weer en skryf presies op wat die Bybel sê — nie wat jy dink nie."}],"teaching_en":"God wants us to know who Jesus is and what he calls people to believe and do through his words, actions, and authority.","teaching_why_en":"Gospel chapters record what Jesus taught, healed, commanded, or revealed about the kingdom. Focus on what the chapter says Jesus did and said—not later tradition.","teaching_af":"God wil hê ons moet weet wie Jesus is en wat Hy mense roep om te glo en te doen deur sy woorde, dade en gesag.","teaching_why_af":"Evangelie-hoofstukke beskryf wat Jesus geleer, genees, beveel of openbaar het. Fokus op wat die hoofstuk sê Jesus gedoen en gesê het.","cross_references_en":[{"ref":"Parallel Gospels","comparison":"Many events in Matthew, Mark, Luke, and John appear in more than one Gospel with matching or overlapping details. Compare the same episode across Gospels to see what each writer records."}],"cross_references_af":[{"ref":"Parallelle Evangelies","comparison":"Baie gebeure in Matteus, Markus, Lukas en Johannes verskyn in meer as een Evangelie. Vergelyk dieselfde episode oor Evangelies heen."}],"highlights_en":["In the beginning was the Word","Light shines in darkness","Come and see"],"highlights_af":["In die begin was die Woord","Lig skyn in duisternis","Kom en sien"]}],"commentary_en":"Today''s themed reading: John 1. Study each chapter section below as you read.\n\nJohn 1\nJohn opens with the eternal Word — Jesus as Creator and Light. John the Baptist prepares the way; Jesus calls the first disciples. Read John 1 yourself and verify each statement against the verses in your Bible version.\n\nIn the beginning was the Word\nThe text of John 1 records or illustrates: In the beginning was the Word. Re-read those verses and note exactly what Scripture states.\n\nLight shines in darkness\nThe text of John 1 records or illustrates: Light shines in darkness. Re-read those verses and note exactly what Scripture states.\n\nCome and see\nThe text of John 1 records or illustrates: Come and see. Re-read those verses and note exactly what Scripture states.\n\nWhat God wants us to know:\nGod wants us to know who Jesus is and what he calls people to believe and do through his words, actions, and authority.\n\nWhy:\nGospel chapters record what Jesus taught, healed, commanded, or revealed about the kingdom. Focus on what the chapter says Jesus did and said—not later tradition.\n\nSimilar elsewhere:\nParallel Gospels: Many events in Matthew, Mark, Luke, and John appear in more than one Gospel with matching or overlapping details. Compare the same episode across Gospels to see what each writer records.","commentary_af":"Vandag se tematiese leeswerk: Johannes 1. Bestudeer elke hoofstuk-afdeling hieronder terwyl jy lees.\n\nJohannes 1\nJohannes open met die ewige Woord — Jesus as Skepper en Lig. Johannes die Doper berei die pad; Jesus roep die eerste dissipels. Lees Johannes 1 self en kontroleer elke stelling teen die verse in jou Bybelweergawe.\n\nIn die begin was die Woord\nDie teks van Johannes 1 noem of illustreer: In die begin was die Woord. Lees daardie verse weer en skryf presies op wat die Bybel sê — nie wat jy dink nie.\n\nLig skyn in duisternis\nDie teks van Johannes 1 noem of illustreer: Lig skyn in duisternis. Lees daardie verse weer en skryf presies op wat die Bybel sê — nie wat jy dink nie.\n\nKom en sien\nDie teks van Johannes 1 noem of illustreer: Kom en sien. Lees daardie verse weer en skryf presies op wat die Bybel sê — nie wat jy dink nie.\n\nWhat God wants us to know:\nGod wil hê ons moet weet wie Jesus is en wat Hy mense roep om te glo en te doen deur sy woorde, dade en gesag.\n\nWhy:\nEvangelie-hoofstukke beskryf wat Jesus geleer, genees, beveel of openbaar het. Fokus op wat die hoofstuk sê Jesus gedoen en gesê het.\n\nSimilar elsewhere:\nParallelle Evangelies: Baie gebeure in Matteus, Markus, Lukas en Johannes verskyn in meer as een Evangelie. Vergelyk dieselfde episode oor Evangelies heen.","questions_en":["What does this passage reveal about God?","What promise, command, or truth stands out to you?","How can you apply this to your life today?"],"questions_af":["Wat openbaar hierdie gedeelte oor God?","Watter belofte, gebod of waarheid val vir jou op?","Hoe kan jy dit vandag in jou lewe toepas?"]},{"day":2,"title_en":"John 2","title_af":"Johannes 2","passages":[{"book_id":43,"chapter":2}],"commentary_intro_en":"Today''s themed reading: John 2. Study each chapter section below as you read.","commentary_intro_af":"Vandag se tematiese leeswerk: Johannes 2. Bestudeer elke hoofstuk-afdeling hieronder terwyl jy lees.","commentary_sections":[{"book_id":43,"chapter":2,"heading_en":"John 2","heading_af":"Johannes 2","summary_en":"John 2. The Gospels reveal Jesus — His teaching, authority, compassion, and mission. Ask: Who is Jesus here, and what is He calling me to believe and do? Read John 2 yourself and verify each statement against the verses in your Bible version.","summary_af":"Johannes 2. Die Evangelies openbaar Jesus — Sy lering, gesag, barmhartigheid en sending. Vra: Wie is Jesus hier, en wat roep Hy my om te glo en te doen? Lees Johannes 2 self en kontroleer elke stelling teen die verse in jou Bybelweergawe.","study_points_en":[{"title":"Jesus'' identity and authority","verses":"","detail":"The text of John 2 records or illustrates: Jesus'' identity and authority. Re-read those verses and note exactly what Scripture states."},{"title":"Kingdom teaching","verses":"","detail":"The text of John 2 records or illustrates: Kingdom teaching. Re-read those verses and note exactly what Scripture states."},{"title":"Calls to follow","verses":"","detail":"The text of John 2 records or illustrates: Calls to follow. Re-read those verses and note exactly what Scripture states."}],"study_points_af":[{"title":"Jesus se identiteit en gesag","verses":"","detail":"Die teks van Johannes 2 noem of illustreer: Jesus se identiteit en gesag. Lees daardie verse weer en skryf presies op wat die Bybel sê — nie wat jy dink nie."},{"title":"Koninkryk-lering","verses":"","detail":"Die teks van Johannes 2 noem of illustreer: Koninkryk-lering. Lees daardie verse weer en skryf presies op wat die Bybel sê — nie wat jy dink nie."},{"title":"Oproepe om te volg","verses":"","detail":"Die teks van Johannes 2 noem of illustreer: Oproepe om te volg. Lees daardie verse weer en skryf presies op wat die Bybel sê — nie wat jy dink nie."}],"teaching_en":"God wants us to know who Jesus is and what he calls people to believe and do through his words, actions, and authority.","teaching_why_en":"Gospel chapters record what Jesus taught, healed, commanded, or revealed about the kingdom. Focus on what the chapter says Jesus did and said—not later tradition.","teaching_af":"God wil hê ons moet weet wie Jesus is en wat Hy mense roep om te glo en te doen deur sy woorde, dade en gesag.","teaching_why_af":"Evangelie-hoofstukke beskryf wat Jesus geleer, genees, beveel of openbaar het. Fokus op wat die hoofstuk sê Jesus gedoen en gesê het.","cross_references_en":[{"ref":"John 1","comparison":"Compare with John 1, which immediately precedes this chapter in the same book — notice what events or themes continue or change."},{"ref":"Parallel Gospels","comparison":"Many events in Matthew, Mark, Luke, and John appear in more than one Gospel with matching or overlapping details. Compare the same episode across Gospels to see what each writer records."}],"cross_references_af":[{"ref":"Johannes 1","comparison":"Compare with Johannes 1, wat direct voor hierdie hoofstuk kom — let op wat voortgaan of verander."},{"ref":"Parallelle Evangelies","comparison":"Baie gebeure in Matteus, Markus, Lukas en Johannes verskyn in meer as een Evangelie. Vergelyk dieselfde episode oor Evangelies heen."}],"highlights_en":["Jesus'' identity and authority","Kingdom teaching","Calls to follow"],"highlights_af":["Jesus se identiteit en gesag","Koninkryk-lering","Oproepe om te volg"]}],"commentary_en":"Today''s themed reading: John 2. Study each chapter section below as you read.\n\nJohn 2\nJohn 2. The Gospels reveal Jesus — His teaching, authority, compassion, and mission. Ask: Who is Jesus here, and what is He calling me to believe and do? Read John 2 yourself and verify each statement against the verses in your Bible version.\n\nJesus'' identity and authority\nThe text of John 2 records or illustrates: Jesus'' identity and authority. Re-read those verses and note exactly what Scripture states.\n\nKingdom teaching\nThe text of John 2 records or illustrates: Kingdom teaching. Re-read those verses and note exactly what Scripture states.\n\nCalls to follow\nThe text of John 2 records or illustrates: Calls to follow. Re-read those verses and note exactly what Scripture states.\n\nWhat God wants us to know:\nGod wants us to know who Jesus is and what he calls people to believe and do through his words, actions, and authority.\n\nWhy:\nGospel chapters record what Jesus taught, healed, commanded, or revealed about the kingdom. Focus on what the chapter says Jesus did and said—not later tradition.\n\nSimilar elsewhere:\nJohn 1: Compare with John 1, which immediately precedes this chapter in the same book — notice what events or themes continue or change.\nParallel Gospels: Many events in Matthew, Mark, Luke, and John appear in more than one Gospel with matching or overlapping details. Compare the same episode across Gospels to see what each writer records.","commentary_af":"Vandag se tematiese leeswerk: Johannes 2. Bestudeer elke hoofstuk-afdeling hieronder terwyl jy lees.\n\nJohannes 2\nJohannes 2. Die Evangelies openbaar Jesus — Sy lering, gesag, barmhartigheid en sending. Vra: Wie is Jesus hier, en wat roep Hy my om te glo en te doen? Lees Johannes 2 self en kontroleer elke stelling teen die verse in jou Bybelweergawe.\n\nJesus se identiteit en gesag\nDie teks van Johannes 2 noem of illustreer: Jesus se identiteit en gesag. Lees daardie verse weer en skryf presies op wat die Bybel sê — nie wat jy dink nie.\n\nKoninkryk-lering\nDie teks van Johannes 2 noem of illustreer: Koninkryk-lering. Lees daardie verse weer en skryf presies op wat die Bybel sê — nie wat jy dink nie.\n\nOproepe om te volg\nDie teks van Johannes 2 noem of illustreer: Oproepe om te volg. Lees daardie verse weer en skryf presies op wat die Bybel sê — nie wat jy dink nie.\n\nWhat God wants us to know:\nGod wil hê ons moet weet wie Jesus is en wat Hy mense roep om te glo en te doen deur sy woorde, dade en gesag.\n\nWhy:\nEvangelie-hoofstukke beskryf wat Jesus geleer, genees, beveel of openbaar het. Fokus op wat die hoofstuk sê Jesus gedoen en gesê het.\n\nSimilar elsewhere:\nJohannes 1: Compare with Johannes 1, wat direct voor hierdie hoofstuk kom — let op wat voortgaan of verander.\nParallelle Evangelies: Baie gebeure in Matteus, Markus, Lukas en Johannes verskyn in meer as een Evangelie. Vergelyk dieselfde episode oor Evangelies heen.","questions_en":["What does this passage reveal about God?","What promise, command, or truth stands out to you?","How can you apply this to your life today?"],"questions_af":["Wat openbaar hierdie gedeelte oor God?","Watter belofte, gebod of waarheid val vir jou op?","Hoe kan jy dit vandag in jou lewe toepas?"]},{"day":3,"title_en":"John 3","title_af":"Johannes 3","passages":[{"book_id":43,"chapter":3}],"commentary_intro_en":"Today''s themed reading: John 3. Study each chapter section below as you read.","commentary_intro_af":"Vandag se tematiese leeswerk: Johannes 3. Bestudeer elke hoofstuk-afdeling hieronder terwyl jy lees.","commentary_sections":[{"book_id":43,"chapter":3,"heading_en":"John 3","heading_af":"Johannes 3","summary_en":"Nicodemus visits by night; Jesus teaches born-again necessity. John 3:16 declares God''s love and eternal life through the Son. Read John 3 yourself and verify each statement against the verses in your Bible version.","summary_af":"Nikodemus besoek snags; Jesus leer wedergeboorte-noodsaaklikheid. Johannes 3:16 verklaar God se liefde en ewige lewe deur die Seun. Lees Johannes 3 self en kontroleer elke stelling teen die verse in jou Bybelweergawe.","study_points_en":[{"title":"You must be born again","verses":"","detail":"The text of John 3 records or illustrates: You must be born again. Re-read those verses and note exactly what Scripture states."},{"title":"God so loved the world","verses":"","detail":"The text of John 3 records or illustrates: God so loved the world. Re-read those verses and note exactly what Scripture states."},{"title":"Light vs. darkness","verses":"","detail":"The text of John 3 records or illustrates: Light vs. darkness. Re-read those verses and note exactly what Scripture states."}],"study_points_af":[{"title":"Jy moet weergebore word","verses":"","detail":"Die teks van Johannes 3 noem of illustreer: Jy moet weergebore word. Lees daardie verse weer en skryf presies op wat die Bybel sê — nie wat jy dink nie."},{"title":"God so liefde die wêreld gehad het","verses":"","detail":"Die teks van Johannes 3 noem of illustreer: God so liefde die wêreld gehad het. Lees daardie verse weer en skryf presies op wat die Bybel sê — nie wat jy dink nie."},{"title":"Lig vs. duisternis","verses":"","detail":"Die teks van Johannes 3 noem of illustreer: Lig vs. duisternis. Lees daardie verse weer en skryf presies op wat die Bybel sê — nie wat jy dink nie."}],"teaching_en":"God wants us to know who Jesus is and what he calls people to believe and do through his words, actions, and authority.","teaching_why_en":"Gospel chapters record what Jesus taught, healed, commanded, or revealed about the kingdom. Focus on what the chapter says Jesus did and said—not later tradition.","teaching_af":"God wil hê ons moet weet wie Jesus is en wat Hy mense roep om te glo en te doen deur sy woorde, dade en gesag.","teaching_why_af":"Evangelie-hoofstukke beskryf wat Jesus geleer, genees, beveel of openbaar het. Fokus op wat die hoofstuk sê Jesus gedoen en gesê het.","cross_references_en":[{"ref":"John 3:16","comparison":"John 3 records Jesus telling Nicodemus that God loved the world and gave his Son so believers receive eternal life (v. 16). The same chapter ties new birth (vv. 3–8) to this gift."},{"ref":"Ezekiel 36:26–27","comparison":"Jesus speaks of being born of water and Spirit (John 3:5). Ezekiel 36:26–27 records God promising a new heart and putting his Spirit within — both link inner renewal with God''s Spirit."}],"cross_references_af":[{"ref":"Johannes 3:16","comparison":"Johannes 3 beskryf Jesus wat vir Nikodemus sê God het die wêreld liefgehad en Sy Seun gegee (v. 16). Dieselfde hoofstuk verbind wedergeboorte (vv. 3–8) hiermee."},{"ref":"Esegiël 36:26–27","comparison":"Jesus praat van gebore word uit water en Gees (Joh 3:5). Esegiël 36:26–27 beloof ''n nuwe hart en God se Gees binne-in — beide verbind innerlike vernuwing met God se Gees."}],"highlights_en":["You must be born again","God so loved the world","Light vs. darkness"],"highlights_af":["Jy moet weergebore word","God so liefde die wêreld gehad het","Lig vs. duisternis"]}],"commentary_en":"Today''s themed reading: John 3. Study each chapter section below as you read.\n\nJohn 3\nNicodemus visits by night; Jesus teaches born-again necessity. John 3:16 declares God''s love and eternal life through the Son. Read John 3 yourself and verify each statement against the verses in your Bible version.\n\nYou must be born again\nThe text of John 3 records or illustrates: You must be born again. Re-read those verses and note exactly what Scripture states.\n\nGod so loved the world\nThe text of John 3 records or illustrates: God so loved the world. Re-read those verses and note exactly what Scripture states.\n\nLight vs. darkness\nThe text of John 3 records or illustrates: Light vs. darkness. Re-read those verses and note exactly what Scripture states.\n\nWhat God wants us to know:\nGod wants us to know who Jesus is and what he calls people to believe and do through his words, actions, and authority.\n\nWhy:\nGospel chapters record what Jesus taught, healed, commanded, or revealed about the kingdom. Focus on what the chapter says Jesus did and said—not later tradition.\n\nSimilar elsewhere:\nJohn 3:16: John 3 records Jesus telling Nicodemus that God loved the world and gave his Son so believers receive eternal life (v. 16). The same chapter ties new birth (vv. 3–8) to this gift.\nEzekiel 36:26–27: Jesus speaks of being born of water and Spirit (John 3:5). Ezekiel 36:26–27 records God promising a new heart and putting his Spirit within — both link inner renewal with God''s Spirit.","commentary_af":"Vandag se tematiese leeswerk: Johannes 3. Bestudeer elke hoofstuk-afdeling hieronder terwyl jy lees.\n\nJohannes 3\nNikodemus besoek snags; Jesus leer wedergeboorte-noodsaaklikheid. Johannes 3:16 verklaar God se liefde en ewige lewe deur die Seun. Lees Johannes 3 self en kontroleer elke stelling teen die verse in jou Bybelweergawe.\n\nJy moet weergebore word\nDie teks van Johannes 3 noem of illustreer: Jy moet weergebore word. Lees daardie verse weer en skryf presies op wat die Bybel sê — nie wat jy dink nie.\n\nGod so liefde die wêreld gehad het\nDie teks van Johannes 3 noem of illustreer: God so liefde die wêreld gehad het. Lees daardie verse weer en skryf presies op wat die Bybel sê — nie wat jy dink nie.\n\nLig vs. duisternis\nDie teks van Johannes 3 noem of illustreer: Lig vs. duisternis. Lees daardie verse weer en skryf presies op wat die Bybel sê — nie wat jy dink nie.\n\nWhat God wants us to know:\nGod wil hê ons moet weet wie Jesus is en wat Hy mense roep om te glo en te doen deur sy woorde, dade en gesag.\n\nWhy:\nEvangelie-hoofstukke beskryf wat Jesus geleer, genees, beveel of openbaar het. Fokus op wat die hoofstuk sê Jesus gedoen en gesê het.\n\nSimilar elsewhere:\nJohannes 3:16: Johannes 3 beskryf Jesus wat vir Nikodemus sê God het die wêreld liefgehad en Sy Seun gegee (v. 16). Dieselfde hoofstuk verbind wedergeboorte (vv. 3–8) hiermee.\nEsegiël 36:26–27: Jesus praat van gebore word uit water en Gees (Joh 3:5). Esegiël 36:26–27 beloof ''n nuwe hart en God se Gees binne-in — beide verbind innerlike vernuwing met God se Gees.","questions_en":["What does this passage reveal about God?","What promise, command, or truth stands out to you?","How can you apply this to your life today?"],"questions_af":["Wat openbaar hierdie gedeelte oor God?","Watter belofte, gebod of waarheid val vir jou op?","Hoe kan jy dit vandag in jou lewe toepas?"]},{"day":4,"title_en":"John 4","title_af":"Johannes 4","passages":[{"book_id":43,"chapter":4}],"commentary_intro_en":"Today''s themed reading: John 4. Study each chapter section below as you read.","commentary_intro_af":"Vandag se tematiese leeswerk: Johannes 4. Bestudeer elke hoofstuk-afdeling hieronder terwyl jy lees.","commentary_sections":[{"book_id":43,"chapter":4,"heading_en":"John 4","heading_af":"Johannes 4","summary_en":"John 4. The Gospels reveal Jesus — His teaching, authority, compassion, and mission. Ask: Who is Jesus here, and what is He calling me to believe and do? Read John 4 yourself and verify each statement against the verses in your Bible version.","summary_af":"Johannes 4. Die Evangelies openbaar Jesus — Sy lering, gesag, barmhartigheid en sending. Vra: Wie is Jesus hier, en wat roep Hy my om te glo en te doen? Lees Johannes 4 self en kontroleer elke stelling teen die verse in jou Bybelweergawe.","study_points_en":[{"title":"Jesus'' identity and authority","verses":"","detail":"The text of John 4 records or illustrates: Jesus'' identity and authority. Re-read those verses and note exactly what Scripture states."},{"title":"Kingdom teaching","verses":"","detail":"The text of John 4 records or illustrates: Kingdom teaching. Re-read those verses and note exactly what Scripture states."},{"title":"Calls to follow","verses":"","detail":"The text of John 4 records or illustrates: Calls to follow. Re-read those verses and note exactly what Scripture states."}],"study_points_af":[{"title":"Jesus se identiteit en gesag","verses":"","detail":"Die teks van Johannes 4 noem of illustreer: Jesus se identiteit en gesag. Lees daardie verse weer en skryf presies op wat die Bybel sê — nie wat jy dink nie."},{"title":"Koninkryk-lering","verses":"","detail":"Die teks van Johannes 4 noem of illustreer: Koninkryk-lering. Lees daardie verse weer en skryf presies op wat die Bybel sê — nie wat jy dink nie."},{"title":"Oproepe om te volg","verses":"","detail":"Die teks van Johannes 4 noem of illustreer: Oproepe om te volg. Lees daardie verse weer en skryf presies op wat die Bybel sê — nie wat jy dink nie."}],"teaching_en":"God wants us to know who Jesus is and what he calls people to believe and do through his words, actions, and authority.","teaching_why_en":"Gospel chapters record what Jesus taught, healed, commanded, or revealed about the kingdom. Focus on what the chapter says Jesus did and said—not later tradition.","teaching_af":"God wil hê ons moet weet wie Jesus is en wat Hy mense roep om te glo en te doen deur sy woorde, dade en gesag.","teaching_why_af":"Evangelie-hoofstukke beskryf wat Jesus geleer, genees, beveel of openbaar het. Fokus op wat die hoofstuk sê Jesus gedoen en gesê het.","cross_references_en":[{"ref":"John 3","comparison":"Compare with John 3, which immediately precedes this chapter in the same book — notice what events or themes continue or change."},{"ref":"Parallel Gospels","comparison":"Many events in Matthew, Mark, Luke, and John appear in more than one Gospel with matching or overlapping details. Compare the same episode across Gospels to see what each writer records."}],"cross_references_af":[{"ref":"Johannes 3","comparison":"Compare with Johannes 3, wat direct voor hierdie hoofstuk kom — let op wat voortgaan of verander."},{"ref":"Parallelle Evangelies","comparison":"Baie gebeure in Matteus, Markus, Lukas en Johannes verskyn in meer as een Evangelie. Vergelyk dieselfde episode oor Evangelies heen."}],"highlights_en":["Jesus'' identity and authority","Kingdom teaching","Calls to follow"],"highlights_af":["Jesus se identiteit en gesag","Koninkryk-lering","Oproepe om te volg"]}],"commentary_en":"Today''s themed reading: John 4. Study each chapter section below as you read.\n\nJohn 4\nJohn 4. The Gospels reveal Jesus — His teaching, authority, compassion, and mission. Ask: Who is Jesus here, and what is He calling me to believe and do? Read John 4 yourself and verify each statement against the verses in your Bible version.\n\nJesus'' identity and authority\nThe text of John 4 records or illustrates: Jesus'' identity and authority. Re-read those verses and note exactly what Scripture states.\n\nKingdom teaching\nThe text of John 4 records or illustrates: Kingdom teaching. Re-read those verses and note exactly what Scripture states.\n\nCalls to follow\nThe text of John 4 records or illustrates: Calls to follow. Re-read those verses and note exactly what Scripture states.\n\nWhat God wants us to know:\nGod wants us to know who Jesus is and what he calls people to believe and do through his words, actions, and authority.\n\nWhy:\nGospel chapters record what Jesus taught, healed, commanded, or revealed about the kingdom. Focus on what the chapter says Jesus did and said—not later tradition.\n\nSimilar elsewhere:\nJohn 3: Compare with John 3, which immediately precedes this chapter in the same book — notice what events or themes continue or change.\nParallel Gospels: Many events in Matthew, Mark, Luke, and John appear in more than one Gospel with matching or overlapping details. Compare the same episode across Gospels to see what each writer records.","commentary_af":"Vandag se tematiese leeswerk: Johannes 4. Bestudeer elke hoofstuk-afdeling hieronder terwyl jy lees.\n\nJohannes 4\nJohannes 4. Die Evangelies openbaar Jesus — Sy lering, gesag, barmhartigheid en sending. Vra: Wie is Jesus hier, en wat roep Hy my om te glo en te doen? Lees Johannes 4 self en kontroleer elke stelling teen die verse in jou Bybelweergawe.\n\nJesus se identiteit en gesag\nDie teks van Johannes 4 noem of illustreer: Jesus se identiteit en gesag. Lees daardie verse weer en skryf presies op wat die Bybel sê — nie wat jy dink nie.\n\nKoninkryk-lering\nDie teks van Johannes 4 noem of illustreer: Koninkryk-lering. Lees daardie verse weer en skryf presies op wat die Bybel sê — nie wat jy dink nie.\n\nOproepe om te volg\nDie teks van Johannes 4 noem of illustreer: Oproepe om te volg. Lees daardie verse weer en skryf presies op wat die Bybel sê — nie wat jy dink nie.\n\nWhat God wants us to know:\nGod wil hê ons moet weet wie Jesus is en wat Hy mense roep om te glo en te doen deur sy woorde, dade en gesag.\n\nWhy:\nEvangelie-hoofstukke beskryf wat Jesus geleer, genees, beveel of openbaar het. Fokus op wat die hoofstuk sê Jesus gedoen en gesê het.\n\nSimilar elsewhere:\nJohannes 3: Compare with Johannes 3, wat direct voor hierdie hoofstuk kom — let op wat voortgaan of verander.\nParallelle Evangelies: Baie gebeure in Matteus, Markus, Lukas en Johannes verskyn in meer as een Evangelie. Vergelyk dieselfde episode oor Evangelies heen.","questions_en":["What does this passage reveal about God?","What promise, command, or truth stands out to you?","How can you apply this to your life today?"],"questions_af":["Wat openbaar hierdie gedeelte oor God?","Watter belofte, gebod of waarheid val vir jou op?","Hoe kan jy dit vandag in jou lewe toepas?"]},{"day":5,"title_en":"John 5","title_af":"Johannes 5","passages":[{"book_id":43,"chapter":5}],"commentary_intro_en":"Today''s themed reading: John 5. Study each chapter section below as you read.","commentary_intro_af":"Vandag se tematiese leeswerk: Johannes 5. Bestudeer elke hoofstuk-afdeling hieronder terwyl jy lees.","commentary_sections":[{"book_id":43,"chapter":5,"heading_en":"John 5","heading_af":"Johannes 5","summary_en":"John 5. The Gospels reveal Jesus — His teaching, authority, compassion, and mission. Ask: W