) VALUES (
    'beginner-14',
    'Beginner''s Bible Overview',
    'Beginner se Bybel Oorsig',
    '14 essential chapters to introduce the major themes of the Bible.',
    '14 essensiële hoofstukke om die hoof temas van die Bybel bekend te stel.',
    'A guided introduction with a summary for each essential chapter and why it matters.',
    '''n Begeleide inleiding met ''n opsomming vir elke essensiële hoofstuk en hoekom dit saak maak.',
    14,
    'topic',
    '[{"day":1,"title_en":"In the Beginning","title_af":"In die Begin","passages":[{"book_id":1,"chapter":1}],"commentary_intro_en":"Foundational Bible reading. Each chapter summary explains why this passage matters in the bigger story.","commentary_intro_af":"Grondleggende Bybel leeswerk. Elke hoofstuk-opsomming verduidelik hoekom hierdie gedeelte saak maak in die groter storie.","commentary_sections":[{"book_id":1,"chapter":1,"heading_en":"Genesis 1","heading_af":"Genesis 1","summary_en":"The chapter records God creating the heavens and the earth (v. 1). The earth is first described as formless and empty with darkness over the deep; the Spirit of God moves over the waters (v. 2). Over six days God speaks and creation follows: light separated from darkness (vv. 3–5); sky separating waters (vv. 6–8); dry land, seas, and vegetation (vv. 9–13); sun, moon, and stars (vv. 14–19); sea creatures and birds (vv. 20–23); livestock, creeping things, wild animals, and mankind — male and female — in his image (vv. 24–27). God calls each stage good and mankind very good (v. 31). The account of seventh-day rest continues at the start of chapter 2 (2:2–3).","summary_af":"Die hoofstuk beskryf dat God die hemel en die aarde geskape het (v. 1). Die aarde is eers formlos en leeg met duisternis oor die watervloed; die Gees van God beweeg oor die waters (v. 2). Oor ses dae spreek God en skepping volg: lig (vv. 3–5); hemelruim (vv. 6–8); droë land, see en plante (vv. 9–13); son, maan en sterre (vv. 14–19); seediere en voëls (vv. 20–23); vee, kruipende diere, wilde diere en die mens — man en vrou — na sy beeld (vv. 24–27). God noem elke stap goed en die mens baie goed (v. 31). Op die sewende dag rus God, seën die dag en heilig dit (2:2–3).","study_points_en":[{"title":"Creation by God''s spoken command","verses":"vv. 3, 6, 9, 11, 14, 20, 24, 26","detail":"The text repeatedly records God saying \"Let there be…\" or \"Let the earth bring forth…\" and the item appearing. Light (v. 3), the expanse (v. 6), gathered seas and dry land (v. 9), plants (v. 11), heavenly lights (v. 14), sea life and birds (v. 20), land animals (v. 24), and humans (v. 26) each follow a divine word."},{"title":"God declares creation \"good\"","verses":"vv. 4, 10, 12, 18, 21, 25, 31","detail":"After major stages God sees that it is good (vv. 4, 10, 12, 18, 21, 25). On the sixth day he sees all he made and calls it very good (v. 31). The chapter does not define the word \"good\" but repeats the evaluation at each step."},{"title":"Humanity in God''s image, male and female","verses":"vv. 26–28","detail":"God says \"Let us make man in our image, after our likeness\" (v. 26). They are to be fruitful, multiply, fill the earth, and subdue it; they receive dominion over fish, birds, livestock, and the earth (vv. 26–28). Male and female are both created in his image (v. 27)."},{"title":"Seventh-day rest","verses":"vv. 31–2:3","detail":"After six days of making, God rests on the seventh day from all his work (2:2). He blesses the seventh day and makes it holy because he rested (2:3). The chapter ends with this rest, not with more creation."}],"study_points_af":[{"title":"Skepping deur God se gesproke bevel","verses":"vv. 3, 6, 9, 11, 14, 20, 24, 26","detail":"Die teks beskryf herhaaldelik dat God sê \"Laat daar wees…\" en dit verskyn: lig (v. 3), uitspansel (v. 6), land en see (v. 9), plante (v. 11), hemelliggame (v. 14), seediere en voëls (v. 20), landdiere (v. 24), en mense (v. 26)."},{"title":"God verklaar die skepping \"goed\"","verses":"vv. 4, 10, 12, 18, 21, 25, 31","detail":"Na groot stadia sien God dat dit goed is (vv. 4, 10, 12, 18, 21, 25). Op die sesde dag sien hy alles en noem dit baie goed (v. 31)."},{"title":"Mens na God se beeld, man en vrou","verses":"vv. 26–28","detail":"God sê: \"Laat ons mens maak na ons beeld\" (v. 26). Hulle moet vrugbaar wees, vermeerder, die aarde vul en onderwerping uitoefen (vv. 26–28). Man en vrou is beide na sy beeld geskape (v. 27)."},{"title":"Rus op die sewende dag","verses":"vv. 31–2:3","detail":"Na ses dae rus God op die sewende dag van al sy werk (2:2). Hy seën die dag en heilig dit omdat Hy gerus het (2:3)."}],"teaching_en":"God wants us to know that he alone is the Creator of all things, that what he made is good, and that human beings occupy a unique place as his image-bearers under his rule.","teaching_why_en":"The chapter records no other source of existence except God''s word (vv. 3–26). He repeatedly evaluates creation as \"good\" (vv. 4, 10, 12, 18, 21, 25) and mankind as \"very good\" (v. 31). Humanity receives dominion—not independence from God (vv. 26–28).","teaching_af":"God wil hê ons moet weet dat Hy alleen die Skepper van alle dinge is, dat wat Hy gemaak het goed is, en dat mense ''n unieke plek inneem as sy beeld-draers onder sy heerskappy.","teaching_why_af":"Die hoofstuk beskryf geen andere bron van bestaan as God se woord nie (vv. 3–26). Hy beoordeel herhaaldelik die skepping as \"goed\" (vv. 4, 10, 12, 18, 21, 25) en die mens as \"baie goed\" (v. 31). Die mens ontvang heerskappy—nie onafhanklikheid van God nie (vv. 26–28).","cross_references_en":[{"ref":"John 1:1–3","comparison":"Genesis 1 records God creating by spoken command over six days. John 1 records that \"all things were made through\" the Word who was with God in the beginning. Both tie creation to God''s word — one as narrative, one as prologue."},{"ref":"Psalm 104:1–9","comparison":"Psalm 104 praises God for stretching out the heavens, setting the earth on its foundations, and bounding the waters — themes that parallel Genesis 1:6–10 where God separates waters and forms dry land."},{"ref":"Exodus 20:11","comparison":"The Sabbath command in Exodus 20:11 points back to Genesis 1, stating that in six days the Lord made heaven, earth, and sea and rested the seventh day — the same six-plus-one pattern Genesis 1 narrates."}],"cross_references_af":[{"ref":"Johannes 1:1–3","comparison":"Genesis 1 beskryf God wat deur gesproke bevel oor ses dae skep. Johannes 1 sê dat \"alle dinge deur die Woord\" gemaak is wat in die begin by God was. Beide verbind skepping met God se woord."},{"ref":"Psalm 104:1–9","comparison":"Psalm 104 prys God wat die hemel uitsprei, die aarde op fondamente stel en waters begrens — temas wat ooreenstem met Genesis 1:6–10 waar God waters skei en droë grond vorm."},{"ref":"Exodus 20:11","comparison":"Die Sabbatgebod in Exodus 20:11 verwys terug na Genesis 1 en sê dat die Here in ses dae hemel, aarde en see gemaak het en die sewende dag gerus het — dieselfde ses-plus-een patroon as Genesis 1."}],"highlights_en":["Creation by God''s spoken command","God declares creation \"good\"","Humanity in God''s image, male and female","Seventh-day rest"],"highlights_af":["Skepping deur God se gesproke bevel","God verklaar die skepping \"goed\"","Mens na God se beeld, man en vrou","Rus op die sewende dag"]}],"commentary_en":"Foundational Bible reading. Each chapter summary explains why this passage matters in the bigger story.\n\nGenesis 1\nThe chapter records God creating the heavens and the earth (v. 1). The earth is first described as formless and empty with darkness over the deep; the Spirit of God moves over the waters (v. 2). Over six days God speaks and creation follows: light separated from darkness (vv. 3–5); sky separating waters (vv. 6–8); dry land, seas, and vegetation (vv. 9–13); sun, moon, and stars (vv. 14–19); sea creatures and birds (vv. 20–23); livestock, creeping things, wild animals, and mankind — male and female — in his image (vv. 24–27). God calls each stage good and mankind very good (v. 31). The account of seventh-day rest continues at the start of chapter 2 (2:2–3).\n\nCreation by God''s spoken command [vv. 3, 6, 9, 11, 14, 20, 24, 26]\nThe text repeatedly records God saying \"Let there be…\" or \"Let the earth bring forth…\" and the item appearing. Light (v. 3), the expanse (v. 6), gathered seas and dry land (v. 9), plants (v. 11), heavenly lights (v. 14), sea life and birds (v. 20), land animals (v. 24), and humans (v. 26) each follow a divine word.\n\nGod declares creation \"good\" [vv. 4, 10, 12, 18, 21, 25, 31]\nAfter major stages God sees that it is good (vv. 4, 10, 12, 18, 21, 25). On the sixth day he sees all he made and calls it very good (v. 31). The chapter does not define the word \"good\" but repeats the evaluation at each step.\n\nHumanity in God''s image, male and female [vv. 26–28]\nGod says \"Let us make man in our image, after our likeness\" (v. 26). They are to be fruitful, multiply, fill the earth, and subdue it; they receive dominion over fish, birds, livestock, and the earth (vv. 26–28). Male and female are both created in his image (v. 27).\n\nSeventh-day rest [vv. 31–2:3]\nAfter six days of making, God rests on the seventh day from all his work (2:2). He blesses the seventh day and makes it holy because he rested (2:3). The chapter ends with this rest, not with more creation.\n\nWhat God wants us to know:\nGod wants us to know that he alone is the Creator of all things, that what he made is good, and that human beings occupy a unique place as his image-bearers under his rule.\n\nWhy:\nThe chapter records no other source of existence except God''s word (vv. 3–26). He repeatedly evaluates creation as \"good\" (vv. 4, 10, 12, 18, 21, 25) and mankind as \"very good\" (v. 31). Humanity receives dominion—not independence from God (vv. 26–28).\n\nSimilar elsewhere:\nJohn 1:1–3: Genesis 1 records God creating by spoken command over six days. John 1 records that \"all things were made through\" the Word who was with God in the beginning. Both tie creation to God''s word — one as narrative, one as prologue.\nPsalm 104:1–9: Psalm 104 praises God for stretching out the heavens, setting the earth on its foundations, and bounding the waters — themes that parallel Genesis 1:6–10 where God separates waters and forms dry land.\nExodus 20:11: The Sabbath command in Exodus 20:11 points back to Genesis 1, stating that in six days the Lord made heaven, earth, and sea and rested the seventh day — the same six-plus-one pattern Genesis 1 narrates.","commentary_af":"Grondleggende Bybel leeswerk. Elke hoofstuk-opsomming verduidelik hoekom hierdie gedeelte saak maak in die groter storie.\n\nGenesis 1\nDie hoofstuk beskryf dat God die hemel en die aarde geskape het (v. 1). Die aarde is eers formlos en leeg met duisternis oor die watervloed; die Gees van God beweeg oor die waters (v. 2). Oor ses dae spreek God en skepping volg: lig (vv. 3–5); hemelruim (vv. 6–8); droë land, see en plante (vv. 9–13); son, maan en sterre (vv. 14–19); seediere en voëls (vv. 20–23); vee, kruipende diere, wilde diere en die mens — man en vrou — na sy beeld (vv. 24–27). God noem elke stap goed en die mens baie goed (v. 31). Op die sewende dag rus God, seën die dag en heilig dit (2:2–3).\n\nSkepping deur God se gesproke bevel [vv. 3, 6, 9, 11, 14, 20, 24, 26]\nDie teks beskryf herhaaldelik dat God sê \"Laat daar wees…\" en dit verskyn: lig (v. 3), uitspansel (v. 6), land en see (v. 9), plante (v. 11), hemelliggame (v. 14), seediere en voëls (v. 20), landdiere (v. 24), en mense (v. 26).\n\nGod verklaar die skepping \"goed\" [vv. 4, 10, 12, 18, 21, 25, 31]\nNa groot stadia sien God dat dit goed is (vv. 4, 10, 12, 18, 21, 25). Op die sesde dag sien hy alles en noem dit baie goed (v. 31).\n\nMens na God se beeld, man en vrou [vv. 26–28]\nGod sê: \"Laat ons mens maak na ons beeld\" (v. 26). Hulle moet vrugbaar wees, vermeerder, die aarde vul en onderwerping uitoefen (vv. 26–28). Man en vrou is beide na sy beeld geskape (v. 27).\n\nRus op die sewende dag [vv. 31–2:3]\nNa ses dae rus God op die sewende dag van al sy werk (2:2). Hy seën die dag en heilig dit omdat Hy gerus het (2:3).\n\nWhat God wants us to know:\nGod wil hê ons moet weet dat Hy alleen die Skepper van alle dinge is, dat wat Hy gemaak het goed is, en dat mense ''n unieke plek inneem as sy beeld-draers onder sy heerskappy.\n\nWhy:\nDie hoofstuk beskryf geen andere bron van bestaan as God se woord nie (vv. 3–26). Hy beoordeel herhaaldelik die skepping as \"goed\" (vv. 4, 10, 12, 18, 21, 25) en die mens as \"baie goed\" (v. 31). Die mens ontvang heerskappy—nie onafhanklikheid van God nie (vv. 26–28).\n\nSimilar elsewhere:\nJohannes 1:1–3: Genesis 1 beskryf God wat deur gesproke bevel oor ses dae skep. Johannes 1 sê dat \"alle dinge deur die Woord\" gemaak is wat in die begin by God was. Beide verbind skepping met God se woord.\nPsalm 104:1–9: Psalm 104 prys God wat die hemel uitsprei, die aarde op fondamente stel en waters begrens — temas wat ooreenstem met Genesis 1:6–10 waar God waters skei en droë grond vorm.\nExodus 20:11: Die Sabbatgebod in Exodus 20:11 verwys terug na Genesis 1 en sê dat die Here in ses dae hemel, aarde en see gemaak het en die sewende dag gerus het — dieselfde ses-plus-een patroon as Genesis 1.","questions_en":["What does this passage reveal about God?","What promise, command, or truth stands out to you?","How can you apply this to your life today?"],"questions_af":["Wat openbaar hierdie gedeelte oor God?","Watter belofte, gebod of waarheid val vir jou op?","Hoe kan jy dit vandag in jou lewe toepas?"]},{"day":2,"title_en":"The Word Became Flesh","title_af":"Die Woord Word Vlees","passages":[{"book_id":43,"chapter":1}],"commentary_intro_en":"Foundational Bible reading. Each chapter summary explains why this passage matters in the bigger story.","commentary_intro_af":"Grondleggende Bybel leeswerk. Elke hoofstuk-opsomming verduidelik hoekom hierdie gedeelte saak maak in die groter storie.","commentary_sections":[{"book_id":43,"chapter":1,"heading_en":"John 1","heading_af":"Johannes 1","summary_en":"John opens with the eternal Word — Jesus as Creator and Light. John the Baptist prepares the way; Jesus calls the first disciples. Read John 1 yourself and verify each statement against the verses in your Bible version.","summary_af":"Johannes open met die ewige Woord — Jesus as Skepper en Lig. Johannes die Doper berei die pad; Jesus roep die eerste dissipels. Lees Johannes 1 self en kontroleer elke stelling teen die verse in jou Bybelweergawe.","study_points_en":[{"title":"In the beginning was the Word","verses":"","detail":"The text of John 1 records or illustrates: In the beginning was the Word. Re-read those verses and note exactly what Scripture states."},{"title":"Light shines in darkness","verses":"","detail":"The text of John 1 records or illustrates: Light shines in darkness. Re-read those verses and note exactly what Scripture states."},{"title":"Come and see","verses":"","detail":"The text of John 1 records or illustrates: Come and see. Re-read those verses and note exactly what Scripture states."}],"study_points_af":[{"title":"In die begin was die Woord","verses":"","detail":"Die teks van Johannes 1 noem of illustreer: In die begin was die Woord. Lees daardie verse weer en skryf presies op wat die Bybel sê — nie wat jy dink nie."},{"title":"Lig skyn in duisternis","verses":"","detail":"Die teks van Johannes 1 noem of illustreer: Lig skyn in duisternis. Lees daardie verse weer en skryf presies op wat die Bybel sê — nie wat jy dink nie."},{"title":"Kom en sien","verses":"","detail":"Die teks van Johannes 1 noem of illustreer: Kom en sien. Lees daardie verse weer en skryf presies op wat die Bybel sê — nie wat jy dink nie."}],"teaching_en":"God wants us to know who Jesus is and what he calls people to believe and do through his words, actions, and authority.","teaching_why_en":"Gospel chapters record what Jesus taught, healed, commanded, or revealed about the kingdom. Focus on what the chapter says Jesus did and said—not later tradition.","teaching_af":"God wil hê ons moet weet wie Jesus is en wat Hy mense roep om te glo en te doen deur sy woorde, dade en gesag.","teaching_why_af":"Evangelie-hoofstukke beskryf wat Jesus geleer, genees, beveel of openbaar het. Fokus op wat die hoofstuk sê Jesus gedoen en gesê het.","cross_references_en":[{"ref":"Parallel Gospels","comparison":"Many events in Matthew, Mark, Luke, and John appear in more than one Gospel with matching or overlapping details. Compare the same episode across Gospels to see what each writer records."}],"cross_references_af":[{"ref":"Parallelle Evangelies","comparison":"Baie gebeure in Matteus, Markus, Lukas en Johannes verskyn in meer as een Evangelie. Vergelyk dieselfde episode oor Evangelies heen."}],"highlights_en":["In the beginning was the Word","Light shines in darkness","Come and see"],"highlights_af":["In die begin was die Woord","Lig skyn in duisternis","Kom en sien"]}],"commentary_en":"Foundational Bible reading. Each chapter summary explains why this passage matters in the bigger story.\n\nJohn 1\nJohn opens with the eternal Word — Jesus as Creator and Light. John the Baptist prepares the way; Jesus calls the first disciples. Read John 1 yourself and verify each statement against the verses in your Bible version.\n\nIn the beginning was the Word\nThe text of John 1 records or illustrates: In the beginning was the Word. Re-read those verses and note exactly what Scripture states.\n\nLight shines in darkness\nThe text of John 1 records or illustrates: Light shines in darkness. Re-read those verses and note exactly what Scripture states.\n\nCome and see\nThe text of John 1 records or illustrates: Come and see. Re-read those verses and note exactly what Scripture states.\n\nWhat God wants us to know:\nGod wants us to know who Jesus is and what he calls people to believe and do through his words, actions, and authority.\n\nWhy:\nGospel chapters record what Jesus taught, healed, commanded, or revealed about the kingdom. Focus on what the chapter says Jesus did and said—not later tradition.\n\nSimilar elsewhere:\nParallel Gospels: Many events in Matthew, Mark, Luke, and John appear in more than one Gospel with matching or overlapping details. Compare the same episode across Gospels to see what each writer records.","commentary_af":"Grondleggende Bybel leeswerk. Elke hoofstuk-opsomming verduidelik hoekom hierdie gedeelte saak maak in die groter storie.\n\nJohannes 1\nJohannes open met die ewige Woord — Jesus as Skepper en Lig. Johannes die Doper berei die pad; Jesus roep die eerste dissipels. Lees Johannes 1 self en kontroleer elke stelling teen die verse in jou Bybelweergawe.\n\nIn die begin was die Woord\nDie teks van Johannes 1 noem of illustreer: In die begin was die Woord. Lees daardie verse weer en skryf presies op wat die Bybel sê — nie wat jy dink nie.\n\nLig skyn in duisternis\nDie teks van Johannes 1 noem of illustreer: Lig skyn in duisternis. Lees daardie verse weer en skryf presies op wat die Bybel sê — nie wat jy dink nie.\n\nKom en sien\nDie teks van Johannes 1 noem of illustreer: Kom en sien. Lees daardie verse weer en skryf presies op wat die Bybel sê — nie wat jy dink nie.\n\nWhat God wants us to know:\nGod wil hê ons moet weet wie Jesus is en wat Hy mense roep om te glo en te doen deur sy woorde, dade en gesag.\n\nWhy:\nEvangelie-hoofstukke beskryf wat Jesus geleer, genees, beveel of openbaar het. Fokus op wat die hoofstuk sê Jesus gedoen en gesê het.\n\nSimilar elsewhere:\nParallelle Evangelies: Baie gebeure in Matteus, Markus, Lukas en Johannes verskyn in meer as een Evangelie. Vergelyk dieselfde episode oor Evangelies heen.","questions_en":["What does this passage reveal about God?","What promise, command, or truth stands out to you?","How can you apply this to your life today?"],"questions_af":["Wat openbaar hierdie gedeelte oor God?","Watter belofte, gebod of waarheid val vir jou op?","Hoe kan jy dit vandag in jou lewe toepas?"]},{"day":3,"title_en":"God So Loved the World","title_af":"God So Die Wêreld Liefgehad Het","passages":[{"book_id":43,"chapter":3}],"commentary_intro_en":"Foundational Bible reading. Each chapter summary explains why this passage matters in the bigger story.","commentary_intro_af":"Grondleggende Bybel leeswerk. Elke hoofstuk-opsomming verduidelik hoekom hierdie gedeelte saak maak in die groter storie.","commentary_sections":[{"book_id":43,"chapter":3,"heading_en":"John 3","heading_af":"Johannes 3","summary_en":"Nicodemus visits by night; Jesus teaches born-again necessity. John 3:16 declares God''s love and eternal life through the Son. Read John 3 yourself and verify each statement against the verses in your Bible version.","summary_af":"Nikodemus besoek snags; Jesus leer wedergeboorte-noodsaaklikheid. Johannes 3:16 verklaar God se liefde en ewige lewe deur die Seun. Lees Johannes 3 self en kontroleer elke stelling teen die verse in jou Bybelweergawe.","study_points_en":[{"title":"You must be born again","verses":"","detail":"The text of John 3 records or illustrates: You must be born again. Re-read those verses and note exactly what Scripture states."},{"title":"God so loved the world","verses":"","detail":"The text of John 3 records or illustrates: God so loved the world. Re-read those verses and note exactly what Scripture states."},{"title":"Light vs. darkness","verses":"","detail":"The text of John 3 records or illustrates: Light vs. darkness. Re-read those verses and note exactly what Scripture states."}],"study_points_af":[{"title":"Jy moet weergebore word","verses":"","detail":"Die teks van Johannes 3 noem of illustreer: Jy moet weergebore word. Lees daardie verse weer en skryf presies op wat die Bybel sê — nie wat jy dink nie."},{"title":"God so liefde die wêreld gehad het","verses":"","detail":"Die teks van Johannes 3 noem of illustreer: God so liefde die wêreld gehad het. Lees daardie verse weer en skryf presies op wat die Bybel sê — nie wat jy dink nie."},{"title":"Lig vs. duisternis","verses":"","detail":"Die teks van Johannes 3 noem of illustreer: Lig vs. duisternis. Lees daardie verse weer en skryf presies op wat die Bybel sê — nie wat jy dink nie."}],"teaching_en":"God wants us to know who Jesus is and what he calls people to believe and do through his words, actions, and authority.","teaching_why_en":"Gospel chapters record what Jesus taught, healed, commanded, or revealed about the kingdom. Focus on what the chapter says Jesus did and said—not later tradition.","teaching_af":"God wil hê ons moet weet wie Jesus is en wat Hy mense roep om te glo en te doen deur sy woorde, dade en gesag.","teaching_why_af":"Evangelie-hoofstukke beskryf wat Jesus geleer, genees, beveel of openbaar het. Fokus op wat die hoofstuk sê Jesus gedoen en gesê het.","cross_references_en":[{"ref":"John 3:16","comparison":"John 3 records Jesus telling Nicodemus that God loved the world and gave his Son so believers receive eternal life (v. 16). The same chapter ties new birth (vv. 3–8) to this gift."},{"ref":"Ezekiel 36:26–27","comparison":"Jesus speaks of being born of water and Spirit (John 3:5). Ezekiel 36:26–27 records God promising a new heart and putting his Spirit within — both link inner renewal with God''s Spirit."}],"cross_references_af":[{"ref":"Johannes 3:16","comparison":"Johannes 3 beskryf Jesus wat vir Nikodemus sê God het die wêreld liefgehad en Sy Seun gegee (v. 16). Dieselfde hoofstuk verbind wedergeboorte (vv. 3–8) hiermee."},{"ref":"Esegiël 36:26–27","comparison":"Jesus praat van gebore word uit water en Gees (Joh 3:5). Esegiël 36:26–27 beloof ''n nuwe hart en God se Gees binne-in — beide verbind innerlike vernuwing met God se Gees."}],"highlights_en":["You must be born again","God so loved the world","Light vs. darkness"],"highlights_af":["Jy moet weergebore word","God so liefde die wêreld gehad het","Lig vs. duisternis"]}],"commentary_en":"Foundational Bible reading. Each chapter summary explains why this passage matters in the bigger story.\n\nJohn 3\nNicodemus visits by night; Jesus teaches born-again necessity. John 3:16 declares God''s love and eternal life through the Son. Read John 3 yourself and verify each statement against the verses in your Bible version.\n\nYou must be born again\nThe text of John 3 records or illustrates: You must be born again. Re-read those verses and note exactly what Scripture states.\n\nGod so loved the world\nThe text of John 3 records or illustrates: God so loved the world. Re-read those verses and note exactly what Scripture states.\n\nLight vs. darkness\nThe text of John 3 records or illustrates: Light vs. darkness. Re-read those verses and note exactly what Scripture states.\n\nWhat God wants us to know:\nGod wants us to know who Jesus is and what he calls people to believe and do through his words, actions, and authority.\n\nWhy:\nGospel chapters record what Jesus taught, healed, commanded, or revealed about the kingdom. Focus on what the chapter says Jesus did and said—not later tradition.\n\nSimilar elsewhere:\nJohn 3:16: John 3 records Jesus telling Nicodemus that God loved the world and gave his Son so believers receive eternal life (v. 16). The same chapter ties new birth (vv. 3–8) to this gift.\nEzekiel 36:26–27: Jesus speaks of being born of water and Spirit (John 3:5). Ezekiel 36:26–27 records God promising a new heart and putting his Spirit within — both link inner renewal with God''s Spirit.","commentary_af":"Grondleggende Bybel leeswerk. Elke hoofstuk-opsomming verduidelik hoekom hierdie gedeelte saak maak in die groter storie.\n\nJohannes 3\nNikodemus besoek snags; Jesus leer wedergeboorte-noodsaaklikheid. Johannes 3:16 verklaar God se liefde en ewige lewe deur die Seun. Lees Johannes 3 self en kontroleer elke stelling teen die verse in jou Bybelweergawe.\n\nJy moet weergebore word\nDie teks van Johannes 3 noem of illustreer: Jy moet weergebore word. Lees daardie verse weer en skryf presies op wat die Bybel sê — nie wat jy dink nie.\n\nGod so liefde die wêreld gehad het\nDie teks van Johannes 3 noem of illustreer: God so liefde die wêreld gehad het. Lees daardie verse weer en skryf presies op wat die Bybel sê — nie wat jy dink nie.\n\nLig vs. duisternis\nDie teks van Johannes 3 noem of illustreer: Lig vs. duisternis. Lees daardie verse weer en skryf presies op wat die Bybel sê — nie wat jy dink nie.\n\nWhat God wants us to know:\nGod wil hê ons moet weet wie Jesus is en wat Hy mense roep om te glo en te doen deur sy woorde, dade en gesag.\n\nWhy:\nEvangelie-hoofstukke beskryf wat Jesus geleer, genees, beveel of openbaar het. Fokus op wat die hoofstuk sê Jesus gedoen en gesê het.\n\nSimilar elsewhere:\nJohannes 3:16: Johannes 3 beskryf Jesus wat vir Nikodemus sê God het die wêreld liefgehad en Sy Seun gegee (v. 16). Dieselfde hoofstuk verbind wedergeboorte (vv. 3–8) hiermee.\nEsegiël 36:26–27: Jesus praat van gebore word uit water en Gees (Joh 3:5). Esegiël 36:26–27 beloof ''n nuwe hart en God se Gees binne-in — beide verbind innerlike vernuwing met God se Gees.","questions_en":["What does this passage reveal about God?","What promise, command, or truth stands out to you?","How can you apply this to your life today?"],"questions_af":["Wat openbaar hierdie gedeelte oor God?","Watter belofte, gebod of waarheid val vir jou op?","Hoe kan jy dit vandag in jou lewe toepas?"]},{"day":4,"title_en":"The Lord Is My Shepherd","title_af":"Die Here Is My Herder","passages":[{"book_id":19,"chapter":23}],"commentary_intro_en":"Foundational Bible reading. Each chapter summary explains why this passage matters in the bigger story.","commentary_intro_af":"Grondleggende Bybel leeswerk. Elke hoofstuk-opsomming verduidelik hoekom hierdie gedeelte saak maak in die groter storie.","commentary_sections":[{"book_id":19,"chapter":23,"heading_en":"Psalms 23","heading_af":"Psalms 23","summary_en":"The Lord is my shepherd — provision, guidance, protection, and dwelling in God''s house forever. Read Psalms 23 yourself and verify each statement against the verses in your Bible version.","summary_af":"Die Here is my Herder — voorsiening, leiding, beskerming en woning in God se huis vir altyd. Lees Psalms 23 self en kontroleer elke stelling teen die verse in jou Bybelweergawe.","study_points_en":[{"title":"The Lord shepherds me","verses":"","detail":"The text of Psalms 23 records or illustrates: The Lord shepherds me. Re-read those verses and note exactly what Scripture states."},{"title":"Valley of shadow — fear no evil","verses":"","detail":"The text of Psalms 23 records or illustrates: Valley of shadow — fear no evil. Re-read those verses and note exactly what Scripture states."},{"title":"Goodness and mercy follow","verses":"","detail":"The text of Psalms 23 records or illustrates: Goodness and mercy follow. Re-read those verses and note exactly what Scripture states."}],"study_points_af":[{"title":"Die Here weid my","verses":"","detail":"Die teks van Psalms 23 noem of illustreer: Die Here weid my. Lees daardie verse weer en skryf presies op wat die Bybel sê — nie wat jy dink nie."},{"title":"Skaduwee-vallei — geen vrees","verses":"","detail":"Die teks van Psalms 23 noem of illustreer: Skaduwee-vallei — geen vrees. Lees daardie verse weer en skryf presies op wat die Bybel sê — nie wat jy dink nie."},{"title":"Goedertierenheid en barmhartigheid volg","verses":"","detail":"Die teks van Psalms 23 noem of illustreer: Goedertierenheid en barmhartigheid volg. Lees daardie verse weer en skryf presies op wat die Bybel sê — nie wat jy dink nie."}],"teaching_en":"God wants us to know that true wisdom begins with reverence for him and shapes daily choices, speech, and worship.","teaching_why_en":"Wisdom passages tie understanding to the fear of the Lord and practical living. Notice commands, prayers, or counsel in this chapter and what attitude toward God they assume.","teaching_af":"God wil hê ons moet weet dat ware wysheid begin met eerbied vir Hom en daaglikse keuses, spraak en aanbidding vorm.","teaching_why_af":"Wysheid verbind insig met die vrees vir die Here. Let op gebooie, gebede of raad in hierdie hoofstuk en watter houding teenoor God dit veronderstel.","cross_references_en":[{"ref":"John 10:11","comparison":"Psalm 23:1 says \"The Lord is my shepherd.\" John 10:11 records Jesus saying \"I am the good shepherd.\" Both use shepherd language — one in a psalm, one in Jesus'' speech."},{"ref":"Revelation 7:17","comparison":"Psalm 23 speaks of the Lord shepherding and dwelling with the psalmist. Revelation 7:17 says the Lamb will shepherd and lead to living waters — similar shepherd-and-guidance imagery."}],"cross_references_af":[{"ref":"Johannes 10:11","comparison":"Psalm 23:1 sê \"Die Here is my Herder.\" Johannes 10:11 beskryf Jesus wat sê \"Ek is die goeie Herder.\" Beide gebruik herder-taal."},{"ref":"Openbaring 7:17","comparison":"Psalm 23 praat van die Here as Herder. Openbaring 7:17 sê die Lam sal weid en lei na lewende waters — soortgelyke herder-beeld."}],"highlights_en":["The Lord shepherds me","Valley of shadow — fear no evil","Goodness and mercy follow"],"highlights_af":["Die Here weid my","Skaduwee-vallei — geen vrees","Goedertierenheid en barmhartigheid volg"]}],"commentary_en":"Foundational Bible reading. Each chapter summary explains why this passage matters in the bigger story.\n\nPsalms 23\nThe Lord is my shepherd — provision, guidance, protection, and dwelling in God''s house forever. Read Psalms 23 yourself and verify each statement against the verses in your Bible version.\n\nThe Lord shepherds me\nThe text of Psalms 23 records or illustrates: The Lord shepherds me. Re-read those verses and note exactly what Scripture states.\n\nValley of shadow — fear no evil\nThe text of Psalms 23 records or illustrates: Valley of shadow — fear no evil. Re-read those verses and note exactly what Scripture states.\n\nGoodness and mercy follow\nThe text of Psalms 23 records or illustrates: Goodness and mercy follow. Re-read those verses and note exactly what Scripture states.\n\nWhat God wants us to know:\nGod wants us to know that true wisdom begins with reverence for him and shapes daily choices, speech, and worship.\n\nWhy:\nWisdom passages tie understanding to the fear of the Lord and practical living. Notice commands, prayers, or counsel in this chapter and what attitude toward God they assume.\n\nSimilar elsewhere:\nJohn 10:11: Psalm 23:1 says \"The Lord is my shepherd.\" John 10:11 records Jesus saying \"I am the good shepherd.\" Both use shepherd language — one in a psalm, one in Jesus'' speech.\nRevelation 7:17: Psalm 23 speaks of the Lord shepherding and dwelling with the psalmist. Revelation 7:17 says the Lamb will shepherd and lead to living waters — similar shepherd-and-guidance imagery.","commentary_af":"Grondleggende Bybel leeswerk. Elke hoofstuk-opsomming verduidelik hoekom hierdie gedeelte saak maak in die groter storie.\n\nPsalms 23\nDie Here is my Herder — voorsiening, leiding, beskerming en woning in God se huis vir altyd. Lees Psalms 23 self en kontroleer elke stelling teen die verse in jou Bybelweergawe.\n\nDie Here weid my\nDie teks van Psalms 23 noem of illustreer: Die Here weid my. Lees daardie verse weer en skryf presies op wat die Bybel sê — nie wat jy dink nie.\n\nSkaduwee-vallei — geen vrees\nDie teks van Psalms 23 noem of illustreer: Skaduwee-vallei — geen vrees. Lees daardie verse weer en skryf presies op wat die Bybel sê — nie wat jy dink nie.\n\nGoedertierenheid en barmhartigheid volg\nDie teks van Psalms 23 noem of illustreer: Goedertierenheid en barmhartigheid volg. Lees daardie verse weer en skryf presies op wat die Bybel sê — nie wat jy dink nie.\n\nWhat God wants us to know:\nGod wil hê ons moet weet dat ware wysheid begin met eerbied vir Hom en daaglikse keuses, spraak en aanbidding vorm.\n\nWhy:\nWysheid verbind insig met die vrees vir die Here. Let op gebooie, gebede of raad in hierdie hoofstuk en watter houding teenoor God dit veronderstel.\n\nSimilar elsewhere:\nJohannes 10:11: Psalm 23:1 sê \"Die Here is my Herder.\" Johannes 10:11 beskryf Jesus wat sê \"Ek is die goeie Herder.\" Beide gebruik herder-taal.\nOpenbaring 7:17: Psalm 23 praat van die Here as Herder. Openbaring 7:17 sê die Lam sal weid en lei na lewende waters — soortgelyke herder-beeld.","questions_en":["What does this passage reveal about God?","What promise, command, or truth stands out to you?","How can you apply this to your life today?"],"questions_af":["Wat openbaar hierdie gedeelte oor God?","Watter belofte, gebod of waarheid val vir jou op?","Hoe kan jy dit vandag in jou lewe toepas?"]},{"day":5,"title_en":"No Condemnation in Christ","title_af":"Geen Verdoemenis in Christus","passages":[{"book_id":45,"chapter":8}],"commentary_intro_en":"Foundational Bible reading. Each chapter summary explains why this passage matters in the bigger story.","commentary_intro_af":"Grondleggende Bybel leeswerk. Elke hoofstuk-opsomming verduidelik hoekom hierdie gedeelte saak maak in die groter storie.","commentary_sections":[{"book_id":45,"chapter":8,"heading_en":"Romans 8","heading_af":"Romeine 8","summary_en":"No condemnation for those in Christ. Life in the Spirit vs. flesh. All things work together; nothing separates from God''s love. Read Romans 8 yourself and verify each statement against the verses in your Bible version.","summary_af":"Geen veroordeling vir die wat in Christus is. Lewe in die Gees vs. vlees. Alles werk saam; niks skei van God se liefde. Lees Romeine 8 self en kontroleer elke stelling teen die verse in jou Bybelweergawe.","study_points_en":[{"title":"No condemnation in Christ","verses":"","detail":"The text of Romans 8 records or illustrates: No condemnation in Christ. Re-read those verses and note exactly what Scripture states."},{"title":"Spirit gives life","verses":"","detail":"The text of Romans 8 records or illustrates: Spirit gives life. Re-read those verses and note exactly what Scripture states."},{"title":"Nothing can separate us from love","verses":"","detail":"The text of Romans 8 records or illustrates: Nothing can separate us from love. Re-read those verses and note exactly what Scripture states."}],"study_points_af":[{"title":"Geen veroordeling in Christus","verses":"","detail":"Die teks van Romeine 8 noem of illustreer: Geen veroordeling in Christus. Lees daardie verse weer en skryf presies op wat die Bybel sê — nie wat jy dink nie."},{"title":"Gees gee lewe","verses":"","detail":"Die teks van Romeine 8 noem of illustreer: Gees gee lewe. Lees daardie verse weer en skryf presies op wat die Bybel sê — nie wat jy dink nie."},{"title":"Niks kan ons van liefde skei","verses":"","detail":"Die teks van Romeine 8 noem of illustreer: Niks kan ons van liefde skei. Lees daardie verse weer en skryf presies op wat die Bybel sê — nie wat jy dink nie."}],"teaching_en":"God wants believers to know gospel truth and how it should shape church life, holiness, and love for others.","teaching_why_en":"Paul''s letters argue from what Christ has done to how Christians should live. Find the doctrinal statement in this chapter and the conduct it connects to.","teaching_af":"God wil gelowiges laat weet evangelie-waarheid en hoe dit kerklewe, heiligheid en liefde moet vorm.","teaching_why_af":"Paulus redeneer van wat Christus gedoen het na hoe Christene moet leef. Soek die leerstelling in hierdie hoofstuk en die lewe wat dit verbind.","cross_references_en":[{"ref":"Romans 8:1","comparison":"Romans 8:1 states there is no condemnation for those in Christ Jesus. Romans 8:2–4 contrasts life in the Spirit with the law of sin and death — continuing the same argument in one chapter."},{"ref":"John 5:24","comparison":"Romans 8:1 speaks of no condemnation for those in Christ. John 5:24 records Jesus saying whoever hears and believes has eternal life and does not come into judgment — similar no-condemnation language."}],"cross_references_af":[{"ref":"Romeine 8:1","comparison":"Romeine 8:1 sê daar is geen veroordeling vir die wat in Christus Jesus is nie. Romeine 8:2–4 kontrasteer lewe in die Gees met die wet van sonde en dood."},{"ref":"Johannes 5:24","comparison":"Romeine 8:1 spreek van geen veroordeling vir die in Christus nie. Johannes 5:24 beskryf Jesus wat sê wie hoor en glo het ewige lewe en nie in veroordeling kom nie."}],"highlights_en":["No condemnation in Christ","Spirit gives life","Nothing can separate us from love"],"highlights_af":["Geen veroordeling in Christus","Gees gee lewe","Niks kan ons van liefde skei"]}],"commentary_en":"Foundational Bible reading. Each chapter summary explains why this passage matters in the bigger story.\n\nRomans 8\nNo condemnation for those in Christ. Life in the Spirit vs. flesh. All things work together; nothing separates from God''s love. Read Romans 8 yourself and verify each statement against the verses in your Bible version.\n\nNo condemnation in Christ\nThe text of Romans 8 records or illustrates: No condemnation in Christ. Re-read those verses and note exactly what Scripture states.\n\nSpirit gives life\nThe text of Romans 8 records or illustrates: Spirit gives life. Re-read those verses and note exactly what Scripture states.\n\nNothing can separate us from love\nThe text of Romans 8 records or illustrates: Nothing can separate us from love. Re-read those verses and note exactly what Scripture states.\n\nWhat God wants us to know:\nGod wants believers to know gospel truth and how it should shape church life, holiness, and love for others.\n\nWhy:\nPaul''s letters argue from what Christ has done to how Christians should live. Find the doctrinal statement in this chapter and the conduct it connects to.\n\nSimilar elsewhere:\nRomans 8:1: Romans 8:1 states there is no condemnation for those in Christ Jesus. Romans 8:2–4 contrasts life in the Spirit with the law of sin and death — continuing the same argument in one chapter.\nJohn 5:24: Romans 8:1 speaks of no condemnation for those in Christ. John 5:24 records Jesus saying whoever hears and believes has eternal life and does not come into judgment — similar no-condemnation language.","commentary_af":"Grondleggende Bybel leeswerk. Elke hoofstuk-opsomming verduidelik hoekom hierdie gedeelte saak maak in die groter storie.\n\nRomeine 8\nGeen veroordeling vir die wat in Christus is. Lewe in die Gees vs. vlees. Alles werk saam; niks skei van God se liefde. Lees Romeine 8 self en kontroleer elke stelling teen die verse in jou Bybelweergawe.\n\nGeen veroordeling in Christus\nDie teks van Romeine 8 noem of illustreer: Geen veroordeling in Christus. Lees daardie verse weer en skryf presies op wat die Bybel sê — nie wat jy dink nie.\n\nGees gee lewe\nDie teks van Romeine 8 noem of illustreer: Gees gee lewe. Lees daardie verse weer en skryf presies op wat die Bybel sê — nie wat jy dink nie.\n\nNiks kan ons van liefde skei\nDie teks van Romeine 8 noem of illustreer: Niks kan ons van liefde skei. Lees daardie verse weer en skryf presies op wat die Bybel sê — nie wat jy dink nie.\n\nWhat God wants us to know:\nGod wil gelowiges laat weet evangelie-waarheid en hoe dit kerklewe, heiligheid en liefde moet vorm.\n\nWhy:\nPaulus redeneer van wat Christus gedoen het na hoe Christene moet leef. Soek die leerstelling in hierdie hoofstuk en die lewe wat dit verbind.\n\nSimilar elsewhere:\nRomeine 8:1: Romeine 8:1 sê daar is geen veroordeling vir die wat in Christus Jesus is nie. Romeine 8:2–4 kontrasteer lewe in die Gees met die wet van sonde en dood.\nJohannes 5:24: Romeine 8:1 spreek van geen veroordeling vir die in Christus nie. Johannes 5:24 beskryf Jesus wat sê wie hoor en glo het ewige lewe en nie in veroordeling kom nie.","questions_en":["What does this passage reveal about God?","What promise, command, or truth stands out to you?","How can you apply this to your life today?"],"questions_af":["Wat openbaar hierdie gedeelte oor God?","Watter belofte, gebod of waarheid val vir jou op?","Hoe kan jy dit vandag in jou lewe toepas?"]},{"day":6,"title_en":"The Beatitudes","title_af":"Die Saligprekings","passages":[{"book_id":40,"chapter":5}],"commentary_intro_en":"Foundational Bible reading. Each chapter summary explains why this passage matters in the bigger story.","commentary_intro_af":"Grondleggende Bybel leeswerk. Elke hoofstuk-opsomming verduidelik hoekom hierdie gedeelte saak maak in die groter storie.","commentary_sections":[{"book_id":40,"chapter":5,"heading_en":"Matthew 5","heading_af":"Matteus 5","summary_en":"The Sermon on the Mount begins — Beatitudes, salt and light, fulfillment of the Law, anger, lust, oaths, enemies. Read Matthew 5 yourself and verify each statement against the verses in your Bible version.","summary_af":"Die Bergprediking begin — Saligprekings, sout en lig, vervulling van die Wet, toorn, begeerte, eede, vyande. Lees Matteus 5 self en kontroleer elke stelling teen die verse in jou Bybelweergawe.","study_points_en":[{"title":"Kingdom values invert worldly success","verses":"","detail":"The text of Matthew 5 records or illustrates: Kingdom values invert worldly success. Re-read those verses and note exactly what Scripture states."},{"title":"Blessed are the poor in spirit","verses":"","detail":"The text of Matthew 5 records or illustrates: Blessed are the poor in spirit. Re-read those verses and note exactly what Scripture states."},{"title":"Love your enemies","verses":"","detail":"The text of Matthew 5 records or illustrates: Love your enemies. Re-read those verses and note exactly what Scripture states."}],"study_points_af":[{"title":"Koninkryk-waardes keer wêreldse sukses om","verses":"","detail":"Die teks van Matteus 5 noem of illustreer: Koninkryk-waardes keer wêreldse sukses om. Lees daardie verse weer en skryf presies op wat die Bybel sê — nie wat jy dink nie."},{"title":"Salig die armes van gees","verses":"","detail":"Die teks van Matteus 5 noem of illustreer: Salig die armes van gees. Lees daardie verse weer en skryf presies op wat die Bybel sê — nie wat jy dink nie."},{"title":"Lieft jou vyande","verses":"","detail":"Die teks van Matteus 5 noem of illustreer: Lieft jou vyande. Lees daardie verse weer en skryf presies op wat die Bybel sê — nie wat jy dink nie."}],"teaching_en":"God wants us to know who Jesus is and what he calls people to believe and do through his words, actions, and authority.","teaching_why_en":"Gospel chapters record what Jesus taught, healed, commanded, or revealed about the kingdom. Focus on what the chapter says Jesus did and said—not later tradition.","teaching_af":"God wil hê ons moet weet wie Jesus is en wat Hy mense roep om te glo en te doen deur sy woorde, dade en gesag.","teaching_why_af":"Evangelie-hoofstukke beskryf wat Jesus geleer, genees, beveel of openbaar het. Fokus op wat die hoofstuk sê Jesus gedoen en gesê het.","cross_references_en":[{"ref":"Book 40 4","comparison":"Compare with Book 40 4, which immediately precedes this chapter in the same book — notice what events or themes continue or change."},{"ref":"Parallel Gospels","comparison":"Many events in Matthew, Mark, Luke, and John appear in more than one Gospel with matching or overlapping details. Compare the same episode across Gospels to see what each writer records."}],"cross_references_af":[{"ref":"Book 40 4","comparison":"Compare with Book 40 4, wat direct voor hierdie hoofstuk kom — let op wat voortgaan of verander."},{"ref":"Parallelle Evangelies","comparison":"Baie gebeure in Matteus, Markus, Lukas en Johannes verskyn in meer as een Evangelie. Vergelyk dieselfde episode oor Evangelies heen."}],"highlights_en":["Kingdom values invert worldly success","Blessed are the poor in spirit","Love your enemies"],"highlights_af":["Koninkryk-waardes keer wêreldse sukses om","Salig die armes van gees","Lieft jou vyande"]}],"commentary_en":"Foundational Bible reading. Each chapter summary explains why this passage matters in the bigger story.\n\nMatthew 5\nThe Sermon on the Mount begins — Beatitudes, salt and light, fulfillment of the Law, anger, lust, oaths, enemies. Read Matthew 5 yourself and verify each statement against the verses in your Bible version.\n\nKingdom values invert worldly success\nThe text of Matthew 5 records or illustrates: Kingdom values invert worldly success. Re-read those verses and note exactly what Scripture states.\n\nBlessed are the poor in spirit\nThe text of Matthew 5 records or illustrates: Blessed are the poor in spirit. Re-read those verses and note exactly what Scripture states.\n\nLove your enemies\nThe text of Matthew 5 records or illustrates: Love your enemies. Re-read those verses and note exactly what Scripture states.\n\nWhat God wants us to know:\nGod wants us to know who Jesus is and what he calls people to believe and do through his words, actions, and authority.\n\nWhy:\nGospel chapters record what Jesus taught, healed, commanded, or revealed about the kingdom. Focus on what the chapter says Jesus did and said—not later tradition.\n\nSimilar elsewhere:\nBook 40 4: Compare with Book 40 4, which immediately precedes this chapter in the same book — notice what events or themes continue or change.\nParallel Gospels: Many events in Matthew, Mark, Luke, and John appear in more than one Gospel with matching or overlapping details. Compare the same episode across Gospels to see what each writer records.","commentary_af":"Grondleggende Bybel leeswerk. Elke hoofstuk-opsomming verduidelik hoekom hierdie gedeelte saak maak in die groter storie.\n\nMatteus 5\nDie Bergprediking begin — Saligprekings, sout en lig, vervulling van die Wet, toorn, begeerte, eede, vyande. Lees Matteus 5 self en kontroleer elke stelling teen die verse in jou Bybelweergawe.\n\nKoninkryk-waardes keer wêreldse sukses om\nDie teks van Matteus 5 noem of illustreer: Koninkryk-waardes keer wêreldse sukses om. Lees daardie verse weer en skryf presies op wat die Bybel sê — nie wat jy dink nie.\n\nSalig die armes van gees\nDie teks van Matteus 5 noem of illustreer: Salig die armes van gees. Lees daardie verse weer en skryf presies op wat die Bybel sê — nie wat jy dink nie.\n\nLieft jou vyande\nDie teks van Matteus 5 noem of illustreer: Lieft jou vyande. Lees daardie verse weer en skryf presies op wat die Bybel sê — nie wat jy dink nie.\n\nWhat God wants us to know:\nGod wil hê ons moet weet wie Jesus is en wat Hy mense roep om te glo en te doen deur sy woorde, dade en gesag.\n\nWhy:\nEvangelie-hoofstukke beskryf wat Jesus geleer, genees, beveel of openbaar het. Fokus op wat die hoofstuk sê Jesus gedoen en gesê het.\n\nSimilar elsewhere:\nBook 40 4: Compare with Book 40 4, wat direct voor hierdie hoofstuk kom — let op wat voortgaan of verander.\nParallelle Evangelies: Baie gebeure in Matteus, Markus, Lukas en Johannes verskyn in meer as een Evangelie. Vergelyk dieselfde episode oor Evangelies heen.","questions_en":["What does this passage reveal about God?","What promise, command, or truth stands out to you?","How can you apply this to your life today?"],"questions_af":["Wat openbaar hierdie gedeelte oor God?","Watter belofte, gebod of waarheid val vir jou op?","Hoe kan jy dit vandag in jou lewe toepas?"]},{"day":7,"title_en":"The Birth of Jesus","title_af":"Die Geboorte van Jesus","passages":[{"book_id":42,"chapter":2}],"commentary_intro_en":"Foundational Bible reading. Each chapter summary explains why this passage matters in the bigger story.","commentary_intro_af":"Grondleggende Bybel leeswerk. Elke hoofstuk-opsomming verduidelik hoekom hierdie gedeelte saak maak in die groter storie.","commentary_sections":[{"book_id":42,"chapter":2,"heading_en":"Luke 2","heading_af":"Lukas 2","summary_en":"Luke 2. The Gospels reveal Jesus — His teaching, authority, compassion, and mission. Ask: Who is Jesus here, and what is He calling me to believe and do? Read Luke 2 yourself and verify each statement against the verses in your Bible version.","summary_af":"Lukas 2. Die Evangelies openbaar Jesus — Sy lering, gesag, barmhartigheid en sending. Vra: Wie is Jesus hier, en wat roep Hy my om te glo en te doen? Lees Lukas 2 self en kontroleer elke stelling teen die verse in jou Bybelweergawe.","study_points_en":[{"title":"Jesus'' identity and authority","verses":"","detail":"The text of Luke 2 records or illustrates: Jesus'' identity and authority. Re-read those verses and note exactly what Scripture states."},{"title":"Kingdom teaching","verses":"","detail":"The text 