pare with Book 42 1, wat direct voor hierdie hoofstuk kom — let op wat voortgaan of verander."},{"ref":"Parallelle Evangelies","comparison":"Baie gebeure in Matteus, Markus, Lukas en Johannes verskyn in meer as een Evangelie. Vergelyk dieselfde episode oor Evangelies heen."}],"highlights_en":["Jesus'' identity and authority","Kingdom teaching","Calls to follow"],"highlights_af":["Jesus se identiteit en gesag","Koninkryk-lering","Oproepe om te volg"]}],"commentary_en":"Foundational Bible reading. Each chapter summary explains why this passage matters in the bigger story.\n\nLuke 2\nLuke 2. The Gospels reveal Jesus — His teaching, authority, compassion, and mission. Ask: Who is Jesus here, and what is He calling me to believe and do? Read Luke 2 yourself and verify each statement against the verses in your Bible version.\n\nJesus'' identity and authority\nThe text of Luke 2 records or illustrates: Jesus'' identity and authority. Re-read those verses and note exactly what Scripture states.\n\nKingdom teaching\nThe text of Luke 2 records or illustrates: Kingdom teaching. Re-read those verses and note exactly what Scripture states.\n\nCalls to follow\nThe text of Luke 2 records or illustrates: Calls to follow. Re-read those verses and note exactly what Scripture states.\n\nWhat God wants us to know:\nGod wants us to know who Jesus is and what he calls people to believe and do through his words, actions, and authority.\n\nWhy:\nGospel chapters record what Jesus taught, healed, commanded, or revealed about the kingdom. Focus on what the chapter says Jesus did and said—not later tradition.\n\nSimilar elsewhere:\nBook 42 1: Compare with Book 42 1, which immediately precedes this chapter in the same book — notice what events or themes continue or change.\nParallel Gospels: Many events in Matthew, Mark, Luke, and John appear in more than one Gospel with matching or overlapping details. Compare the same episode across Gospels to see what each writer records.","commentary_af":"Grondleggende Bybel leeswerk. Elke hoofstuk-opsomming verduidelik hoekom hierdie gedeelte saak maak in die groter storie.\n\nLukas 2\nLukas 2. Die Evangelies openbaar Jesus — Sy lering, gesag, barmhartigheid en sending. Vra: Wie is Jesus hier, en wat roep Hy my om te glo en te doen? Lees Lukas 2 self en kontroleer elke stelling teen die verse in jou Bybelweergawe.\n\nJesus se identiteit en gesag\nDie teks van Lukas 2 noem of illustreer: Jesus se identiteit en gesag. Lees daardie verse weer en skryf presies op wat die Bybel sê — nie wat jy dink nie.\n\nKoninkryk-lering\nDie teks van Lukas 2 noem of illustreer: Koninkryk-lering. Lees daardie verse weer en skryf presies op wat die Bybel sê — nie wat jy dink nie.\n\nOproepe om te volg\nDie teks van Lukas 2 noem of illustreer: Oproepe om te volg. Lees daardie verse weer en skryf presies op wat die Bybel sê — nie wat jy dink nie.\n\nWhat God wants us to know:\nGod wil hê ons moet weet wie Jesus is en wat Hy mense roep om te glo en te doen deur sy woorde, dade en gesag.\n\nWhy:\nEvangelie-hoofstukke beskryf wat Jesus geleer, genees, beveel of openbaar het. Fokus op wat die hoofstuk sê Jesus gedoen en gesê het.\n\nSimilar elsewhere:\nBook 42 1: Compare with Book 42 1, wat direct voor hierdie hoofstuk kom — let op wat voortgaan of verander.\nParallelle Evangelies: Baie gebeure in Matteus, Markus, Lukas en Johannes verskyn in meer as een Evangelie. Vergelyk dieselfde episode oor Evangelies heen.","questions_en":["What does this passage reveal about God?","What promise, command, or truth stands out to you?","How can you apply this to your life today?"],"questions_af":["Wat openbaar hierdie gedeelte oor God?","Watter belofte, gebod of waarheid val vir jou op?","Hoe kan jy dit vandag in jou lewe toepas?"]},{"day":8,"title_en":"The Ten Commandments","title_af":"Die Tien Gebooie","passages":[{"book_id":2,"chapter":20}],"commentary_intro_en":"Foundational Bible reading. Each chapter summary explains why this passage matters in the bigger story.","commentary_intro_af":"Grondleggende Bybel leeswerk. Elke hoofstuk-opsomming verduidelik hoekom hierdie gedeelte saak maak in die groter storie.","commentary_sections":[{"book_id":2,"chapter":20,"heading_en":"Exodus 20","heading_af":"Eksodus 20","summary_en":"Exodus 20. This chapter advances the story of God''s covenant people — watch for promises, obedience, and how God keeps His word despite human failure. Read Exodus 20 yourself and verify each statement against the verses in your Bible version.","summary_af":"Eksodus 20. Hierdie hoofstuk beweeg die verhaal van God se verbondsvolk vorentoe — let op beloftes, gehoorsaamheid en hoe God Sy woord hou ondanks menslike mislukking. Lees Eksodus 20 self en kontroleer elke stelling teen die verse in jou Bybelweergawe.","study_points_en":[{"title":"Covenant promises","verses":"","detail":"The text of Exodus 20 records or illustrates: Covenant promises. Re-read those verses and note exactly what Scripture states."},{"title":"Obedience and consequences","verses":"","detail":"The text of Exodus 20 records or illustrates: Obedience and consequences. Re-read those verses and note exactly what Scripture states."},{"title":"God''s faithfulness","verses":"","detail":"The text of Exodus 20 records or illustrates: God''s faithfulness. Re-read those verses and note exactly what Scripture states."}],"study_points_af":[{"title":"Verbondbeloftes","verses":"","detail":"Die teks van Eksodus 20 noem of illustreer: Verbondbeloftes. Lees daardie verse weer en skryf presies op wat die Bybel sê — nie wat jy dink nie."},{"title":"Gehoorsaamheid en gevolge","verses":"","detail":"Die teks van Eksodus 20 noem of illustreer: Gehoorsaamheid en gevolge. Lees daardie verse weer en skryf presies op wat die Bybel sê — nie wat jy dink nie."},{"title":"God se getrouheid","verses":"","detail":"Die teks van Eksodus 20 noem of illustreer: God se getrouheid. Lees daardie verse weer en skryf presies op wat die Bybel sê — nie wat jy dink nie."}],"teaching_en":"God wants his people to know that he initiates relationship by promise and command, and expects trust and obedience in response.","teaching_why_en":"Pentateuch chapters typically record what God said and did toward Israel or the patriarchs—not human achievement alone. Look for direct speech from God and the response it calls for in this chapter.","teaching_af":"God wil sy volk laat weet dat Hy verhouding begin met belofte en gebod, en vertroue en gehoorsaamheid verwag.","teaching_why_af":"Pentateug-hoofstukke beskryf gewoonlik wat God gesê en gedoen het—kyk vir God se directe spraak en die reaksie wat hierdie hoofstuk van sy volk vra.","cross_references_en":[{"ref":"Exodus 19","comparison":"Compare with Exodus 19, which immediately precedes this chapter in the same book — notice what events or themes continue or change."},{"ref":"Deuteronomy 30:15–20","comparison":"Like other Pentateuch chapters, this text forms part of Moses'' covenant instruction. Deuteronomy 30 places life and death, blessing and curse, before Israel and calls them to choose obedience to God''s command."}],"cross_references_af":[{"ref":"Eksodus 19","comparison":"Compare with Eksodus 19, wat direct voor hierdie hoofstuk kom — let op wat voortgaan of verander."},{"ref":"Deuteronomium 30:15–20","comparison":"Soos ander Pentateug-hoofstukke vorm hierdie teks deel van Moses se verbondsinstruksie. Deut 30 stel lewe en dood, seën en vloek, voor Israel."}],"highlights_en":["Covenant promises","Obedience and consequences","God''s faithfulness"],"highlights_af":["Verbondbeloftes","Gehoorsaamheid en gevolge","God se getrouheid"]}],"commentary_en":"Foundational Bible reading. Each chapter summary explains why this passage matters in the bigger story.\n\nExodus 20\nExodus 20. This chapter advances the story of God''s covenant people — watch for promises, obedience, and how God keeps His word despite human failure. Read Exodus 20 yourself and verify each statement against the verses in your Bible version.\n\nCovenant promises\nThe text of Exodus 20 records or illustrates: Covenant promises. Re-read those verses and note exactly what Scripture states.\n\nObedience and consequences\nThe text of Exodus 20 records or illustrates: Obedience and consequences. Re-read those verses and note exactly what Scripture states.\n\nGod''s faithfulness\nThe text of Exodus 20 records or illustrates: God''s faithfulness. Re-read those verses and note exactly what Scripture states.\n\nWhat God wants us to know:\nGod wants his people to know that he initiates relationship by promise and command, and expects trust and obedience in response.\n\nWhy:\nPentateuch chapters typically record what God said and did toward Israel or the patriarchs—not human achievement alone. Look for direct speech from God and the response it calls for in this chapter.\n\nSimilar elsewhere:\nExodus 19: Compare with Exodus 19, which immediately precedes this chapter in the same book — notice what events or themes continue or change.\nDeuteronomy 30:15–20: Like other Pentateuch chapters, this text forms part of Moses'' covenant instruction. Deuteronomy 30 places life and death, blessing and curse, before Israel and calls them to choose obedience to God''s command.","commentary_af":"Grondleggende Bybel leeswerk. Elke hoofstuk-opsomming verduidelik hoekom hierdie gedeelte saak maak in die groter storie.\n\nEksodus 20\nEksodus 20. Hierdie hoofstuk beweeg die verhaal van God se verbondsvolk vorentoe — let op beloftes, gehoorsaamheid en hoe God Sy woord hou ondanks menslike mislukking. Lees Eksodus 20 self en kontroleer elke stelling teen die verse in jou Bybelweergawe.\n\nVerbondbeloftes\nDie teks van Eksodus 20 noem of illustreer: Verbondbeloftes. Lees daardie verse weer en skryf presies op wat die Bybel sê — nie wat jy dink nie.\n\nGehoorsaamheid en gevolge\nDie teks van Eksodus 20 noem of illustreer: Gehoorsaamheid en gevolge. Lees daardie verse weer en skryf presies op wat die Bybel sê — nie wat jy dink nie.\n\nGod se getrouheid\nDie teks van Eksodus 20 noem of illustreer: God se getrouheid. Lees daardie verse weer en skryf presies op wat die Bybel sê — nie wat jy dink nie.\n\nWhat God wants us to know:\nGod wil sy volk laat weet dat Hy verhouding begin met belofte en gebod, en vertroue en gehoorsaamheid verwag.\n\nWhy:\nPentateug-hoofstukke beskryf gewoonlik wat God gesê en gedoen het—kyk vir God se directe spraak en die reaksie wat hierdie hoofstuk van sy volk vra.\n\nSimilar elsewhere:\nEksodus 19: Compare with Eksodus 19, wat direct voor hierdie hoofstuk kom — let op wat voortgaan of verander.\nDeuteronomium 30:15–20: Soos ander Pentateug-hoofstukke vorm hierdie teks deel van Moses se verbondsinstruksie. Deut 30 stel lewe en dood, seën en vloek, voor Israel.","questions_en":["What does this passage reveal about God?","What promise, command, or truth stands out to you?","How can you apply this to your life today?"],"questions_af":["Wat openbaar hierdie gedeelte oor God?","Watter belofte, gebod of waarheid val vir jou op?","Hoe kan jy dit vandag in jou lewe toepas?"]},{"day":9,"title_en":"Rejoice in the Lord","title_af":"Verheug in die Here","passages":[{"book_id":50,"chapter":4}],"commentary_intro_en":"Foundational Bible reading. Each chapter summary explains why this passage matters in the bigger story.","commentary_intro_af":"Grondleggende Bybel leeswerk. Elke hoofstuk-opsomming verduidelik hoekom hierdie gedeelte saak maak in die groter storie.","commentary_sections":[{"book_id":50,"chapter":4,"heading_en":"Book 50 4","heading_af":"Boek 50 4","summary_en":"Book 50 4. Paul teaches doctrine and Christian living. Connect theological truth to practical obedience in church, family, and daily relationships. Read Book 50 4 yourself and verify each statement against the verses in your Bible version.","summary_af":"Boek 50 4. Paulus leer leerstelling en Christelike lewe. Verbind teologiese waarheid met praktiese gehoorsaamheid in kerk, gesin en daaglikse verhoudings. Lees Boek 50 4 self en kontroleer elke stelling teen die verse in jou Bybelweergawe.","study_points_en":[{"title":"Gospel truth","verses":"","detail":"The text of Book 50 4 records or illustrates: Gospel truth. Re-read those verses and note exactly what Scripture states."},{"title":"Life in the Spirit","verses":"","detail":"The text of Book 50 4 records or illustrates: Life in the Spirit. Re-read those verses and note exactly what Scripture states."},{"title":"Practical ethics","verses":"","detail":"The text of Book 50 4 records or illustrates: Practical ethics. Re-read those verses and note exactly what Scripture states."}],"study_points_af":[{"title":"Evangelie-waarheid","verses":"","detail":"Die teks van Boek 50 4 noem of illustreer: Evangelie-waarheid. Lees daardie verse weer en skryf presies op wat die Bybel sê — nie wat jy dink nie."},{"title":"Lewe in die Gees","verses":"","detail":"Die teks van Boek 50 4 noem of illustreer: Lewe in die Gees. Lees daardie verse weer en skryf presies op wat die Bybel sê — nie wat jy dink nie."},{"title":"Praktiese etiek","verses":"","detail":"Die teks van Boek 50 4 noem of illustreer: Praktiese etiek. Lees daardie verse weer en skryf presies op wat die Bybel sê — nie wat jy dink nie."}],"teaching_en":"God wants believers to know gospel truth and how it should shape church life, holiness, and love for others.","teaching_why_en":"Paul''s letters argue from what Christ has done to how Christians should live. Find the doctrinal statement in this chapter and the conduct it connects to.","teaching_af":"God wil gelowiges laat weet evangelie-waarheid en hoe dit kerklewe, heiligheid en liefde moet vorm.","teaching_why_af":"Paulus redeneer van wat Christus gedoen het na hoe Christene moet leef. Soek die leerstelling in hierdie hoofstuk en die lewe wat dit verbind.","cross_references_en":[{"ref":"Book 50 3","comparison":"Compare with Book 50 3, which immediately precedes this chapter in the same book — notice what events or themes continue or change."}],"cross_references_af":[{"ref":"Book 50 3","comparison":"Compare with Book 50 3, wat direct voor hierdie hoofstuk kom — let op wat voortgaan of verander."}],"highlights_en":["Gospel truth","Life in the Spirit","Practical ethics"],"highlights_af":["Evangelie-waarheid","Lewe in die Gees","Praktiese etiek"]}],"commentary_en":"Foundational Bible reading. Each chapter summary explains why this passage matters in the bigger story.\n\nBook 50 4\nBook 50 4. Paul teaches doctrine and Christian living. Connect theological truth to practical obedience in church, family, and daily relationships. Read Book 50 4 yourself and verify each statement against the verses in your Bible version.\n\nGospel truth\nThe text of Book 50 4 records or illustrates: Gospel truth. Re-read those verses and note exactly what Scripture states.\n\nLife in the Spirit\nThe text of Book 50 4 records or illustrates: Life in the Spirit. Re-read those verses and note exactly what Scripture states.\n\nPractical ethics\nThe text of Book 50 4 records or illustrates: Practical ethics. Re-read those verses and note exactly what Scripture states.\n\nWhat God wants us to know:\nGod wants believers to know gospel truth and how it should shape church life, holiness, and love for others.\n\nWhy:\nPaul''s letters argue from what Christ has done to how Christians should live. Find the doctrinal statement in this chapter and the conduct it connects to.\n\nSimilar elsewhere:\nBook 50 3: Compare with Book 50 3, which immediately precedes this chapter in the same book — notice what events or themes continue or change.","commentary_af":"Grondleggende Bybel leeswerk. Elke hoofstuk-opsomming verduidelik hoekom hierdie gedeelte saak maak in die groter storie.\n\nBoek 50 4\nBoek 50 4. Paulus leer leerstelling en Christelike lewe. Verbind teologiese waarheid met praktiese gehoorsaamheid in kerk, gesin en daaglikse verhoudings. Lees Boek 50 4 self en kontroleer elke stelling teen die verse in jou Bybelweergawe.\n\nEvangelie-waarheid\nDie teks van Boek 50 4 noem of illustreer: Evangelie-waarheid. Lees daardie verse weer en skryf presies op wat die Bybel sê — nie wat jy dink nie.\n\nLewe in die Gees\nDie teks van Boek 50 4 noem of illustreer: Lewe in die Gees. Lees daardie verse weer en skryf presies op wat die Bybel sê — nie wat jy dink nie.\n\nPraktiese etiek\nDie teks van Boek 50 4 noem of illustreer: Praktiese etiek. Lees daardie verse weer en skryf presies op wat die Bybel sê — nie wat jy dink nie.\n\nWhat God wants us to know:\nGod wil gelowiges laat weet evangelie-waarheid en hoe dit kerklewe, heiligheid en liefde moet vorm.\n\nWhy:\nPaulus redeneer van wat Christus gedoen het na hoe Christene moet leef. Soek die leerstelling in hierdie hoofstuk en die lewe wat dit verbind.\n\nSimilar elsewhere:\nBook 50 3: Compare with Book 50 3, wat direct voor hierdie hoofstuk kom — let op wat voortgaan of verander.","questions_en":["What does this passage reveal about God?","What promise, command, or truth stands out to you?","How can you apply this to your life today?"],"questions_af":["Wat openbaar hierdie gedeelte oor God?","Watter belofte, gebod of waarheid val vir jou op?","Hoe kan jy dit vandag in jou lewe toepas?"]},{"day":10,"title_en":"Trust in the Lord","title_af":"Vertrou op die Here","passages":[{"book_id":20,"chapter":3}],"commentary_intro_en":"Foundational Bible reading. Each chapter summary explains why this passage matters in the bigger story.","commentary_intro_af":"Grondleggende Bybel leeswerk. Elke hoofstuk-opsomming verduidelik hoekom hierdie gedeelte saak maak in die groter storie.","commentary_sections":[{"book_id":20,"chapter":3,"heading_en":"Proverbs 3","heading_af":"Spreuke 3","summary_en":"Trust the Lord, not your own understanding; honor with wealth. Read Proverbs 3 yourself and verify each statement against the verses in your Bible version.","summary_af":"Vertrou die Here, nie jou eie insig; eer met rykdom. Lees Spreuke 3 self en kontroleer elke stelling teen die verse in jou Bybelweergawe.","study_points_en":[{"title":"Practical wisdom for daily choices","verses":"","detail":"The text of Proverbs 3 records or illustrates: Practical wisdom for daily choices. Re-read those verses and note exactly what Scripture states."},{"title":"Fear of the Lord as foundation","verses":"","detail":"The text of Proverbs 3 records or illustrates: Fear of the Lord as foundation. Re-read those verses and note exactly what Scripture states."},{"title":"One principle to practice today","verses":"","detail":"The text of Proverbs 3 records or illustrates: One principle to practice today. Re-read those verses and note exactly what Scripture states."}],"study_points_af":[{"title":"Praktiese wysheid vir daaglikse keuses","verses":"","detail":"Die teks van Spreuke 3 noem of illustreer: Praktiese wysheid vir daaglikse keuses. Lees daardie verse weer en skryf presies op wat die Bybel sê — nie wat jy dink nie."},{"title":"Vrees vir die Here as fondament","verses":"","detail":"Die teks van Spreuke 3 noem of illustreer: Vrees vir die Here as fondament. Lees daardie verse weer en skryf presies op wat die Bybel sê — nie wat jy dink nie."},{"title":"Een beginsel om vandag te oefen","verses":"","detail":"Die teks van Spreuke 3 noem of illustreer: Een beginsel om vandag te oefen. Lees daardie verse weer en skryf presies op wat die Bybel sê — nie wat jy dink nie."}],"teaching_en":"God wants us to know that true wisdom begins with reverence for him and shapes daily choices, speech, and worship.","teaching_why_en":"Wisdom passages tie understanding to the fear of the Lord and practical living. Notice commands, prayers, or counsel in this chapter and what attitude toward God they assume.","teaching_af":"God wil hê ons moet weet dat ware wysheid begin met eerbied vir Hom en daaglikse keuses, spraak en aanbidding vorm.","teaching_why_af":"Wysheid verbind insig met die vrees vir die Here. Let op gebooie, gebede of raad in hierdie hoofstuk en watter houding teenoor God dit veronderstel.","cross_references_en":[{"ref":"Book 20 2","comparison":"Compare with Book 20 2, which immediately precedes this chapter in the same book — notice what events or themes continue or change."},{"ref":"Proverbs 1:7","comparison":"Wisdom books often repeat the theme that the fear of the Lord is the beginning of wisdom (Proverbs 1:7). Compare how each psalm or proverb applies that foundation differently."}],"cross_references_af":[{"ref":"Book 20 2","comparison":"Compare with Book 20 2, wat direct voor hierdie hoofstuk kom — let op wat voortgaan of verander."},{"ref":"Spreuke 1:7","comparison":"Wysheidsboeke herhaal dat die vrees vir die Here die begin van wysheid is (Spr 1:7). Vergelyk hoe elke psalm of spreuk dit toepas."}],"highlights_en":["Practical wisdom for daily choices","Fear of the Lord as foundation","One principle to practice today"],"highlights_af":["Praktiese wysheid vir daaglikse keuses","Vrees vir die Here as fondament","Een beginsel om vandag te oefen"]}],"commentary_en":"Foundational Bible reading. Each chapter summary explains why this passage matters in the bigger story.\n\nProverbs 3\nTrust the Lord, not your own understanding; honor with wealth. Read Proverbs 3 yourself and verify each statement against the verses in your Bible version.\n\nPractical wisdom for daily choices\nThe text of Proverbs 3 records or illustrates: Practical wisdom for daily choices. Re-read those verses and note exactly what Scripture states.\n\nFear of the Lord as foundation\nThe text of Proverbs 3 records or illustrates: Fear of the Lord as foundation. Re-read those verses and note exactly what Scripture states.\n\nOne principle to practice today\nThe text of Proverbs 3 records or illustrates: One principle to practice today. Re-read those verses and note exactly what Scripture states.\n\nWhat God wants us to know:\nGod wants us to know that true wisdom begins with reverence for him and shapes daily choices, speech, and worship.\n\nWhy:\nWisdom passages tie understanding to the fear of the Lord and practical living. Notice commands, prayers, or counsel in this chapter and what attitude toward God they assume.\n\nSimilar elsewhere:\nBook 20 2: Compare with Book 20 2, which immediately precedes this chapter in the same book — notice what events or themes continue or change.\nProverbs 1:7: Wisdom books often repeat the theme that the fear of the Lord is the beginning of wisdom (Proverbs 1:7). Compare how each psalm or proverb applies that foundation differently.","commentary_af":"Grondleggende Bybel leeswerk. Elke hoofstuk-opsomming verduidelik hoekom hierdie gedeelte saak maak in die groter storie.\n\nSpreuke 3\nVertrou die Here, nie jou eie insig; eer met rykdom. Lees Spreuke 3 self en kontroleer elke stelling teen die verse in jou Bybelweergawe.\n\nPraktiese wysheid vir daaglikse keuses\nDie teks van Spreuke 3 noem of illustreer: Praktiese wysheid vir daaglikse keuses. Lees daardie verse weer en skryf presies op wat die Bybel sê — nie wat jy dink nie.\n\nVrees vir die Here as fondament\nDie teks van Spreuke 3 noem of illustreer: Vrees vir die Here as fondament. Lees daardie verse weer en skryf presies op wat die Bybel sê — nie wat jy dink nie.\n\nEen beginsel om vandag te oefen\nDie teks van Spreuke 3 noem of illustreer: Een beginsel om vandag te oefen. Lees daardie verse weer en skryf presies op wat die Bybel sê — nie wat jy dink nie.\n\nWhat God wants us to know:\nGod wil hê ons moet weet dat ware wysheid begin met eerbied vir Hom en daaglikse keuses, spraak en aanbidding vorm.\n\nWhy:\nWysheid verbind insig met die vrees vir die Here. Let op gebooie, gebede of raad in hierdie hoofstuk en watter houding teenoor God dit veronderstel.\n\nSimilar elsewhere:\nBook 20 2: Compare with Book 20 2, wat direct voor hierdie hoofstuk kom — let op wat voortgaan of verander.\nSpreuke 1:7: Wysheidsboeke herhaal dat die vrees vir die Here die begin van wysheid is (Spr 1:7). Vergelyk hoe elke psalm of spreuk dit toepas.","questions_en":["What does this passage reveal about God?","What promise, command, or truth stands out to you?","How can you apply this to your life today?"],"questions_af":["Wat openbaar hierdie gedeelte oor God?","Watter belofte, gebod of waarheid val vir jou op?","Hoe kan jy dit vandag in jou lewe toepas?"]},{"day":11,"title_en":"The Suffering Servant","title_af":"Die Lydinge Kneg","passages":[{"book_id":23,"chapter":53}],"commentary_intro_en":"Foundational Bible reading. Each chapter summary explains why this passage matters in the bigger story.","commentary_intro_af":"Grondleggende Bybel leeswerk. Elke hoofstuk-opsomming verduidelik hoekom hierdie gedeelte saak maak in die groter storie.","commentary_sections":[{"book_id":23,"chapter":53,"heading_en":"Book 23 53","heading_af":"Boek 23 53","summary_en":"Book 23 53. Prophetic word calling God''s people to covenant faithfulness. Listen for judgment, hope, and promises pointing to Messiah and restoration. Read Book 23 53 yourself and verify each statement against the verses in your Bible version.","summary_af":"Boek 23 53. Profetiese woord wat God se volk roep tot verbondstrousheid. Luister vir vonnis, hoop en beloftes wat wys na Messias en herstel. Lees Boek 23 53 self en kontroleer elke stelling teen die verse in jou Bybelweergawe.","study_points_en":[{"title":"Sin and repentance","verses":"","detail":"The text of Book 23 53 records or illustrates: Sin and repentance. Re-read those verses and note exactly what Scripture states."},{"title":"God''s holy standards","verses":"","detail":"The text of Book 23 53 records or illustrates: God''s holy standards. Re-read those verses and note exactly what Scripture states."},{"title":"Hope for the future","verses":"","detail":"The text of Book 23 53 records or illustrates: Hope for the future. Re-read those verses and note exactly what Scripture states."}],"study_points_af":[{"title":"Sonde en berou","verses":"","detail":"Die teks van Boek 23 53 noem of illustreer: Sonde en berou. Lees daardie verse weer en skryf presies op wat die Bybel sê — nie wat jy dink nie."},{"title":"God se heilige standaarde","verses":"","detail":"Die teks van Boek 23 53 noem of illustreer: God se heilige standaarde. Lees daardie verse weer en skryf presies op wat die Bybel sê — nie wat jy dink nie."},{"title":"Hoop vir die toekoms","verses":"","detail":"Die teks van Boek 23 53 noem of illustreer: Hoop vir die toekoms. Lees daardie verse weer en skryf presies op wat die Bybel sê — nie wat jy dink nie."}],"teaching_en":"God wants his people to know that he calls them back to faithfulness, warns of judgment, and often pairs correction with hope.","teaching_why_en":"Prophetic chapters usually contain God''s speech—accusation, command, or promise. Identify what God says he will do and what he asks his people to do.","teaching_af":"God wil sy volk laat weet dat Hy hulle terugroep na trou, waarsku vir vonnis, en korreksie dikwels met hoop paar.","teaching_why_af":"Profetiese hoofstukke bevat gewoonlik God se spraak—beskuldiging, gebod of belofte. Identifiseer wat God sê Hy sal doen en wat Hy van sy volk vra.","cross_references_en":[{"ref":"Book 23 52","comparison":"Compare with Book 23 52, which immediately precedes this chapter in the same book — notice what events or themes continue or change."}],"cross_references_af":[{"ref":"Book 23 52","comparison":"Compare with Book 23 52, wat direct voor hierdie hoofstuk kom — let op wat voortgaan of verander."}],"highlights_en":["Sin and repentance","God''s holy standards","Hope for the future"],"highlights_af":["Sonde en berou","God se heilige standaarde","Hoop vir die toekoms"]}],"commentary_en":"Foundational Bible reading. Each chapter summary explains why this passage matters in the bigger story.\n\nBook 23 53\nBook 23 53. Prophetic word calling God''s people to covenant faithfulness. Listen for judgment, hope, and promises pointing to Messiah and restoration. Read Book 23 53 yourself and verify each statement against the verses in your Bible version.\n\nSin and repentance\nThe text of Book 23 53 records or illustrates: Sin and repentance. Re-read those verses and note exactly what Scripture states.\n\nGod''s holy standards\nThe text of Book 23 53 records or illustrates: God''s holy standards. Re-read those verses and note exactly what Scripture states.\n\nHope for the future\nThe text of Book 23 53 records or illustrates: Hope for the future. Re-read those verses and note exactly what Scripture states.\n\nWhat God wants us to know:\nGod wants his people to know that he calls them back to faithfulness, warns of judgment, and often pairs correction with hope.\n\nWhy:\nProphetic chapters usually contain God''s speech—accusation, command, or promise. Identify what God says he will do and what he asks his people to do.\n\nSimilar elsewhere:\nBook 23 52: Compare with Book 23 52, which immediately precedes this chapter in the same book — notice what events or themes continue or change.","commentary_af":"Grondleggende Bybel leeswerk. Elke hoofstuk-opsomming verduidelik hoekom hierdie gedeelte saak maak in die groter storie.\n\nBoek 23 53\nBoek 23 53. Profetiese woord wat God se volk roep tot verbondstrousheid. Luister vir vonnis, hoop en beloftes wat wys na Messias en herstel. Lees Boek 23 53 self en kontroleer elke stelling teen die verse in jou Bybelweergawe.\n\nSonde en berou\nDie teks van Boek 23 53 noem of illustreer: Sonde en berou. Lees daardie verse weer en skryf presies op wat die Bybel sê — nie wat jy dink nie.\n\nGod se heilige standaarde\nDie teks van Boek 23 53 noem of illustreer: God se heilige standaarde. Lees daardie verse weer en skryf presies op wat die Bybel sê — nie wat jy dink nie.\n\nHoop vir die toekoms\nDie teks van Boek 23 53 noem of illustreer: Hoop vir die toekoms. Lees daardie verse weer en skryf presies op wat die Bybel sê — nie wat jy dink nie.\n\nWhat God wants us to know:\nGod wil sy volk laat weet dat Hy hulle terugroep na trou, waarsku vir vonnis, en korreksie dikwels met hoop paar.\n\nWhy:\nProfetiese hoofstukke bevat gewoonlik God se spraak—beskuldiging, gebod of belofte. Identifiseer wat God sê Hy sal doen en wat Hy van sy volk vra.\n\nSimilar elsewhere:\nBook 23 52: Compare with Book 23 52, wat direct voor hierdie hoofstuk kom — let op wat voortgaan of verander.","questions_en":["What does this passage reveal about God?","What promise, command, or truth stands out to you?","How can you apply this to your life today?"],"questions_af":["Wat openbaar hierdie gedeelte oor God?","Watter belofte, gebod of waarheid val vir jou op?","Hoe kan jy dit vandag in jou lewe toepas?"]},{"day":12,"title_en":"The Day of Pentecost","title_af":"Die Dag van Pinkster","passages":[{"book_id":44,"chapter":2}],"commentary_intro_en":"Foundational Bible reading. Each chapter summary explains why this passage matters in the bigger story.","commentary_intro_af":"Grondleggende Bybel leeswerk. Elke hoofstuk-opsomming verduidelik hoekom hierdie gedeelte saak maak in die groter storie.","commentary_sections":[{"book_id":44,"chapter":2,"heading_en":"Acts 2","heading_af":"Handeling 2","summary_en":"Pentecost — Holy Spirit fills believers; Peter preaches; three thousand saved. The church is born in power. Read Acts 2 yourself and verify each statement against the verses in your Bible version.","summary_af":"Pinkster — Heilige Gees vul gelowiges; Petrus preek; drieduisend gered. Die kerk word in krag gebore. Lees Handeling 2 self en kontroleer elke stelling teen die verse in jou Bybelweergawe.","study_points_en":[{"title":"Spirit like tongues of fire","verses":"","detail":"The text of Acts 2 records or illustrates: Spirit like tongues of fire. Re-read those verses and note exactly what Scripture states."},{"title":"Peter''s sermon — crucified and risen","verses":"","detail":"The text of Acts 2 records or illustrates: Peter''s sermon — crucified and risen. Re-read those verses and note exactly what Scripture states."},{"title":"Repent and be baptized","verses":"","detail":"The text of Acts 2 records or illustrates: Repent and be baptized. Re-read those verses and note exactly what Scripture states."}],"study_points_af":[{"title":"Gees soos vuurtong","verses":"","detail":"Die teks van Handeling 2 noem of illustreer: Gees soos vuurtong. Lees daardie verse weer en skryf presies op wat die Bybel sê — nie wat jy dink nie."},{"title":"Petrus se preek — gekruisig en opgestaan","verses":"","detail":"Die teks van Handeling 2 noem of illustreer: Petrus se preek — gekruisig en opgestaan. Lees daardie verse weer en skryf presies op wat die Bybel sê — nie wat jy dink nie."},{"title":"Bekeer en doop","verses":"","detail":"Die teks van Handeling 2 noem of illustreer: Bekeer en doop. Lees daardie verse weer en skryf presies op wat die Bybel sê — nie wat jy dink nie."}],"teaching_en":"God wants us to know that the risen Christ continues his work through the Spirit, the apostles, and the growing church.","teaching_why_en":"Acts records preaching, conversions, miracles, and persecution. Notice how the Spirit empowers witness and how the church responds in this chapter.","teaching_af":"God wil hê ons moet weet dat die opgestane Christus voortwerk deur die Gees, die apostels en die groeiende kerk.","teaching_why_af":"Handeling beskryf preek, bekering, wonderwerke en vervolging. Let hoe die Gees getuienis bemagtig en hoe die kerk reageer.","cross_references_en":[{"ref":"Book 44 1","comparison":"Compare with Book 44 1, which immediately precedes this chapter in the same book — notice what events or themes continue or change."}],"cross_references_af":[{"ref":"Book 44 1","comparison":"Compare with Book 44 1, wat direct voor hierdie hoofstuk kom — let op wat voortgaan of verander."}],"highlights_en":["Spirit like tongues of fire","Peter''s sermon — crucified and risen","Repent and be baptized"],"highlights_af":["Gees soos vuurtong","Petrus se preek — gekruisig en opgestaan","Bekeer en doop"]}],"commentary_en":"Foundational Bible reading. Each chapter summary explains why this passage matters in the bigger story.\n\nActs 2\nPentecost — Holy Spirit fills believers; Peter preaches; three thousand saved. The church is born in power. Read Acts 2 yourself and verify each statement against the verses in your Bible version.\n\nSpirit like tongues of fire\nThe text of Acts 2 records or illustrates: Spirit like tongues of fire. Re-read those verses and note exactly what Scripture states.\n\nPeter''s sermon — crucified and risen\nThe text of Acts 2 records or illustrates: Peter''s sermon — crucified and risen. Re-read those verses and note exactly what Scripture states.\n\nRepent and be baptized\nThe text of Acts 2 records or illustrates: Repent and be baptized. Re-read those verses and note exactly what Scripture states.\n\nWhat God wants us to know:\nGod wants us to know that the risen Christ continues his work through the Spirit, the apostles, and the growing church.\n\nWhy:\nActs records preaching, conversions, miracles, and persecution. Notice how the Spirit empowers witness and how the church responds in this chapter.\n\nSimilar elsewhere:\nBook 44 1: Compare with Book 44 1, which immediately precedes this chapter in the same book — notice what events or themes continue or change.","commentary_af":"Grondleggende Bybel leeswerk. Elke hoofstuk-opsomming verduidelik hoekom hierdie gedeelte saak maak in die groter storie.\n\nHandeling 2\nPinkster — Heilige Gees vul gelowiges; Petrus preek; drieduisend gered. Die kerk word in krag gebore. Lees Handeling 2 self en kontroleer elke stelling teen die verse in jou Bybelweergawe.\n\nGees soos vuurtong\nDie teks van Handeling 2 noem of illustreer: Gees soos vuurtong. Lees daardie verse weer en skryf presies op wat die Bybel sê — nie wat jy dink nie.\n\nPetrus se preek — gekruisig en opgestaan\nDie teks van Handeling 2 noem of illustreer: Petrus se preek — gekruisig en opgestaan. Lees daardie verse weer en skryf presies op wat die Bybel sê — nie wat jy dink nie.\n\nBekeer en doop\nDie teks van Handeling 2 noem of illustreer: Bekeer en doop. Lees daardie verse weer en skryf presies op wat die Bybel sê — nie wat jy dink nie.\n\nWhat God wants us to know:\nGod wil hê ons moet weet dat die opgestane Christus voortwerk deur die Gees, die apostels en die groeiende kerk.\n\nWhy:\nHandeling beskryf preek, bekering, wonderwerke en vervolging. Let hoe die Gees getuienis bemagtig en hoe die kerk reageer.\n\nSimilar elsewhere:\nBook 44 1: Compare with Book 44 1, wat direct voor hierdie hoofstuk kom — let op wat voortgaan of verander.","questions_en":["What does this passage reveal about God?","What promise, command, or truth stands out to you?","How can you apply this to your life today?"],"questions_af":["Wat openbaar hierdie gedeelte oor God?","Watter belofte, gebod of waarheid val vir jou op?","Hoe kan jy dit vandag in jou lewe toepas?"]},{"day":13,"title_en":"A New Heaven and Earth","title_af":"''n Nuwe Hemel en Aarde","passages":[{"book_id":66,"chapter":21}],"commentary_intro_en":"Foundational Bible reading. Each chapter summary explains why this passage matters in the bigger story.","commentary_intro_af":"Grondleggende Bybel leeswerk. Elke hoofstuk-opsomming verduidelik hoekom hierdie gedeelte saak maak in die groter storie.","commentary_sections":[{"book_id":66,"chapter":21,"heading_en":"Revelation 21","heading_af":"Openbaring 21","summary_en":"Revelation 21. Apocalyptic vision of Christ''s victory and final renewal. Balance symbolic imagery with the certainty that God wins and His people inherit eternal life. Read Revelation 21 yourself and verify each statement against the verses in your Bible version.","summary_af":"Openbaring 21. Apokaliptiese visie van Christus se oorwinning en finale vernuwing. Balanseer simboliese beelde met die sekerheid dat God wen en Sy volk erf ewige lewe. Lees Openbaring 21 self en kontroleer elke stelling teen die verse in jou Bybelweergawe.","study_points_en":[{"title":"Christ the victorious Lamb","verses":"","detail":"The text of Revelation 21 records or illustrates: Christ the victorious Lamb. Re-read those verses and note exactly what Scripture states."},{"title":"Judgment and mercy","verses":"","detail":"The text of Revelation 21 records or illustrates: Judgment and mercy. Re-read those verses and note exactly what Scripture states."},{"title":"New creation hope","verses":"","detail":"The text of Revelation 21 records or illustrates: New creation hope. Re-read those verses and note exactly what Scripture states."}],"study_points_af":[{"title":"Christus die oorwinnaar-Lam","verses":"","detail":"Die teks van Openbaring 21 noem of illustreer: Christus die oorwinnaar-Lam. Lees daardie verse weer en skryf presies op wat die Bybel sê — nie wat jy dink nie."},{"title":"Vonnis en barmhartigheid","verses":"","detail":"Die teks van Openbaring 21 noem of illustreer: Vonnis en barmhartigheid. Lees daardie verse weer en skryf presies op wat die Bybel sê — nie wat jy dink nie."},{"title":"Nuwe-skepping hoop","verses":"","detail":"Die teks van Openbaring 21 noem of illustreer: Nuwe-skepping hoop. Lees daardie verse weer en skryf presies op wat die Bybel sê — nie wat jy dink nie."}],"teaching_en":"God wants us to know that Christ reigns, justice will be done, and God will renew creation for his people.","teaching_why_en":"Revelation uses visions of throne, Lamb, judgment, and new creation. Identify what this chapter records about Christ''s authority and the future God promises.","teaching_af":"God wil hê ons moet weet dat Christus regeer, geregtigheid geskied, en God die skepping vir sy volk sal vernuwe.","teaching_why_af":"Openbaring gebruik visies van troon, Lam, vonnis en nuwe skepping. Identifiseer wat hierdie hoofstuk oor Christus se gesag en die toekoms rekord.","cross_references_en":[{"ref":"Book 66 20","comparison":"Compare with Book 66 20, which immediately precedes this chapter in the same book — notice what events or themes continue or change."}],"cross_references_af":[{"ref":"Book 66 20","comparison":"Compare with Book 66 20, wat direct voor hierdie hoofstuk kom — let op wat voortgaan of verander."}],"highlights_en":["Christ the victorious Lamb","Judgment and mercy","New creation hope"],"highlights_af":["Christus die oorwinnaar-Lam","Vonnis en barmhartigheid","Nuwe-skepping hoop"]}],"commentary_en":"Foundational Bible reading. Each chapter summary explains why this passage matters in the bigger story.\n\nRevelation 21\nRevelation 21. Apocalyptic vision of Christ''s victory and final renewal. Balance symbolic imagery with the certainty that God wins and His people inherit eternal life. Read Revelation 21 yourself and verify each statement against the verses in your Bible version.\n\nChrist the victorious Lamb\nThe text of Revelation 21 records or illustrates: Christ the victorious Lamb. Re-read those verses and note exactly what Scripture states.\n\nJudgment and mercy\nThe text of Revelation 21 records or illustrates: Judgment and mercy. Re-read those verses and note exactly what Scripture states.\n\nNew creation hope\nThe text of Revelation 21 records or illustrates: New creation hope. Re-read those verses and note exactly what Scripture states.\n\nWhat God wants us to know:\nGod wants us to know that Christ reigns, justice will be done, and God will renew creation for his people.\n\nWhy:\nRevelation uses visions of throne, Lamb, judgment, and new creation. Identify what this chapter records about Christ''s authority and the future God promises.\n\nSimilar elsewhere:\nBook 66 20: Compare with Book 66 20, which immediately precedes this chapter in the same book — notice what events or themes continue or change.","commentary_af":"Grondleggende Bybel leeswerk. Elke hoofstuk-opsomming verduidelik hoekom hierdie gedeelte saak maak in die groter storie.\n\nOpenbaring 21\nOpenbaring 21. Apokaliptiese visie van Christus se oorwinning en finale vernuwing. Balanseer simboliese beelde met die sekerheid dat God wen en Sy volk erf ewige lewe. Lees Openbaring 21 self en kontroleer elke stelling teen die verse in jou Bybelweergawe.\n\nChristus die oorwinnaar-Lam\nDie teks van Openbaring 21 noem of illustreer: Christus die oorwinnaar-Lam. Lees daardie verse weer en skryf presies op wat die Bybel sê — nie wat jy dink nie.\n\nVonnis en barmhartigheid\nDie teks van Openbaring 21 noem of illustreer: Vonnis en barmhartigheid. Lees daardie verse weer en skryf presies op wat die Bybel sê — nie wat jy dink nie.\n\nNuwe-skepping hoop\nDie teks van Openbaring 21 noem of illustreer: Nuwe-skepping hoop. Lees daardie verse weer en skryf presies op wat die Bybel sê — nie wat jy dink nie.\n\nWhat God wants us to know:\nGod wil hê ons moet weet dat Christus regeer, geregtigheid geskied, en God die skepping vir sy volk sal vernuwe.\n\nWhy:\nOpenbaring gebruik visies van troon, Lam, vonnis en nuwe skepping. Identifiseer wat hierdie hoofstuk oor Christus se gesag en die toekoms rekord.\n\nSimilar elsewhere:\nBook 66 20: Compare with Book 66 20, wat direct voor hierdie hoofstuk kom — let op wat voortgaan of verander.","questions_en":["What does this passage reveal about God?","What promise, command, or truth stands out to you?","How can you apply this to your life today?"],"questions_af":["Wat openbaar hierdie gedeelte oor God?","Watter belofte, gebod of waarheid val vir jou op?","Hoe kan jy dit vandag in jou lewe toepas?"]},{"day":14,"title_en":"The Call of Abraham","title_af":"Die Roeping van Abraham","passages":[{"book_id":1,"chapter":12}],"commentary_intro_en":"Foundational Bible reading. Each chapter summary explains why this passage matters in the bigger story.","commentary_intro_af":"Grondleggende Bybel leeswerk. Elke hoofstuk-opsomming verduidelik hoekom hierdie gedeelte saak maak in die groter storie.","commentary_sections":[{"book_id":1,"chapter":12,"heading_en":"Genesis 12","heading_af":"Genesis 12","summary_en":"Abram and Lot separate; Abram rescues Lot; Melchizedek blesses; God''s covenant confirmed. Read Genesis 12 yourself and verify each statement against the verses in your Bible version.","summary_af":"Abram en Lot skei; Abram red Lot; Melchisedek seën; God se verbond bevestig. Lees Genesis 12 self en kontroleer elke stelling teen die verse in jou Bybelweergawe.","study_points_en":[{"title":"Key events in God''s covenant story","verses":"","detail":"The text of Genesis 12 records or illustrates: Key events in God''s covenant story. Re-read those verses and note exactly what Scripture states."},{"title":"Watch how promises survive human failure","verses":"","detail":"The text of Genesis 12 records or illustrates: Watch how promises survive human failure. Re-read those verses and note exactly what Scripture states."},{"title":"Note worship, obedience, and grace","verses":"","detail":"The text of Genesis 12 records or illustrates: Note worship, obedience, and grace. Re-read those verses and note exactly what Scripture states."}],"study_points_af":[{"title":"Sleutelgebeure in God se verbondverhaal","verses":"","detail":"Die teks van Genesis 12 noem of illustreer: Sleutelgebeure in God se verbondverhaal. Lees daardie verse weer en skryf presies op wat die Bybel sê — nie wat jy dink nie."},{"title":"Let hoe beloftes menslike mislukking oorleef","verses":"","detail":"Die teks van Genesis 12 noem of illustreer: Let hoe beloftes menslike mislukking oorleef. Lees daardie verse weer en skryf presies op wat die Bybel sê — nie wat jy dink nie."},{"title":"Let op aanbidding, gehoorsaamheid en genade","verses":"","detail":"Die teks van Genesis 12 noem of illustreer: Let op aanbidding, gehoorsaamheid en genade. Lees daardie verse weer en skryf presies op wat die Bybel sê — nie wat jy dink nie."}],"teaching_en":"God wants his people to know that he initiates relationship by promise and command, and expects trust and obedience in response.","teaching_why_en":"Pentateuch chapters typically record what God said and did toward Israel or the patriarchs—not human achievement alone. Look for direct speech from God and the response it calls for in this chapter.","teaching_af":"God wil sy volk laat weet dat Hy verhouding begin met belofte en gebod, en vertroue en gehoorsaamheid verwag.","teaching_why_af":"Pentateug-hoofstukke beskryf gewoonlik wat God gesê en gedoen het—kyk vir God se directe spraak en die reaksie wat hierdie hoofstuk van sy volk vra.","cross_references_en":[{"ref":"Acts 7:2–4","comparison":"Genesis 12 records God calling Abram to leave his country. Stephen in Acts 7:2–4 recounts the God of glory appearing to Abraham in Mesopotamia and telling him to leave — the same call narrative."},{"ref":"Galatians 3:8","comparison":"Genesis 12:3 records God promising to bless all families of the earth through Abram. Galatians 3:8 cites Scripture foreseeing that God would justify the nations by faith — quoting that promise theme."}],"cross_references_af":[{"ref":"Hand 7:2–4","comparison":"Genesis 12 beskryf God wat Abram roep om sy land te verlaat. Stefanus in Hand 7:2–4 herhaal dat die God van heerlikheid aan Abraham verskyn het en hom gesê het om te trek."},{"ref":"Galasiërs 3:8","comparison":"Genesis 12:3 beskryf God se belofte om alle geslagte van die aarde deur Abram te seën. Gal 3:8 verwys na Skrif wat voorsien dat God die nasies deur geloof regverdig."}],"highlights_en":["Key events in God''s covenant story","Watch how promises survive human failure","Note worship, obedience, and grace"],"highlights_af":["Sleutelgebeure in God se verbondverhaal","Let hoe beloftes menslike mislukking oorleef","Let op aanbidding, gehoorsaamheid en genade"]}],"commentary_en":"Foundational Bible reading. Each chapter summary explains why this passage matters in the bigger story.\n\nGenesis 12\nAbram and Lot separate; Abram rescues Lot; Melchizedek blesses; God''s covenant confirmed. Read Genesis 12 yourself and verify each statement against the verses in your Bible version.\n\nKey events in God''s covenant story\nThe text of Genesis 12 records or illustrates: Key events in God''s covenant story. Re-read those verses and note exactly what Scripture states.\n\nWatch how promises survive human failure\nThe text of Genesis 12 records or illustrates: Watch how promises survive human failure. Re-read those verses and note exactly what Scripture states.\n\nNote worship, obedience, and grace\nThe text of Genesis 12 records or illustrates: Note worship, obedience, and grace. Re-read those verses and note exactly what Scripture states.\n\nWhat God wants us to know:\nGod wants his people to know that he initiates relationship by promise and command, and expects trust and obedience in response.\n\nWhy:\nPentateuch chapters typically record what God said and did toward Israel or the patriarchs—not human achievement alone. Look for direct speech from God and the response it calls for in this chapter.\n\nSimilar elsewhere:\nActs 7:2–4: Genesis 12 records God calling Abram to leave his country. Stephen in Acts 7:2–4 recounts the God of glory appearing to Abraham in Mesopotamia and telling him to leave — the same call narrative.\nGalatians 3:8: Genesis 12:3 records God promising to bless all families of the earth through Abram. Galatians 3:8 cites Scripture foreseeing that God would justify the nations by faith — quoting that promise theme.","commentary_af":"Grondleggende Bybel leeswerk. Elke hoofstuk-opsomming verduidelik hoekom hierdie gedeelte saak maak in die groter storie.\n\nGenesis 12\nAbram en Lot skei; Abram red Lot; Melchisedek seën; God se verbond bevestig. Lees Genesis 12 self en kontroleer elke stelling teen die verse in jou Bybelweergawe.\n\nSleutelgebeure in God se verbondverhaal\nDie teks van Genesis 12 noem of illustreer: Sleutelgebeure in God se verbondverhaal. Lees daardie verse weer en skryf presies op wat die Bybel sê — nie wat jy dink nie.\n\nLet hoe beloftes menslike mislukking oorleef\nDie teks van Genesis 12 noem of illustreer: Let hoe beloftes menslike mislukking oorleef. Lees daardie verse weer en skryf presies op wat die Bybel sê — nie wat jy dink nie.\n\nLet op aanbidding, gehoorsaamheid en genade\nDie teks van Genesis 12 noem of illustreer: Let op aanbidding, gehoorsaamheid en genade. Lees daardie verse weer en skryf presies op wat die Bybel sê — nie wat jy dink nie.\n\nWhat God wants us to know:\nGod wil sy volk laat weet dat Hy verhouding begin met belofte en gebod, en vertroue en gehoorsaamheid verwag.\n\nWhy:\nPentateug-hoofstukke beskryf gewoonlik wat God gesê en gedoen het—kyk vir God se directe spraak en die reaksie wat hierdie hoofstuk van sy volk vra.\n\nSimilar elsewhere:\nHand 7:2–4: Genesis 12 beskryf God wat Abram roep om sy land te verlaat. Stefanus in Hand 7:2–4 herhaal dat die God van heerlikheid aan Abraham verskyn het en hom gesê het om te trek.\nGalasiërs 3:8: Genesis 12:3 beskryf God se belofte om alle geslagte van die aarde deur Abram te seën. Gal 3:8 verwys na Skrif wat voorsien dat God die nasies deur geloof regverdig.","questions_en":["What does this passage reveal about God?","What promise, command, or truth stands out to you?","How can you apply this to your life today?"],"questions_af":["Wat openbaar hierdie gedeelte oor God?","Watter belofte, gebod of waarheid val vir jou op?","Hoe kan jy dit vandag in jou lewe toepas?"]}]'::jsonb,
    '🌱',
    15,
    true
)
