skryf presies op wat die Bybel sê — nie wat jy dink nie."},{"title":"Let op aanbidding, gehoorsaamheid en genade","verses":"","detail":"Die teks van Genesis 15 noem of illustreer: Let op aanbidding, gehoorsaamheid en genade. Lees daardie verse weer en skryf presies op wat die Bybel sê — nie wat jy dink nie."}],"teaching_en":"God wants his people to know that he initiates relationship by promise and command, and expects trust and obedience in response.","teaching_why_en":"Pentateuch chapters typically record what God said and did toward Israel or the patriarchs—not human achievement alone. Look for direct speech from God and the response it calls for in this chapter.","teaching_af":"God wil sy volk laat weet dat Hy verhouding begin met belofte en gebod, en vertroue en gehoorsaamheid verwag.","teaching_why_af":"Pentateug-hoofstukke beskryf gewoonlik wat God gesê en gedoen het—kyk vir God se directe spraak en die reaksie wat hierdie hoofstuk van sy volk vra.","cross_references_en":[{"ref":"Genesis 14","comparison":"Compare with Genesis 14, which immediately precedes this chapter in the same book — notice what events or themes continue or change."},{"ref":"Deuteronomy 30:15–20","comparison":"Like other Pentateuch chapters, this text forms part of Moses'' covenant instruction. Deuteronomy 30 places life and death, blessing and curse, before Israel and calls them to choose obedience to God''s command."}],"cross_references_af":[{"ref":"Genesis 14","comparison":"Compare with Genesis 14, wat direct voor hierdie hoofstuk kom — let op wat voortgaan of verander."},{"ref":"Deuteronomium 30:15–20","comparison":"Soos ander Pentateug-hoofstukke vorm hierdie teks deel van Moses se verbondsinstruksie. Deut 30 stel lewe en dood, seën en vloek, voor Israel."}],"highlights_en":["Key events in God''s covenant story","Watch how promises survive human failure","Note worship, obedience, and grace"],"highlights_af":["Sleutelgebeure in God se verbondverhaal","Let hoe beloftes menslike mislukking oorleef","Let op aanbidding, gehoorsaamheid en genade"]}],"commentary_en":"Today''s themed reading: Abraham''s Faith. Study each chapter section below as you read.\n\nGenesis 15\nGod cuts covenant with Abram; stars promise countless descendants; faith credited as righteousness. Read Genesis 15 yourself and verify each statement against the verses in your Bible version.\n\nKey events in God''s covenant story\nThe text of Genesis 15 records or illustrates: Key events in God''s covenant story. Re-read those verses and note exactly what Scripture states.\n\nWatch how promises survive human failure\nThe text of Genesis 15 records or illustrates: Watch how promises survive human failure. Re-read those verses and note exactly what Scripture states.\n\nNote worship, obedience, and grace\nThe text of Genesis 15 records or illustrates: Note worship, obedience, and grace. Re-read those verses and note exactly what Scripture states.\n\nWhat God wants us to know:\nGod wants his people to know that he initiates relationship by promise and command, and expects trust and obedience in response.\n\nWhy:\nPentateuch chapters typically record what God said and did toward Israel or the patriarchs—not human achievement alone. Look for direct speech from God and the response it calls for in this chapter.\n\nSimilar elsewhere:\nGenesis 14: Compare with Genesis 14, which immediately precedes this chapter in the same book — notice what events or themes continue or change.\nDeuteronomy 30:15–20: Like other Pentateuch chapters, this text forms part of Moses'' covenant instruction. Deuteronomy 30 places life and death, blessing and curse, before Israel and calls them to choose obedience to God''s command.","commentary_af":"Vandag se tematiese leeswerk: Abraham se Geloof. Bestudeer elke hoofstuk-afdeling hieronder terwyl jy lees.\n\nGenesis 15\nGod sluit verbond met Abram; sterre beloof ontelbare nageslag; geloof as geregtigheid gereken. Lees Genesis 15 self en kontroleer elke stelling teen die verse in jou Bybelweergawe.\n\nSleutelgebeure in God se verbondverhaal\nDie teks van Genesis 15 noem of illustreer: Sleutelgebeure in God se verbondverhaal. Lees daardie verse weer en skryf presies op wat die Bybel sê — nie wat jy dink nie.\n\nLet hoe beloftes menslike mislukking oorleef\nDie teks van Genesis 15 noem of illustreer: Let hoe beloftes menslike mislukking oorleef. Lees daardie verse weer en skryf presies op wat die Bybel sê — nie wat jy dink nie.\n\nLet op aanbidding, gehoorsaamheid en genade\nDie teks van Genesis 15 noem of illustreer: Let op aanbidding, gehoorsaamheid en genade. Lees daardie verse weer en skryf presies op wat die Bybel sê — nie wat jy dink nie.\n\nWhat God wants us to know:\nGod wil sy volk laat weet dat Hy verhouding begin met belofte en gebod, en vertroue en gehoorsaamheid verwag.\n\nWhy:\nPentateug-hoofstukke beskryf gewoonlik wat God gesê en gedoen het—kyk vir God se directe spraak en die reaksie wat hierdie hoofstuk van sy volk vra.\n\nSimilar elsewhere:\nGenesis 14: Compare with Genesis 14, wat direct voor hierdie hoofstuk kom — let op wat voortgaan of verander.\nDeuteronomium 30:15–20: Soos ander Pentateug-hoofstukke vorm hierdie teks deel van Moses se verbondsinstruksie. Deut 30 stel lewe en dood, seën en vloek, voor Israel.","questions_en":["What does this passage reveal about God?","What promise, command, or truth stands out to you?","How can you apply this to your life today?"],"questions_af":["Wat openbaar hierdie gedeelte oor God?","Watter belofte, gebod of waarheid val vir jou op?","Hoe kan jy dit vandag in jou lewe toepas?"]},{"day":2,"title_en":"Trust in the Lord","title_af":"Vertrou op die Here","passages":[{"book_id":19,"chapter":27}],"commentary_intro_en":"Today''s themed reading: Trust in the Lord. Study each chapter section below as you read.","commentary_intro_af":"Vandag se tematiese leeswerk: Vertrou op die Here. Bestudeer elke hoofstuk-afdeling hieronder terwyl jy lees.","commentary_sections":[{"book_id":19,"chapter":27,"heading_en":"Psalms 27","heading_af":"Psalms 27","summary_en":"Psalm 27 expresses worship, lament, or wisdom before God. Read it as prayer — many psalms foreshadow Christ and speak to every season of the soul. Read Psalms 27 yourself and verify each statement against the verses in your Bible version.","summary_af":"Psalm 27 druk aanbidding, klagte of wysheid voor God uit. Lees dit as gebed — baie psalms wys na Christus en spreek tot elke seisoen van die siel. Lees Psalms 27 self en kontroleer elke stelling teen die verse in jou Bybelweergawe.","study_points_en":[{"title":"Pray the psalm back to God","verses":"","detail":"The text of Psalms 27 records or illustrates: Pray the psalm back to God. Re-read those verses and note exactly what Scripture states."},{"title":"Notice metaphors for God","verses":"","detail":"The text of Psalms 27 records or illustrates: Notice metaphors for God. Re-read those verses and note exactly what Scripture states."},{"title":"Apply its emotion honestly","verses":"","detail":"The text of Psalms 27 records or illustrates: Apply its emotion honestly. Re-read those verses and note exactly what Scripture states."}],"study_points_af":[{"title":"Bid die psalm terug aan God","verses":"","detail":"Die teks van Psalms 27 noem of illustreer: Bid die psalm terug aan God. Lees daardie verse weer en skryf presies op wat die Bybel sê — nie wat jy dink nie."},{"title":"Let op metafore vir God","verses":"","detail":"Die teks van Psalms 27 noem of illustreer: Let op metafore vir God. Lees daardie verse weer en skryf presies op wat die Bybel sê — nie wat jy dink nie."},{"title":"Pas die emosie eerlik toe","verses":"","detail":"Die teks van Psalms 27 noem of illustreer: Pas die emosie eerlik toe. Lees daardie verse weer en skryf presies op wat die Bybel sê — nie wat jy dink nie."}],"teaching_en":"God wants us to know that true wisdom begins with reverence for him and shapes daily choices, speech, and worship.","teaching_why_en":"Wisdom passages tie understanding to the fear of the Lord and practical living. Notice commands, prayers, or counsel in this chapter and what attitude toward God they assume.","teaching_af":"God wil hê ons moet weet dat ware wysheid begin met eerbied vir Hom en daaglikse keuses, spraak en aanbidding vorm.","teaching_why_af":"Wysheid verbind insig met die vrees vir die Here. Let op gebooie, gebede of raad in hierdie hoofstuk en watter houding teenoor God dit veronderstel.","cross_references_en":[{"ref":"Psalms 26","comparison":"Compare with Psalms 26, which immediately precedes this chapter in the same book — notice what events or themes continue or change."},{"ref":"Proverbs 1:7","comparison":"Wisdom books often repeat the theme that the fear of the Lord is the beginning of wisdom (Proverbs 1:7). Compare how each psalm or proverb applies that foundation differently."}],"cross_references_af":[{"ref":"Psalms 26","comparison":"Compare with Psalms 26, wat direct voor hierdie hoofstuk kom — let op wat voortgaan of verander."},{"ref":"Spreuke 1:7","comparison":"Wysheidsboeke herhaal dat die vrees vir die Here die begin van wysheid is (Spr 1:7). Vergelyk hoe elke psalm of spreuk dit toepas."}],"highlights_en":["Pray the psalm back to God","Notice metaphors for God","Apply its emotion honestly"],"highlights_af":["Bid die psalm terug aan God","Let op metafore vir God","Pas die emosie eerlik toe"]}],"commentary_en":"Today''s themed reading: Trust in the Lord. Study each chapter section below as you read.\n\nPsalms 27\nPsalm 27 expresses worship, lament, or wisdom before God. Read it as prayer — many psalms foreshadow Christ and speak to every season of the soul. Read Psalms 27 yourself and verify each statement against the verses in your Bible version.\n\nPray the psalm back to God\nThe text of Psalms 27 records or illustrates: Pray the psalm back to God. Re-read those verses and note exactly what Scripture states.\n\nNotice metaphors for God\nThe text of Psalms 27 records or illustrates: Notice metaphors for God. Re-read those verses and note exactly what Scripture states.\n\nApply its emotion honestly\nThe text of Psalms 27 records or illustrates: Apply its emotion honestly. Re-read those verses and note exactly what Scripture states.\n\nWhat God wants us to know:\nGod wants us to know that true wisdom begins with reverence for him and shapes daily choices, speech, and worship.\n\nWhy:\nWisdom passages tie understanding to the fear of the Lord and practical living. Notice commands, prayers, or counsel in this chapter and what attitude toward God they assume.\n\nSimilar elsewhere:\nPsalms 26: Compare with Psalms 26, which immediately precedes this chapter in the same book — notice what events or themes continue or change.\nProverbs 1:7: Wisdom books often repeat the theme that the fear of the Lord is the beginning of wisdom (Proverbs 1:7). Compare how each psalm or proverb applies that foundation differently.","commentary_af":"Vandag se tematiese leeswerk: Vertrou op die Here. Bestudeer elke hoofstuk-afdeling hieronder terwyl jy lees.\n\nPsalms 27\nPsalm 27 druk aanbidding, klagte of wysheid voor God uit. Lees dit as gebed — baie psalms wys na Christus en spreek tot elke seisoen van die siel. Lees Psalms 27 self en kontroleer elke stelling teen die verse in jou Bybelweergawe.\n\nBid die psalm terug aan God\nDie teks van Psalms 27 noem of illustreer: Bid die psalm terug aan God. Lees daardie verse weer en skryf presies op wat die Bybel sê — nie wat jy dink nie.\n\nLet op metafore vir God\nDie teks van Psalms 27 noem of illustreer: Let op metafore vir God. Lees daardie verse weer en skryf presies op wat die Bybel sê — nie wat jy dink nie.\n\nPas die emosie eerlik toe\nDie teks van Psalms 27 noem of illustreer: Pas die emosie eerlik toe. Lees daardie verse weer en skryf presies op wat die Bybel sê — nie wat jy dink nie.\n\nWhat God wants us to know:\nGod wil hê ons moet weet dat ware wysheid begin met eerbied vir Hom en daaglikse keuses, spraak en aanbidding vorm.\n\nWhy:\nWysheid verbind insig met die vrees vir die Here. Let op gebooie, gebede of raad in hierdie hoofstuk en watter houding teenoor God dit veronderstel.\n\nSimilar elsewhere:\nPsalms 26: Compare with Psalms 26, wat direct voor hierdie hoofstuk kom — let op wat voortgaan of verander.\nSpreuke 1:7: Wysheidsboeke herhaal dat die vrees vir die Here die begin van wysheid is (Spr 1:7). Vergelyk hoe elke psalm of spreuk dit toepas.","questions_en":["What does this passage reveal about God?","What promise, command, or truth stands out to you?","How can you apply this to your life today?"],"questions_af":["Wat openbaar hierdie gedeelte oor God?","Watter belofte, gebod of waarheid val vir jou op?","Hoe kan jy dit vandag in jou lewe toepas?"]},{"day":3,"title_en":"God Is Our Refuge","title_af":"God Is Ons Toevlug","passages":[{"book_id":19,"chapter":46}],"commentary_intro_en":"Today''s themed reading: God Is Our Refuge. Study each chapter section below as you read.","commentary_intro_af":"Vandag se tematiese leeswerk: God Is Ons Toevlug. Bestudeer elke hoofstuk-afdeling hieronder terwyl jy lees.","commentary_sections":[{"book_id":19,"chapter":46,"heading_en":"Psalms 46","heading_af":"Psalms 46","summary_en":"Psalm 46 expresses worship, lament, or wisdom before God. Read it as prayer — many psalms foreshadow Christ and speak to every season of the soul. Read Psalms 46 yourself and verify each statement against the verses in your Bible version.","summary_af":"Psalm 46 druk aanbidding, klagte of wysheid voor God uit. Lees dit as gebed — baie psalms wys na Christus en spreek tot elke seisoen van die siel. Lees Psalms 46 self en kontroleer elke stelling teen die verse in jou Bybelweergawe.","study_points_en":[{"title":"Pray the psalm back to God","verses":"","detail":"The text of Psalms 46 records or illustrates: Pray the psalm back to God. Re-read those verses and note exactly what Scripture states."},{"title":"Notice metaphors for God","verses":"","detail":"Th