it toepas."}],"highlights_en":["Pray the psalm back to God","Notice metaphors for God","Apply its emotion honestly"],"highlights_af":["Bid die psalm terug aan God","Let op metafore vir God","Pas die emosie eerlik toe"]}],"commentary_en":"Today''s themed reading: Wait for the Lord. Study each chapter section below as you read.\n\nPsalms 37\nPsalm 37 expresses worship, lament, or wisdom before God. Read it as prayer — many psalms foreshadow Christ and speak to every season of the soul. Read Psalms 37 yourself and verify each statement against the verses in your Bible version.\n\nPray the psalm back to God\nThe text of Psalms 37 records or illustrates: Pray the psalm back to God. Re-read those verses and note exactly what Scripture states.\n\nNotice metaphors for God\nThe text of Psalms 37 records or illustrates: Notice metaphors for God. Re-read those verses and note exactly what Scripture states.\n\nApply its emotion honestly\nThe text of Psalms 37 records or illustrates: Apply its emotion honestly. Re-read those verses and note exactly what Scripture states.\n\nWhat God wants us to know:\nGod wants us to know that true wisdom begins with reverence for him and shapes daily choices, speech, and worship.\n\nWhy:\nWisdom passages tie understanding to the fear of the Lord and practical living. Notice commands, prayers, or counsel in this chapter and what attitude toward God they assume.\n\nSimilar elsewhere:\nPsalms 36: Compare with Psalms 36, which immediately precedes this chapter in the same book — notice what events or themes continue or change.\nProverbs 1:7: Wisdom books often repeat the theme that the fear of the Lord is the beginning of wisdom (Proverbs 1:7). Compare how each psalm or proverb applies that foundation differently.","commentary_af":"Vandag se tematiese leeswerk: Wag op die Here. Bestudeer elke hoofstuk-afdeling hieronder terwyl jy lees.\n\nPsalms 37\nPsalm 37 druk aanbidding, klagte of wysheid voor God uit. Lees dit as gebed — baie psalms wys na Christus en spreek tot elke seisoen van die siel. Lees Psalms 37 self en kontroleer elke stelling teen die verse in jou Bybelweergawe.\n\nBid die psalm terug aan God\nDie teks van Psalms 37 noem of illustreer: Bid die psalm terug aan God. Lees daardie verse weer en skryf presies op wat die Bybel sê — nie wat jy dink nie.\n\nLet op metafore vir God\nDie teks van Psalms 37 noem of illustreer: Let op metafore vir God. Lees daardie verse weer en skryf presies op wat die Bybel sê — nie wat jy dink nie.\n\nPas die emosie eerlik toe\nDie teks van Psalms 37 noem of illustreer: Pas die emosie eerlik toe. Lees daardie verse weer en skryf presies op wat die Bybel sê — nie wat jy dink nie.\n\nWhat God wants us to know:\nGod wil hê ons moet weet dat ware wysheid begin met eerbied vir Hom en daaglikse keuses, spraak en aanbidding vorm.\n\nWhy:\nWysheid verbind insig met die vrees vir die Here. Let op gebooie, gebede of raad in hierdie hoofstuk en watter houding teenoor God dit veronderstel.\n\nSimilar elsewhere:\nPsalms 36: Compare with Psalms 36, wat direct voor hierdie hoofstuk kom — let op wat voortgaan of verander.\nSpreuke 1:7: Wysheidsboeke herhaal dat die vrees vir die Here die begin van wysheid is (Spr 1:7). Vergelyk hoe elke psalm of spreuk dit toepas.","questions_en":["What does this passage reveal about God?","What promise, command, or truth stands out to you?","How can you apply this to your life today?"],"questions_af":["Wat openbaar hierdie gedeelte oor God?","Watter belofte, gebod of waarheid val vir jou op?","Hoe kan jy dit vandag in jou lewe toepas?"]},{"day":13,"title_en":"The Suffering Servant","title_af":"Die Lydinge Kneg","passages":[{"book_id":23,"chapter":53}],"commentary_intro_en":"Today''s themed reading: The Suffering Servant. Study each chapter section below as you read.","commentary_intro_af":"Vandag se tematiese leeswerk: Die Lydinge Kneg. Bestudeer elke hoofstuk-afdeling hieronder terwyl jy lees.","commentary_sections":[{"book_id":23,"chapter":53,"headi