dat Hy verhouding begin met belofte en gebod, en vertroue en gehoorsaamheid verwag.","teaching_why_af":"Pentateug-hoofstukke beskryf gewoonlik wat God gesê en gedoen het—kyk vir God se directe spraak en die reaksie wat hierdie hoofstuk van sy volk vra.","cross_references_en":[{"ref":"Acts 7:2–4","comparison":"Genesis 12 records God calling Abram to leave his country. Stephen in Acts 7:2–4 recounts the God of glory appearing to Abraham in Mesopotamia and telling him to leave — the same call narrative."},{"ref":"Galatians 3:8","comparison":"Genesis 12:3 records God promising to bless all families of the earth through Abram. Galatians 3:8 cites Scripture foreseeing that God would justify the nations by faith — quoting that promise theme."}],"cross_references_af":[{"ref":"Hand 7:2–4","comparison":"Genesis 12 beskryf God wat Abram roep om sy land te verlaat. Stefanus in Hand 7:2–4 herhaal dat die God van heerlikheid aan Abraham verskyn het en hom gesê het om te trek."},{"ref":"Galasiërs 3:8","comparison":"Genesis 12:3 beskryf God se belofte om alle geslagte van die aarde deur Abram te seën. Gal 3:8 verwys na Skrif wat voorsien dat God die nasies deur geloof regverdig."}],"highlights_en":["Key events in God''s covenant story","Watch how promises survive human failure","Note worship, obedience, and grace"],"highlights_af":["Sleutelgebeure in God se verbondverhaal","Let hoe beloftes menslike mislukking oorleef","Let op aanbidding, gehoorsaamheid en genade"]}],"commentary_en":"Family devotion reading. Read each summary together, then discuss what you learn about God.\n\nGenesis 12\nAbram and Lot separate; Abram rescues Lot; Melchizedek blesses; God''s covenant confirmed. Read Genesis 12 yourself and verify each statement against the verses in your Bible version.\n\nKey events in God''s covenant story\nThe text of Genesis 12 records or illustrates: Key events in God''s covenant story. Re-read those verses and note exactly what Scripture states.\n\nWatch how promises survive human failure\nThe text of Genesis 12 records or illustrates: Watch how promises survive human failure. Re-read those verses and note exactly what Scripture states.\n\nNote worship, obedience, and grace\nThe text of Genesis 12 records or illustrates: Note worship, obedience, and grace. Re-read those verses and note exactly what Scripture states.\n\nWhat God wants us to know:\nGod wants his people to know that he initiates relationship by promise and command, and expects trust and obedience in response.\n\nWhy:\nPentateuch chapters typically record what God said and did toward Israel or the patriarchs—not human achievement alone. Look for direct speech from God and the response it calls for in this chapter.\n\nSimilar elsewhere:\nActs 7:2–4: Genesis 12 records God calling Abram to leave his country. Stephen in Acts 7:2–4 recounts the God of glory appearing to Abraham in Mesopotamia and telling him to leave — the same call narrative.\nGalatians 3:8: Genesis 12:3 records God promising to bless all families of the earth through Abram. Galatians 3:8 cites Scripture foreseeing that God would justify the nations by faith — quoting that promise theme.","commentary_af":"Gesins toewyding leeswerk. Lees elke opsomming saam, bespreek dan wat julle oor God leer.\n\nGenesis 12\nAbram en Lot skei; Abram red Lot; Melchisedek seën; God se verbond bevestig. Lees Genesis 12 self en kontroleer elke stelling teen die verse in jou Bybelweergawe.\n\nSleutelgebeure in God se verbondverhaal\nDie teks van Genesis 12 noem of illustreer: Sleutelgebeure in God se verbondverhaal. Lees daardie verse weer en skryf presies op wat die Bybel sê — nie wat jy dink nie.\n\nLet hoe beloftes menslike mislukking oorleef\nDie teks van Genesis 12 noem of illustreer: Let hoe beloftes menslike mislukking oorleef. Lees daardie verse weer en skryf presies op wat die Bybel sê — nie wat jy dink nie.\n\nLet op aanbidding, gehoorsaamheid en genade\nDie teks van Genesis 12 noem of illustreer: Let op aanbidding, gehoorsaamheid en genade. Lees daardie verse weer en skryf presies op wat die Bybel sê — nie wat jy dink nie.\n\nWhat God wants us to know:\nGod wil sy volk laat weet dat Hy verhouding begin met belofte en gebod, en vertroue en gehoorsaamheid verwag.\n\nWhy:\nPentateug-hoofstukke beskryf gewoonlik wat God gesê en gedoen het—kyk vir God se directe spraak en die reaksie wat hierdie hoofstuk van sy volk vra.\n\nSimilar elsewhere:\nHand 7:2–4: Genesis 12 beskryf God wat Abram roep om sy land te verlaat. Stefanus in Hand 7:2–4 herhaal dat die God van heerlikheid aan Abraham verskyn het en hom gesê het om te trek.\nGalasiërs 3:8: Genesis 12:3 beskryf God se belofte om alle geslagte van die aarde deur Abram te seën. Gal 3:8 verwys na Skrif wat voorsien dat God die nasies deur geloof regverdig.","questions_en":["What does this passage reveal about God?","What promise, command, or truth stands out to you?","How can you apply this to your life today?"],"questions_af":["Wat openbaar hierdie gedeelte oor God?","Watter belofte, gebod of waarheid val vir jou op?","Hoe kan jy dit vandag in jou lewe toepas?"]},{"day":6,"title_en":"Isaac Is Born","title_af":"Isak Word Gebore","passages":[{"book_id":1,"chapter":21}],"commentary_intro_en":"Family devotion reading. Read each summary together, then discuss what you learn about God.","commentary_intro_af":"Gesins toewyding leeswerk. Lees elke opsomming saam, bespreek dan wat julle oor God leer.","commentary_sections":[{"book_id":1,"chapter":21,"heading_en":"Genesis 21","heading_af":"Genesis 21","summary_en":"Isaac born; Hagar and Ishmael sent away; treaty at Beersheba. Read Genesis 21 yourself and verify each statement against the verses in your Bible version.","summary_af":"Isak gebore; Hagar en Ismael weggestuur; verdrag by Bersheba. Lees Genesis 21 self en kontroleer elke stelling teen die verse in jou Bybelweergawe.","study_points_en":[{"title":"Key events in God''s covenant story","verses":"","detail":"The text of Genesis 21 records or il