s daardie verse weer en skryf presies op wat die Bybel sê — nie wat jy dink nie.\n\nOproepe om te volg\nDie teks van Lukas 24 noem of illustreer: Oproepe om te volg. Lees daardie verse weer en skryf presies op wat die Bybel sê — nie wat jy dink nie.\n\nWhat God wants us to know:\nGod wil hê ons moet weet wie Jesus is en wat Hy mense roep om te glo en te doen deur sy woorde, dade en gesag.\n\nWhy:\nEvangelie-hoofstukke beskryf wat Jesus geleer, genees, beveel of openbaar het. Fokus op wat die hoofstuk sê Jesus gedoen en gesê het.\n\nSimilar elsewhere:\nBook 42 23: Compare with Book 42 23, wat direct voor hierdie hoofstuk kom — let op wat voortgaan of verander.\nParallelle Evangelies: Baie gebeure in Matteus, Markus, Lukas en Johannes verskyn in meer as een Evangelie. Vergelyk dieselfde episode oor Evangelies heen.","questions_en":["What does this passage reveal about God?","What promise, command, or truth stands out to you?","How can you apply this to your life today?"],"questions_af":["Wat openbaar hierdie gedeelte oor God?","Watter belofte, gebod of waarheid val vir jou op?","Hoe kan jy dit vandag in jou lewe toepas?"]},{"day":27,"title_en":"The Lord Is My Shepherd","title_af":"Die Here Is My Herder","passages":[{"book_id":19,"chapter":23}],"commentary_intro_en":"Family devotion reading. Read each summary together, then discuss what you learn about God.","commentary_intro_af":"Gesins toewyding leeswerk. Lees elke opsomming saam, bespreek dan wat julle oor God leer.","commentary_sections":[{"book_id":19,"chapter":23,"heading_en":"Psalms 23","heading_af":"Psalms 23","summary_en":"The Lord is my shepherd — provision, guidance, protection, and dwelling in God''s house forever. Read Psalms 23 yourself and verify each statement against the verses in your Bible version.","summary_af":"Die Here is my Herder — voorsiening, leiding, beskerming en woning in God se huis vir altyd. Lees Psalms 23 self en kontroleer elke stelling teen die verse in jou Bybelweergawe.","study_points_en":[{"title":"The Lord shepherds me","verses":"","detail":"The text of Psalms 23 records or illustrates: The Lord shepherds me. Re-read those verses and note exactly what Scripture states."},{"title":"Valley of shadow — fear no evil","verses":"","detail":"The text of Psalms 23 records or illustrates: Valley of shadow — fear no evil. Re-read those verses and note exactly what Scripture states."},{"title":"Goodness and mercy follow","verses":"","detail":"The text of Psalms 23 records or illustrates: Goodness and mercy follow. Re-read those verses and note exactly what Scripture states."}],"study_points_af":[{"title":"Die Here weid my","verses":"","detail":"Die teks van Psalms 23 noem of illustreer: Die Here weid my. Lees daardie verse weer en skryf presies op wat die Bybel sê — nie wat jy dink nie."},{"title":"Skaduwee-vallei — geen vrees","verses":"","detail":"Die teks van Psalms 23 noem of illustreer: Skaduwee-vallei — geen vrees. Lees daardie verse weer en skryf presies op wat die Bybel sê — nie wat jy dink nie."},{"title":"Goedertierenheid en barmhartigheid volg","verses":"","detail":"Die teks van Psalms 23 noem of illustreer: Goedertierenheid en barmhartigheid volg. Lees daardie verse weer en skryf presies op wat die Bybel sê — nie wat jy dink nie."}],"teaching_en":"God wants us to know that true wisdom begins with reverence for him and shapes daily choices, speech, and worship.","teaching_why_en":"Wisdom passages tie understanding to the fear of the Lord and practical living. Notice commands, prayers, or counsel in this chapter and what attitude toward God they assume.","teaching_af":"God wil hê ons moet weet dat ware wysheid begin met eerbied vir Hom en daaglikse keuses, spraak en aanbidding vorm.","teaching_why_af":"Wysheid verbind insig met die vrees vir die Here. Let op gebooie, gebede of raad in hierdie hoofstuk en watter houding teenoor God dit veronderstel.","cross_references_en":[{"ref":"John 10:11","comparison":"Psalm 23:1 says \"The Lord is my shepherd.\" John 10:11 records Jesus saying \"I am the good shepherd.\" Both use shepherd language — one in a psalm, one in Jesus'' speech."},{"ref":"Revelation 7:17","comparison":"Psalm 23 speaks of the Lord shepherding and dwelling with the psalmist. Revelation 7:17 says the Lamb will shepherd and lead to living waters — similar shepherd-and-guidance imagery."}],"cross_references_af":[{"ref":"Johannes 10:11","comparison":"Psalm 23:1 sê \"Die Here is my Herder.\" Johannes 10:11 beskryf Jesus wat sê \"Ek is die goeie Herder.\" Beide gebruik herder-taal."},{"ref":"Openbaring 7:17","comparison":"Psalm 23 praat van die Here as Herder. Openbaring 7:17 sê die Lam sal weid en lei na lewende waters — soortgelyke herder-beeld."}],"highlights_en":["The Lord shepherds me","Valley of shadow — fear no evil","Goodness and mercy follow"],"highlights_af":["Die Here weid my","Skaduwee-vallei — geen vrees","Goedertierenheid en barmhartigheid volg"]}],"commentary_en":"Family devotion reading. Read each summary together, then discuss what you learn about God.\n\nPsalms 23\nThe Lord is my shepherd — provision, guidance, protection, and dwelling in God''s house forever. Read Psalms 23 yourself and verify each statement against the verses in your Bible version.\n\nThe Lord shepherds me\nThe text of Psalms 23 records or illustrates: The Lord shepherds me. Re-read those verses and note exactly what Scripture states.\n\nValley of shadow — fear no evil\nThe text of Psalms 23 records or illustrates: Valley of shadow — fear no evil. Re-read those verses and note exactly what Scripture states.\n\nGoodness and mercy follow\nThe text of Psalms 23 records or illustrates: Goodness and mercy follow. Re-read those verses and note exactly what Scripture states.\n\nWhat God wants us to know:\nGod wants us to know that true wisdom begins with reverence for him and shapes daily choices, speech, and worship.\n\nWhy:\nWisdom passages tie understanding to the fear of the Lord and practical living. Notice commands, prayers, or counsel in this chapter and what attitude toward God they assume.\n\nSimilar elsewhere:\nJohn 10:11: Psalm 23:1 says \"The Lord is my shepherd.\" John 10:11 records Jesus saying \"I am the good shepherd.\" Both use shepherd language — one in a psalm, one in Jesus'' speech.\nRevelation 7:17: Psalm 23 speaks of the Lord shepherding and dwelling with the psalmist. Revelation 7:17 says the Lamb will shepherd and lead to living waters — similar shepherd-and-guidance imagery.","commentary_af":"Gesins toewyding leeswerk. Lees elke opsomming saam, bespreek dan wat julle oor God leer.\n\nPsalms 23\nDie Here is my Herder — voorsiening, leiding, beskerming en woning in God se huis vir altyd. Lees Psalms 23 self en kontroleer elke stelling teen die verse in jou Bybelweergawe.\n\nDie Here weid my\nDie teks van Psalms 23 noem of illustreer: Die Here weid my. Lees daardie verse weer en skryf presies op wat die Bybel sê — nie wat jy dink nie.\n\nSkaduwee-vallei — geen vrees\nDie teks van Psalms 23 noem of illustreer: Skaduwee-vallei — geen vrees. Lees daardie verse weer en skryf presies op wat die Bybel sê — nie wat jy dink nie.\n\nGoedertierenheid en barmhartigheid volg\nDie teks van Psalms 23 noem of illustreer: Goedertierenheid en barmhartigheid volg. Lees daardie verse weer en skryf presies op wat die Bybel sê — nie wat jy dink nie.\n\nWhat God wants us to know:\nGod wil hê ons moet weet dat ware wysheid begin met eerbied vir Hom en daaglikse keuses, spraak en aanbidding vorm.\n\nWhy:\nWysheid verbind insig met die vrees vir die Here. Let op gebooie, gebede of raad in hierdie hoofstuk en watter houding teenoor God dit veronderstel.\n\nSimilar elsewhere:\nJohannes 10:11: Psalm 23:1 sê \"Die Here is my Herder.\" Johannes 10:11 beskryf Jesus wat sê \"Ek is die goeie Herder.\" Beide gebruik herder-taal.\nOpenbaring 7:17: Psalm 23 praat van die Here as Herder. Openbaring 7:17 sê die Lam sal weid en lei na lewende waters — soortgelyke herder-beeld.","questions_en":["What does this passage reveal about God?","What promise, command, or truth stands out to you?","How can you apply this to your life today?"],"questions_af":["Wat openbaar hierdie gedeelte oor God?","Watter belofte, gebod of waarheid val vir jou op?","Hoe kan jy dit vandag in jou lewe toepas?"]},{"day":28,"title_en":"Love One Another","title_af":"Liefhet Mekaar","passages":[{"book_id":43,"chapter":13}],"commentary_intro_en":"Family devotion reading. Read each summary together, then discuss what you learn about God.","commentary_intro_af":"Gesins toewyding leeswerk. Lees elke opsomming saam, bespreek dan wat julle oor God leer.","commentary_sections":[{"book_id":43,"chapter":13,"heading_en":"John 13","heading_af":"Johannes 13","summary_en":"John 13. The Gospels reveal Jesus — His teaching, authority, compassion, and mission. Ask: Who is Jesus here, and what is He calling me to believe and do? Read John 13 yourself and verify each statement against the verses in your Bible version.","summary_af":"Johannes 13. Die Evangelies openbaar Jesus — Sy lering, gesag, barmhartigheid en sending. Vra: Wie is Jesus hier, en wat roep Hy my om te glo en te doen? Lees Johannes 13 self en kontroleer elke stelling teen die verse in jou Bybelweergawe.","study_points_en":[{"title":"Jesus'' identity and authority","verses":"","detail":"The text of John 13 records or illustrates: Jesus'' identity and authority. Re-read those verses and note exactly what Scripture states."},{"title":"Kingdom teaching","verses":"","detail":"The text of John 13 records or illustrates: Kingdom teaching. Re-read those verses and note exactly what Scripture states."},{"title":"Calls to follow","verses":"","detail":"The text of John 13 records or illustrates: Calls to follow. Re-read those verses and note exactly what Scripture states."}],"study_points_af":[{"title":"Jesus se identiteit en gesag","verses":"","detail":"Die teks van Johannes 13 noem of illustreer: Jesus se identiteit en gesag. Lees daardie verse weer en skryf presies op wat die Bybel sê — nie wat jy dink nie."},{"title":"Koninkryk-lering","verses":"","detail":"Die teks van Johannes 13 noem of illustreer: Koninkryk-lering. Lees daardie verse weer en skryf presies op wat die Bybel sê — nie wat jy dink nie."},{"title":"Oproepe om te volg","verses":"","detail":"Die teks van Johannes 13 noem of illustreer: Oproepe om te volg. Lees daardie verse weer en skryf presies op wat die Bybel sê — nie wat jy dink nie."}],"teaching_en":"God wants us to know who Jesus is and what he calls people to believe and do through his words, actions, and authority.","teaching_why_en":"Gospel chapters record what Jesus taught, healed, commanded, or revealed about the kingdom. Focus on what the chapter says Jesus did and said—not later tradition.","teaching_af":"God wil hê ons moet weet wie Jesus is en wat Hy mense roep om te glo en te doen deur sy woorde, dade en gesag.","teaching_why_af":"Evangelie-hoofstukke beskryf wat Jesus geleer, genees, beveel of openbaar het. Fokus op wat die hoofstuk sê Jesus gedoen en gesê het.","cross_references_en":[{"ref":"John 12","comparison":"Compare with John 12, which immediately precedes this chapter in the same book — notice what events or themes continue or change."},{"ref":"Parallel Gospels","comparison":"Many events in Matthew, Mark, Luke, and John appear in more than one Gospel with matching or overlapping details. Compare the same episode across Gospels to see what each writer records."}],"cross_references_af":[{"ref":"Johannes 12","comparison":"Compare with Johannes 12, wat direct voor hierdie hoofstuk kom — let op wat voortgaan of verander."},{"ref":"Parallelle Evangelies","comparison":"Baie gebeure in Matteus, Markus, Lukas en Johannes verskyn in meer as een Evangelie. Vergelyk dieselfde episode oor Evangelies heen."}],"highlights_en":["Jesus'' identity and authority","Kingdom teaching","Calls to follow"],"highlights_af":["Jesus se identiteit en gesag","Koninkryk-lering","Oproepe om te volg"]}],"commentary_en":"Family devotion reading. Read each summary together, then discuss what you learn about God.\n\nJohn 13\nJohn 13. The Gospels reveal Jesus — His teaching, authority, compassion, and mission. Ask: Who is Jesus here, and what is He calling me to believe and do? Read John 13 yourself and verify each statement against the verses in your Bible version.\n\nJesus'' identity and authority\nThe text of John 13 records or illustrates: Jesus'' identity and authority. Re-read those verses and note exactly what Scripture states.\n\nKingdom teaching\nThe text of John 13 records or illustrates: Kingdom teaching. Re-read those verses and note exactly what Scripture states.\n\nCalls to follow\nThe text of John 13 records or illustrates: Calls to follow. Re-read those verses and note exactly what Scripture states.\n\nWhat God wants us to know:\nGod wants us to know who Jesus is and what he calls people to believe and do through his words, actions, and authority.\n\nWhy:\nGospel chapters record what Jesus taught, healed, commanded, or revealed about the kingdom. Focus on what the chapter says Jesus did and said—not later tradition.\n\nSimilar elsewhere:\nJohn 12: Compare with John 12, which immediately precedes this chapter in the same book — notice what events or themes continue or change.\nParallel Gospels: Many events in Matthew, Mark, Luke, and John appear in more than one Gospel with matching or overlapping details. Compare the same episode across Gospels to see what each writer records.","commentary_af":"Gesins toewyding leeswerk. Lees elke opsomming saam, bespreek dan wat julle oor God leer.\n\nJohannes 13\nJohannes 13. Die Evangelies openbaar Jesus — Sy lering, gesag, barmhartigheid en sending. Vra: Wie is Jesus hier, en wat roep Hy my om te glo en te doen? Lees Johannes 13 self en kontroleer elke stelling teen die verse in jou Bybelweergawe.\n\nJesus se identiteit en gesag\nDie teks van Johannes 13 noem of illustreer: Jesus se identiteit en gesag. Lees daardie verse weer en skryf presies op wat die Bybel sê — nie wat jy dink nie.\n\nKoninkryk-lering\nDie teks van Johannes 13 noem of illustreer: Koninkryk-lering. Lees daardie verse weer en skryf presies op wat die Bybel sê — nie wat jy dink nie.\n\nOproepe om te volg\nDie teks van Johannes 13 noem of illustreer: Oproepe om te volg. Lees daardie verse weer en skryf presies op wat die Bybel sê — nie wat jy dink nie.\n\nWhat God wants us to know:\nGod wil hê ons moet weet wie Jesus is en wat Hy mense roep om te glo en te doen deur sy woorde, dade en gesag.\n\nWhy:\nEvangelie-hoofstukke beskryf wat Jesus geleer, genees, beveel of openbaar het. Fokus op wat die hoofstuk sê Jesus gedoen en gesê het.\n\nSimilar elsewhere:\nJohannes 12: Compare with Johannes 12, wat direct voor hierdie hoofstuk kom — let op wat voortgaan of verander.\nParallelle Evangelies: Baie gebeure in Matteus, Markus, Lukas en Johannes verskyn in meer as een Evangelie. Vergelyk dieselfde episode oor Evangelies heen.","questions_en":["What does this passage reveal about God?","What promise, command, or truth stands out to you?","How can you apply this to your life today?"],"questions_af":["Wat openbaar hierdie gedeelte oor God?","Watter belofte, gebod of waarheid val vir jou op?","Hoe kan jy dit vandag in jou lewe toepas?"]},{"day":29,"title_en":"The Fruit of the Spirit","title_af":"Die Vrug van die Gees","passages":[{"book_id":48,"chapter":5}],"commentary_intro_en":"Family devotion reading. Read each summary together, then discuss what you learn about God.","commentary_intro_af":"Gesins toewyding leeswerk. Lees elke opsomming saam, bespreek dan wat julle oor God leer.","commentary_sections":[{"book_id":48,"chapter":5,"heading_en":"Book 48 5","heading_af":"Boek 48 5","summary_en":"Book 48 5. Paul teaches doctrine and Christian living. Connect theological truth to practical obedience in church, family, and daily relationships. Read Book 48 5 yourself and verify each statement against the verses in your Bible 