) VALUES (
    'women-bible-30',
    'Women of the Bible',
    'Vroue van die Bybel',
    '30 days exploring the stories of key women throughout Scripture.',
    '30 dae om die stories van sleutelvroue regdeur die Skrif te verken.',
    '30 stories of women in Scripture with chapter summaries and reflection questions.',
    '30 stories van vroue in die Skrif met hoofstuk-opsommings en refleksie vrae.',
    30,
    'topic',
    '[{"day":1,"title_en":"Eve — Creation","title_af":"Eva — Skepping","passages":[{"book_id":1,"chapter":2}],"commentary_intro_en":"Today''s themed reading: Eve — Creation. Study each chapter section below as you read.","commentary_intro_af":"Vandag se tematiese leeswerk: Eva — Skepping. Bestudeer elke hoofstuk-afdeling hieronder terwyl jy lees.","commentary_sections":[{"book_id":1,"chapter":2,"heading_en":"Genesis 2","heading_af":"Genesis 2","summary_en":"The heavens and earth are finished (v. 1). On the seventh day God rests and blesses the day (vv. 2–3). The narrative shifts to when God forms the man from the dust of the ground and breathes into his nostrils the breath of life (v. 7). God plants Eden in the east and places the man there (v. 8). Two trees are named: the tree of life and the tree of knowledge of good and evil (v. 9). A river flows from Eden to water the garden and divides into four rivers named Pishon, Gihon, Tigris, and Euphrates (vv. 10–14). God commands the man not to eat from the tree of knowledge of good and evil, warning of death (vv. 16–17). Animals are formed and named by the man; no helper is found (vv. 19–20). God builds the woman from the man''s rib; the man calls her \"woman\" and the text states a man leaves father and mother and holds fast to his wife, becoming one flesh (vv. 21–24). They are naked and not ashamed (v. 25).","summary_af":"Die hemel en aarde is voltooi (v. 1). Op die sewende dag rus God (vv. 2–3). Die Here God vorm die man uit stof en blaas lewensasem in sy neus (v. 7). Hy plant Eden in die ooste (v. 8). Twee bome word genoem: lewensboom en boom van kennis (v. 9). ''n Rivier vloei uit Eden en verdeel in vier riviere (vv. 10–14). God verbied die man om van die kennisboom te eet — sterwe sou volg (vv. 16–17). Diere word gevorm en deur die man genoem (vv. 19–20). God bou die vrou uit die man se rib (vv. 21–24). Hulle is naak en nie beskaam nie (v. 25).","study_points_en":[{"title":"Man formed and given breath","verses":"v. 7","detail":"The Lord God forms the man from dust of the ground and breathes into his nostrils the breath of life; the man becomes a living creature. The chapter records both material (dust) and divine breath."},{"title":"Eden and the two named trees","verses":"vv. 8–9, 16–17","detail":"God plants a garden in Eden and puts the man there. The tree of life and the tree of knowledge of good and evil are named. God permits eating from any tree except the tree of knowledge; eating it brings death (vv. 16–17)."},{"title":"Woman formed; one-flesh union stated","verses":"vv. 21–24","detail":"God builds a woman from the man''s rib. The man says she is bone of his bones and flesh of his flesh (v. 23). Verse 24 states a man shall leave father and mother and hold fast to his wife, and they shall become one flesh."},{"title":"Naked without shame","verses":"v. 25","detail":"The chapter ends stating the man and his wife were both naked and were not ashamed — the last recorded condition before chapter 3."}],"study_points_af":[{"title":"Man gevorm en lewensasem gegee","verses":"v. 7","detail":"Die Here God vorm die man uit stof van die grond en blaas lewensasem in sy neus; die man word ''n lewende wese."},{"title":"Eden en die twee bome","verses":"vv. 8–9, 16–17","detail":"God plant ''n tuin in Eden. Die lewensboom en kennisboom word genoem. Eet van die kennisboom bring die dood (vv. 16–17)."},{"title":"Vrou gevorm; een-vlees unie","verses":"vv. 21–24","detail":"God bou ''n vrou uit die man se rib. V. 24 sê ''n man sal sy vader en moeder verlaat en sy vrou aankleef, en hulle word een vlees."},{"title":"Naak sonder skaamte","verses":"v. 25","detail":"Die hoofstuk eindig: hulle was beide naak en nie beskaam nie — die laaste toestand voor hoofstuk 3."}],"teaching_en":"God wants us to know that life, marriage, and work are gifts placed within boundaries that protect fellowship with him.","teaching_why_en":"God forms the man, gives breath (v. 7), provides Eden (v. 8), sets one clear limit on the tree of knowledge (vv. 16–17), and institutes marriage (vv. 22–24). The man''s work of naming and keeping the garden (vv. 15, 19–20) happens before the fall.","teaching_af":"God wil hê ons moet weet dat lewe, huwelik en werk geskenke is binne grense wat gemeenskap met Hom beskerm.","teaching_why_af":"God vorm die man, gee asem (v. 7), voorsien Eden (v. 8), stel een duidelike grens aan die kennisboom (vv. 16–17), en stel huwelik in (vv. 22–24). Die man se werk om te noem en te bewaar (vv. 15, 19–20) gebeur voor die val.","cross_references_en":[{"ref":"Genesis 1:26–27","comparison":"Genesis 1 gives the wide creation account; Genesis 2 focuses on the man formed from dust (v. 7), Eden planted (v. 8), and the woman formed (v. 22). Both describe humanity''s origin but at different narrative zoom levels."},{"ref":"Revelation 22:1–2","comparison":"Genesis 2 describes a river watering Eden and the tree of life. Revelation 22 again mentions the river of life and the tree of life — language that echoes Eden without repeating Genesis 2''s exact details."}],"cross_references_af":[{"ref":"Genesis 1:26–27","comparison":"Genesis 1 gee die breë skeppingsverhaal; Genesis 2 fokus op die man uit stof (v. 7), Eden (v. 8) en die vrou (v. 22). Beide beskryf die mens se oorsprong op verskillende narratiewe vlakke."},{"ref":"Openbaring 22:1–2","comparison":"Genesis 2 beskryf ''n rivier wat Eden besproei en die lewensboom. Openbaring 22 noem weer die rivier van lewe en die lewensboom — taal wat Eden herroep."}],"highlights_en":["Man formed and given breath","Eden and the two named trees","Woman formed; one-flesh union stated","Naked without shame"],"highlights_af":["Man gevorm en lewensasem gegee","Eden en die twee bome","Vrou gevorm; een-vlees unie","Naak sonder skaamte"]}],"commentary_en":"Today''s themed reading: Eve — Creation. Study each chapter section below as you read.\n\nGenesis 2\nThe heavens and earth are finished (v. 1). On the seventh day God rests and blesses the day (vv. 2–3). The narrative shifts to when God forms the man from the dust of the ground and breathes into his nostrils the breath of life (v. 7). God plants Eden in the east and places the man there (v. 8). Two trees are named: the tree of life and the tree of knowledge of good and evil (v. 9). A river flows from Eden to water the garden and divides into four rivers named Pishon, Gihon, Tigris, and Euphrates (vv. 10–14). God commands the man not to eat from the tree of knowledge of good and evil, warning of death (vv. 16–17). Animals are formed and named by the man; no helper is found (vv. 19–20). God builds the woman from the man''s rib; the man calls her \"woman\" and the text states a man leaves father and mother and holds fast to his wife, becoming one flesh (vv. 21–24). They are naked and not ashamed (v. 25).\n\nMan formed and given breath [v. 7]\nThe Lord God forms the man from dust of the ground and breathes into his nostrils the breath of life; the man becomes a living creature. The chapter records both material (dust) and divine breath.\n\nEden and the two named trees [vv. 8–9, 16–17]\nGod plants a garden in Eden and puts the man there. The tree of life and the tree of knowledge of good and evil are named. God permits eating from any tree except the tree of knowledge; eating it brings death (vv. 16–17).\n\nWoman formed; one-flesh union stated [vv. 21–24]\nGod builds a woman from the man''s rib. The man says she is bone of his bones and flesh of his flesh (v. 23). Verse 24 states a man shall leave father and mother and hold fast to his wife, and they shall become one flesh.\n\nNaked without shame [v. 25]\nThe chapter ends stating the man and his wife were both naked and were not ashamed — the last recorded condition before chapter 3.\n\nWhat God wants us to know:\nGod wants us to know that life, marriage, and work are gifts placed within boundaries that protect fellowship with him.\n\nWhy:\nGod forms the man, gives breath (v. 7), provides Eden (v. 8), sets one clear limit on the tree of knowledge (vv. 16–17), and institutes marriage (vv. 22–24). The man''s work of naming and keeping the garden (vv. 15, 19–20) happens before the fall.\n\nSimilar elsewhere:\nGenesis 1:26–27: Genesis 1 gives the wide creation account; Genesis 2 focuses on the man formed from dust (v. 7), Eden planted (v. 8), and the woman formed (v. 22). Both describe humanity''s origin but at different narrative zoom levels.\nRevelation 22:1–2: Genesis 2 describes a river watering Eden and the tree of life. Revelation 22 again mentions the river of life and the tree of life — language that echoes Eden without repeating Genesis 2''s exact details.","commentary_af":"Vandag se tematiese leeswerk: Eva — Skepping. Bestudeer elke hoofstuk-afdeling hieronder terwyl jy lees.\n\nGenesis 2\nDie hemel en aarde is voltooi (v. 1). Op die sewende dag rus God (vv. 2–3). Die Here God vorm die man uit stof en blaas lewensasem in sy neus (v. 7). Hy plant Eden in die ooste (v. 8). Twee bome word genoem: lewensboom en boom van kennis (v. 9). ''n Rivier vloei uit Eden en verdeel in vier riviere (vv. 10–14). God verbied die man om van die kennisboom te eet — sterwe sou volg (vv. 16–17). Diere word gevorm en deur die man genoem (vv. 19–20). God bou die vrou uit die man se rib (vv. 21–24). Hulle is naak en nie beskaam nie (v. 25).\n\nMan gevorm en lewensasem gegee [v. 7]\nDie Here God vorm die man uit stof van die grond en blaas lewensasem in sy neus; die man word ''n lewende wese.\n\nEden en die twee bome [vv. 8–9, 16–17]\nGod plant ''n tuin in Eden. Die lewensboom en kennisboom word genoem. Eet van die kennisboom bring die dood (vv. 16–17).\n\nVrou gevorm; een-vlees unie [vv. 21–24]\nGod bou ''n vrou uit die man se rib. V. 24 sê ''n man sal sy vader en moeder verlaat en sy vrou aankleef, en hulle word een vlees.\n\nNaak sonder skaamte [v. 25]\nDie hoofstuk eindig: hulle was beide naak en nie beskaam nie — die laaste toestand voor hoofstuk 3.\n\nWhat God wants us to know:\nGod wil hê ons moet weet dat lewe, huwelik en werk geskenke is binne grense wat gemeenskap met Hom beskerm.\n\nWhy:\nGod vorm die man, gee asem (v. 7), voorsien Eden (v. 8), stel een duidelike grens aan die kennisboom (vv. 16–17), en stel huwelik in (vv. 22–24). Die man se werk om te noem en te bewaar (vv. 15, 19–20) gebeur voor die val.\n\nSimilar elsewhere:\nGenesis 1:26–27: Genesis 1 gee die breë skeppingsverhaal; Genesis 2 fokus op die man uit stof (v. 7), Eden (v. 8) en die vrou (v. 22). Beide beskryf die mens se oorsprong op verskillende narratiewe vlakke.\nOpenbaring 22:1–2: Genesis 2 beskryf ''n rivier wat Eden besproei en die lewensboom. Openbaring 22 noem weer die rivier van lewe en die lewensboom — taal wat Eden herroep.","questions_en":["What does this passage reveal about God?","What promise, command, or truth stands out to you?","How can you apply this to your life today?"],"questions_af":["Wat openbaar hierdie gedeelte oor God?","Watter belofte, gebod of waarheid val vir jou op?","Hoe kan jy dit vandag in jou lewe toepas?"]},{"day":2,"title_en":"Sarah — Promise of Isaac","title_af":"Sara — Belofte van Isak","passages":[{"book_id":1,"chapter":21}],"commentary_intro_en":"Today''s themed reading: Sarah — Promise of Isaac. Study each chapter section below as you read.","commentary_intro_af":"Vandag se tematiese leeswerk: Sara — Belofte van Isak. Bestudeer elke hoofstuk-afdeling hieronder terwyl jy lees.","commentary_sections":[{"book_id":1,"chapter":21,"heading_en":"Genesis 21","heading_af":"Genesis 21","summary_en":"Isaac born; Hagar and Ishmael sent away; treaty at Beersheba. Read Genesis 21 yourself and verify each statement against the verses in your Bible version.","summary_af":"Isak gebore; Hagar en Ismael weggestuur; verdrag by Bersheba. Lees Genesis 21 self en kontroleer elke stelling teen die verse in jou Bybelweergawe.","study_points_en":[{"title":"Key events in God''s covenant story","verses":"","detail":"The text of Genesis 21 records or illustrates: Key events in God''s covenant story. Re-read those verses and note exactly what Scripture states."},{"title":"Watch how promises survive human failure","verses":"","detail":"The text of Genesis 21 records or illustrates: Watch how promises survive human failure. Re-read those verses and note exactly what Scripture states."},{"title":"Note worship, obedience, and grace","verses":"","detail":"The text of Genesis 21 records or illustrates: Note worship, obedience, and grace. Re-read those verses and note exactly what Scripture states."}],"study_points_af":[{"title":"Sleutelgebeure in God se verbondverhaal","verses":"","detail":"Die teks van Genesis 21 noem of illustreer: Sleutelgebeure in God se verbondverhaal. Lees daardie verse weer en skryf presies op wat die Bybel sê — nie wat jy dink nie."},{"title":"Let hoe beloftes menslike mislukking oorleef","verses":"","detail":"Die teks van Genesis 21 noem of illustreer: Let hoe beloftes menslike mislukking oorleef. Lees daardie verse weer en skryf presies op wat die Bybel sê — nie wat jy dink nie."},{"title":"Let op aanbidding, gehoorsaamheid en genade","verses":"","detail":"Die teks van Genesis 21 noem of illustreer: Let op aanbidding, gehoorsaamheid en genade. Lees daardie verse weer en skryf presies op wat die Bybel sê — nie wat jy dink nie."}],"teaching_en":"God wants his people to know that he initiates relationship by promise and command, and expects trust and obedience in response.","teaching_why_en":"Pentateuch chapters typically record what God said and did toward Israel or the patriarchs—not human achievement alone. Look for direct speech from God and the response it calls for in this chapter.","teaching_af":"God wil sy volk laat weet dat Hy verhouding begin met belofte en gebod, en vertroue en gehoorsaamheid verwag.","teaching_why_af":"Pentateug-hoofstukke beskryf gewoonlik wat God gesê en gedoen het—kyk vir God se directe spraak en die reaksie wat hierdie hoofstuk van sy volk vra.","cross_references_en":[{"ref":"Genesis 20","comparison":"Compare with Genesis 20, which immediately precedes this chapter in the same book — notice what events or themes continue or change."},{"ref":"Deuteronomy 30:15–20","comparison":"Like other Pentateuch chapters, this text forms part of Moses'' covenant instruction. Deuteronomy 30 places life and death, blessing and curse, before Israel and calls them to choose obedience to God''s command."}],"cross_references_af":[{"ref":"Genesis 20","comparison":"Compare with Genesis 20, wat direct voor hierdie hoofstuk kom — let op wat voortgaan of verander."},{"ref":"Deuteronomium 30:15–20","comparison":"Soos ander Pentateug-hoofstukke vorm hierdie teks deel van Moses se verbondsinstruksie. Deut 30 stel lewe en dood, seën en vloek, voor Israel."}],"highlights_en":["Key events in God''s covenant story","Watch how promises survive human failure","Note worship, obedience, and grace"],"highlights_af":["Sleutelgebeure in God se verbondverhaal","Let hoe beloftes menslike mislukking oorleef","Let op aanbidding, gehoorsaamheid en genade"]}],"commentary_en":"Today''s themed reading: Sarah — Promise of Isaac. Study each chapter section below as you read.\n\nGenesis 21\nIsaac born; Hagar and Ishmael sent away; treaty at Beersheba. Read Genesis 21 yourself and verify each statement against the verses in your Bible version.\n\nKey events in God''s covenant story\nThe text of Genesis 21 records or illustrates: Key events in God''s covenant story. Re-read those verses and note exactly what Scripture states.\n\nWatch how promises survive human failure\nThe text of Genesis 21 records or illustrates: Watch how promises survive human failure. Re-read those verses and note exactly what Scripture states.\n\nNote worship, obedience, and grace\nThe text of Genesis 21 records or illustrates: Note worship, obedience, and grace. Re-read those verses and note exactly what Scripture states.\n\nWhat God wants us to know:\nGod wants his people to know that he initiates relationship by promise and command, and expects trust and obedience in response.\n\nWhy:\nPentateuch chapters typically record what God said and did toward Israel or the patriarchs—not human achievement alone. Look for direct speech from God and the response it calls for in this chapter.\n\nSimilar elsewhere:\nGenesis 20: Compare with Genesis 20, which immediately precedes this chapter in the same book — notice what events or themes continue or change.\nDeuteronomy 30:15–20: Like other Pentateuch chapters, this text forms part of Moses'' covenant instruction. Deuteronomy 30 places life and death, blessing and curse, before Israel and calls them to choose obedience to God''s command.","commentary_af":"Vandag se tematiese leeswerk: Sara — Belofte van Isak. Bestudeer elke hoofstuk-afdeling hieronder terwyl jy lees.\n\nGenesis 21\nIsak gebore; Hagar en Ismael weggestuur; verdrag by Bersheba. Lees Genesis 21 self en kontroleer elke stelling teen die verse in jou Bybelweergawe.\n\nSleutelgebeure in God se verbondverhaal\nDie teks van Genesis 21 noem of illustreer: Sleutelgebeure in God se verbondverhaal. Lees daardie verse weer en skryf presies op wat die Bybel sê — nie wat jy dink nie.\n\nLet hoe beloftes menslike mislukking oorleef\nDie teks van Genesis 21 noem of illustreer: Let hoe beloftes menslike mislukking oorleef. Lees daardie verse weer en skryf presies op wat die Bybel sê — nie wat jy dink nie.\n\nLet op aanbidding, gehoorsaamheid en genade\nDie teks van Genesis 21 noem of illustreer: Let op aanbidding, gehoorsaamheid en genade. Lees daardie verse weer en skryf presies op wat die Bybel sê — nie wat jy dink nie.\n\nWhat God wants us to know:\nGod wil sy volk laat weet dat Hy verhouding begin met belofte en gebod, en vertroue en gehoorsaamheid verwag.\n\nWhy:\nPentateug-hoofstukke beskryf gewoonlik wat God gesê en gedoen het—kyk vir God se directe spraak en die reaksie wat hierdie hoofstuk van sy volk vra.\n\nSimilar elsewhere:\nGenesis 20: Compare with Genesis 20, wat direct voor hierdie hoofstuk kom — let op wat voortgaan of verander.\nDeuteronomium 30:15–20: Soos ander Pentateug-hoofstukke vorm hierdie teks deel van Moses se verbondsinstruksie. Deut 30 stel lewe en dood, seën en vloek, voor Israel.","questions_en":["What does this passage reveal about God?","What promise, command, or truth stands out to you?","How can you apply this to your life today?"],"questions_af":["Wat openbaar hierdie gedeelte oor God?","Watter belofte, gebod of waarheid val vir jou op?","Hoe kan jy dit vandag in jou lewe toepas?"]},{"day":3,"title_en":"Rebekah — Chosen Bride","title_af":"Rebekka — Uitverkore Bruid","passages":[{"book_id":1,"chapter":24}],"commentary_intro_en":"Today''s themed reading: Rebekah — Chosen Bride. Study each chapter section below as you read.","commentary_intro_af":"Vandag se tematiese leeswerk: Rebekka — Uitverkore Bruid. Bestudeer elke hoofstuk-afdeling hieronder terwyl jy lees.","commentary_sections":[{"book_id":1,"chapter":24,"heading_en":"Genesis 24","heading_af":"Genesis 24","summary_en":"Servant sent to find Isaac a wife; Rebekah chosen; faithful prayer answered. Read Genesis 24 yourself and verify each statement against the verses in your Bible version.","summary_af":"Dienskneg gestuur om vrou vir Isak te vind; Rebekka gekies; getroue gebed beantwoord. Lees Genesis 24 self en kontroleer elke stelling teen die verse in jou Bybelweergawe.","study_points_en":[{"title":"Key events in God''s covenant story","verses":"","detail":"The text of Genesis 24 records or illustrates: Key events in God''s covenant story. Re-read those verses and note exactly what Scripture states."},{"title":"Watch how promises survive human failure","verses":"","detail":"The text of Genesis 24 records or illustrates: Watch how promises survive human failure. Re-read those verses and note exactly what Scripture states."},{"title":"Note worship, obedience, and grace","verses":"","detail":"The text of Genesis 24 records or illustrates: Note worship, obe